(open questions Q1-Q10 incl. custody: root custody is nil, non-nil refused `:yin.k/unsupported :custody`, \\\"exclusive/holder path is phase 7\\\"). Read the current Stage D/E code and tests: `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{handoff,holder/*,checkpoint,ledger,authority/*,custody,compose,remote}.cljc` and `test/yin/vm/ucf/{stage_e_scenarios,stage_e_world,stage_e_peer,stage_e_rows_test,stage_e_process_test,checkpoint_fixtures,checkpoint_test,ledger_fixtures,ledger_test,handoff_v2_holder_test}.clj*`, the UCF docs (`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` 7.5-7.11 and the export-recovery object 7.7.4, `docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`), and how `rows.cljc` carries custody/fork rows. Owner rulings that bind: A is the only code identity; the AST is never lost; sharing of cursor cells survives transport; BLAKE3; no backward compatibility (clean breaks, regenerate fixtures, never migrate); the stack/de Bruijn kernels and old compilers die at phase 8 so no new work on them; native-lane matrix accepted (61/350) only for the cross-engine laws.\\n4\\tDeliver, in this order: (1) an inventory of every Stage D/E scenario and test, what transport it uses today (old fork bytes, handoff v2, `export-task`, checkpoint codec, ledger records) and what it needs to run over `lift-task`/`lower-task` rows; (2) the set of old transport paths phase 7 deletes versus keeps until phase 8; (3) the DESIGN questions phase 7 forces (exclusive/holder custody on rows: what rows carry the lease/fence/holder state; the export-recovery object re-based on rows; checkpoint and ledger embedding of a row body root; crash cuts: which cuts are meaningful when the body is a Merkle row set; publication of successors; authority/capability tokens vs sealed refs on rows; `:resume-mode` v2 handling: the owner said do not carry it) with a recommendation and cost for each, flagging which ones the OWNER must decide; (4) a SLICING: slices 7a, 7b, ... each with files to change/create, dependencies, acceptance tests named, hosts, and a day estimate for opus implementation plus review rounds (we have averaged 2-4 codex rounds per slice); (5) risks and what could force a redesign; (6) the order of work and what can run concurrently; (7) an honest estimate of total days. Foreground only; do not edit code or docs. Report starts with a 15-line plain summary for the owner, ends READY or NOT READY (with the blocking questions).\\n5\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814\",\"uuid\":\"80daadeb-a607-4f66-9ec2-55d7713b6b7f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-13T08:31:07.401Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/collab/1792410000000-architect-phase7-plan.prompt.md\",\"content\":\"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 08:00 +07\\n# Task: plan phase 7 (Architect; plan only, no code)\\nYou are claude-fable-5-1, NEW session. Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan` (branch `srvm-phase7-plan`, from origin/master = phases 1-6 merged: 6a-6c, 5a-5c, 4b, BLAKE3, the row carrier with `lift-task`/`lower-task`, the layouts). Edit ONLY your report `collab/1792410000000-architect-phase7-plan.report.md`. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3. Phase 7 per `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` section 10 item 7: \\\"Stage D/E rerun. Handoff, fencing, custody, durability, crash-cut and cross-process acceptance over the new transport, three hosts\\\" and the entry conditions in `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` section 8.4 and section 11 (open questions Q1-Q10 incl. custody: root custody is nil, non-nil refused `:yin.k/unsupported :custody`, \\\"exclusive/holder path is phase 7\\\"). Read the current Stage D/E code and tests: `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{handoff,holder/*,checkpoint,ledger,authority/*,custody,compose,remote}.cljc` and `test/yin/vm/ucf/{stage_e_scenarios,stage_e_world,stage_e_peer,stage_e_rows_test,stage_e_process_test,checkpoint_fixtures,checkpoint_test,ledger_