{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BJL1nd4G3nw2e5xawj71xs","type":"tool_result","content":"1019\t## 10. Migration\n1020\t\n1021\tEight phases, each gated; the old evaluator survives only as an oracle\n1022\tuntil phase 8.\n1023\t\n1024\t1. **Identity.** Amend the A-only identity contracts. **Complete**\n1025\t   (merged to master 2026-10-10, `2daa17fb`). Independent of this VM.\n1026\t2. **Freeze.** This document's §3 (grammar, minting), §4 (windows,\n1027\t   delivery, safepoint table), §6 (stamps), §3.4 (rejection rules) are\n1028\t   reviewed and frozen. Gate: Architect sign-off on the frozen text.\n1029\t3. **Linearizer, validator, static analysis.** `project` per §3.3, the\n1030\t   loader rules of §3.4 (both load paths), **and the §8.1 analysis\n1031\t   (def, use, `L`, `saved`)**, which the phase-4 evaluator needs for\n1032\t   every call save and capture and so cannot wait for phase 5. Gate:\n1033\t   deterministic vectors across JVM/Node/Dart on the corpus (the same\n1034\t   inline goldens and pinned addresses on all three); malformed-input\n1035\t   refusal rows for every rule including item 13, on the direct vector;\n1036\t   both AST projection lanes and the direct vector load through the one\n1037\t   validator to equal images (§3.4, direct-vector form; the\n1038\t   vector→datoms equivalence is retired); `L` agrees with an\n1039\t   independent reference implementation on the corpus. The image\n1040\t   `load-vector` returns is `{:vector :address :bodies [{:start :end\n1041\t   :owner :registers}]}` with `:end` **exclusive**; phase 4 computes\n1042\t   `analysis` once per admitted image as engine-local derived data, and\n1043\t   neither parsed trees nor saved sets enter canonical content.\n1044\t   *(Met 2026-10-10, commit 7a010962 on `srvm-phase3`; Architect\n1045\t   review `collab/1791530000000-architect-srvm-phase3-review.*`.)*\n1046\t4. **Evaluator.** `yin.vm.semantic-register` beside `yin.vm.semantic`.\n1047\t   During coexistence the evaluator links under the interim format\n1048\t   `:yin.semantic-register/code`, contract `\"v4\"`; phase 5 supplies its\n1049\t   production linker format record (the dependency-closure scanners over\n1050\t   the new table), and phase 8 retires it in favour of\n1051\t   `:yin.semantic/code` `\"v4\"`.\n1052\t   Gate: walker parity on the full B0 corpus (values, store, effects,\n1053\t   halting) under the §2.5 correspondence; Rule R rows; effects,\n1054\t   non-tail and tail recursion, pure and effectful tail completion,\n1055\t   continuation invocation (including abortive invoke and ownership\n1056\t   refusal), park/resume, gensym, module `store-of`, FFI\n1057\t   retained-request and response phases.\n1058\t5. **Derivations.** §8.2-8.3 implemented; the lexical-address law\n1059\t   (`addresses(H) = addresses(R) = addresses(resolve(A))`) and\n1060\t   behavioural parity of all three kernels on the corpus; the\n1061\t   execution oracle, validators, goldens and determinism checks of §8.4\n1062\t   green on three hosts, the slow C4 rows actually run; **the\n1063\t   dependency-closure scanners (UCF §7.6.1) reimplemented over the\n1064\t   new table agree with the old ones and with the tree-side oracles on\n1065\t   the B0 corpus, the register corpus and the C4 linked-prelude modules\n1066\t   by name**, under three obligations (derivations design §7.3): (i)\n1067\t   unordered agreement, old = new = the tree scanners and queries, on\n1068\t   free-name sets, the multiset of free-name occurrences as\n1069\t   `[name in-body?]`, the multiset of definitions as `[name conditional?]`,\n1070\t   and the store-key, FFI-op, parked-id and effect-kind sets (positions\n1071\t   excluded since the layouts differ; the tree scanners order by\n1072\t   structural path and are compared unordered); (ii) ordered agreement,\n1073\t   old = new = an independent emission-order tree oracle (main sequence\n1074\t   then bodies FIFO; a definition visits only its value operand), on the\n1075\t   occurrence and definition sequences and on the application-site count\n1076\t   (definition applications excluded, FFI sites included); (iii) join\n1077\t   agreement through `linker/verify`, old = new on the **complete\n1078\t   normalised outcome**: a success with its retained obligations as\n1079\t   `[name in-body?]` in order, or a refusal with its reason and name\n1080\t   (`:use-before-definition` included, exercised by a row that must\n1081\t   refuse on both sides). The old scanners' answers, normalised joins\n1082\t   included, are pinned as goldens before cutover deletes them, since the\n1083\t   C4 track's module declarations are built against those answers; the\n1084\t   C4 gate is read-only and compares declarations against the discharged\n1085\t   external-name set (module-defined keys and `yin/def` removed,\n1086\t   requirement-covered names removed), not raw free names.\n1087\t6. **Continuation format.** §4.2 frames and both state shapes, the\n1088\t   full frame validator, the safepoint harness of §4.1 (bidirectional\n1089\t   lift/lower rows for every kind and both delivery modes, pending\n1090\t   waits, nested and reified captures, module contexts, refusals); the\n1091\t   row carrier amended to body version 3 with one profile,\n1092\t   `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying canonical\n1093\t   vectors by A, `:yin.k/trees` and the task's free environment, never\n1094\t   a native image (continuation design §2, §6). Gate: UCF §7.11's\n1095\t   harness green **for every engine intended to reconstruct canonical\n1096\t   frames** (the semantic kernel, the stack and register kernels through\n1097\t   their layouts, the stack kernel with its tail-completion seam; the\n1098\t   walker is excluded), not the semantic profile alone.\n1099\t7. **Stage D/E rerun.** Handoff, fencing, custody, durability,\n1100\t   crash-cut and cross-process acceptance over the new transport, three\n1101\t   hosts.\n1102\t8. **Cutover.** Delete `yin.vm.semantic` (old), rename\n1103\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register` to `yin.vm.semantic`, remove the old H/R\n1104\t   request paths and the `raise` dependency, remove the `:dim/lift-to`\n1105\t   row from both de Bruijn descriptors without a version bump and\n1106\t   regenerate the descriptor hashes and every pinned H and R\n1107\t   (derivations design §8.1-8.2); delete `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve`,\n1108\t   `yin.vm.debruijn-linearize`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile` and\n1109\t   their tests only after the replacement coverage of §8.4 is green and\n1110\t   the descriptor-hash golden has moved to a surviving namespace; switch\n1111\t   `linker/relowered`, `publish-closure!` and the REPL to the A-derived\n1112\t   lowerings (derivations design §8.3); regenerate the manifests'\n1113\t   derivation records as `A → H`, `A → R` and the format index in its\n1114\t   final shape `{format storage-address}` (derivations design §7.6,\n1115\t   §8.1); run the C4 suite over the newly published images as the\n1116\t   install-child gate (derivations design §6.1.4 (c)); finalize\n1117\t   documentation. No compatibility shim.\n1118\t\n1119\t## 11. Questions resolved by the freeze review\n1120\t\n1121\tAll four were answered by the Architect (phase-2 review, item 10) and\n1122\tthe answers are adopted above:\n1123\t\n1124\t1. **The structural `:return` after a tail call**: kept, defined as\n1125\t   layout syntax rather than \"invariably unreachable\" (§3.3 item 4);\n1126\t   structural branch delimiters after terminal arms are likewise\n1127\t   permitted and validated structurally (§3.4 items 8, 10).\n1128\t2. **Body-local register ids**: kept, with validated body ownership and\n1129\t   scope (§3.4 item 6).\n1130\t3. **A carried live claim**: not carried; the window's keys are the\n1131\t   membership claim and are validated by recomputation (§4.2).\n1132\t4. **Tail effects**: routed directly through `K`; the engine's\n1133\t   two restore paths (`engine/resume-from-run-queue`,\n1134\t   `engine/resume-continuation`) call `restore-fn(base, entry, value)`\n1135\t   and neither requires a current activation, so no trampoline; the closed `tail` state and the semantic restore helper\n1136\t   are specified in §2.4.\n1137\t\n1138\tNothing remains open in this document before freeze. The one item\n1139\tthat belongs to the phase-3 implementation brief rather than to the\n1140\tdesign is the choice of the independent reference implementation that\n1141\t§8.1's `L` is checked against.\n1142\t\n1143\t## 12. What this does not change\n1144\t\n1145\tThe Universal AST; code identity (A, as ruled); the walker; the stream\n1146\tprotocol and every outcome vocabulary; custody and admission; the de\n1147\tBruijn contracts' names and versions (their descriptors lose only the\n1148\t`:dim/lift-to` row at cutover, §6); the six invariants' satisfaction, in\n1149\tthe Architect's reading: no hidden global state (register counters are\n1150\tlowering data; windows, destinations and saved state are explicit), no\n1151\timplicit control flow, no callbacks, no shared mutable state (windows\n1152\tare immutable values), interpretation separate from execution, and no\n1153\tassumed graphs (the def/use graph is constructed from validated tuples,\n1154\tnever from provenance or an unavailable AST)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"17432178-1fe6-4a06-9e2e-03f9502e5639","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:31:31.543Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md","content":"## 10. Migration\n\nEight phases, each gated; the old evaluator survives only as an oracle\nuntil phase 8.\n\n1. **Identity.** Amend the A-only identity contracts. **Complete**\n   (merged to master 2026-10-10, `2daa17fb`). Independent of this VM.\n2. **Freeze.** This document's §3 (grammar, minting), §4 (windows,\n   delivery, safepoint table), §6 (stamps), §3.4 (rejection rules) are\n   reviewed and frozen. Gate: Architect sign-off on the frozen text.\n3. **Linearizer, validator, static analysis.** `project` per §3.3, the\n   loader rules of §3.4 (both load paths), **and the §8.1 analysis\n   (def, use, `L`, `saved`)**, which the phase-4 evaluator needs for\n   every call save and capture and so cannot wait for phase 5. Gate:\n   deterministic vectors across JVM/Node/Dart on the corpus (the same\n   inline goldens and pinned addresses on all three); malformed-input\n   refusal rows for every rule including item 13, on the direct vector;\n   both AST projection lanes and the direct vector load through the one\n   validator to equal images (§3.4, direct-vector form; the\n   vector→datoms equivalence is retired); `L` agrees with an\n   independent reference implementation on the corpus. The image\n   `load-vector` returns is `{:vector :address :bodies [{:start :end\n   :owner :registers}]}` with `:end` **exclusive**; phase 4 computes\n   `analysis` once per admitted image as engine-local derived data, and\n   neither parsed trees nor saved sets enter canonical content.\n   *(Met 2026-10-10, commit 7a010962 on `srvm-phase3`; Architect\n   review `collab/1791530000000-architect-srvm-phase3-review.*`.)*\n4. **Evaluator.** `yin.vm.semantic-register` beside `yin.vm.semantic`.\n   During coexistence the evaluator links under the interim format\n   `:yin.semantic-register/code`, contract `\"v4\"`; phase 5 supplies its\n   production linker format record (the dependency-closure scanners over\n   the new table), and phase 8 retires it in favour of\n   `:yin.semantic/code` `\"v4\"`.\n   Gate: walker parity on the full B0 corpus (values, store, effects,\n   halting) under the §2.5 correspondence; Rule R rows; effects,\n   non-tail and tail recursion, pure and effectful tail completion,\n   continuation invocation (including abortive invoke and ownership\n   refusal), park/resume, gensym, module `store-of`, FFI\n   retained-request and response phases.\n5. **Derivations.** §8.2-8.3 implemented; the lexical-address law\n   (`addresses(H) = addresses(R) = addresses(resolve(A))`) and\n   behavioural parity of all three kernels on the corpus; the\n   execution oracle, validators, goldens and determinism checks of §8.4\n   green on three hosts, the slow C4 rows actually run; **the\n   dependency-closure scanners (UCF §7.6.1) reimplemented over the\n   new table agree with the old ones and with the tree-side oracles on\n   the B0 corpus, the register corpus and the C4 linked-prelude modules\n   by name**, under three obligations (derivations design §7.3): (i)\n   unordered agreement, old = new = the tree scanners and queries, on\n   free-name sets, the multiset of free-name occurrences as\n   `[name in-body?]`, the multiset of definitions as `[name conditional?]`,\n   and the store-key, FFI-op, parked-id and effect-kind sets (positions\n   excluded since the layouts differ; the tree scanners order by\n   structural path and are compared unordered); (ii) ordered agreement,\n   old = new = an independent emission-order tree oracle (main sequence\n   then bodies FIFO; a definition visits only its value operand), on the\n   occurrence and definition sequences and on the application-site count\n   (definition applications excluded, FFI sites included); (iii) join\n   agreement through `linker/verify`, old = new on the **complete\n   normalised outcome**: a success with its retained obligations as\n   `[name in-body?]` in order, or a refusal with its reason and name\n   (`:use-before-definition` included, exercised by a row that must\n   refuse on both sides). The old scanners' answers, normalised joins\n   included, are pinned as goldens before cutover deletes them, since the\n   C4 track's module declarations are built against those answers; the\n   C4 gate is read-only and compares declarations against the discharged\n   external-name set (module-defined keys and `yin/def` removed,\n   requirement-covered names removed), not raw free names.\n6. **Continuation format.** §4.2 frames and both state shapes, the\n   full frame validator, the safepoint harness of §4.1 (bidirectional\n   lift/lower rows for every kind and both delivery modes, pending\n   waits, nested and reified captures, module contexts, refusals); the\n   row carrier amended to body version 3 with one profile,\n   `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying canonical\n   vectors by A, `:yin.k/trees` and the task's free environment, never\n   a native image (continuation design §2, §6). Gate: UCF §7.11's\n   harness green **for every engine intended to reconstruct canonical\n   frames** (the semantic kernel, the stack and register kernels through\n   their layouts, the stack kernel with its tail-completion seam; the\n   walker is excluded), not the semantic profile alone.\n7. **Stage D/E rerun.** Handoff, fencing, custody, durability,\n   crash-cut and cross-process acceptance over the new transport, three\n   hosts.\n8. **Cutover.** Delete `yin.vm.semantic` (old), rename\n   `yin.vm.semantic-register` to `yin.vm.semantic`, remove the old H/R\n   request paths and the `raise` dependency, remove the `:dim/lift-to`\n   row from both de Bruijn descriptors without a version bump and\n   regenerate the descriptor hashes and every pinned H and R\n   (derivations design §8.1-8.2); delete `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve`,\n   `yin.vm.debruijn-linearize`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile` and\n   their tests only after the replacement coverage of §8.4 is green and\n   the descriptor-hash golden has moved to a surviving namespace; switch\n   `linker/relowered`, `publish-closure!` and the REPL to the A-derived\n   lowerings (derivations design §8.3); regenerate the manifests'\n   derivation records as `A → H`, `A → R` and the format index in its\n   final shape `{format storage-address}` (derivations design §7.6,\n   §8.1); run the C4 suite over the newly published images as the\n   install-child gate (derivations design §6.1.4 (c)); finalize\n   documentation. No compatibility shim.\n\n## 11. Questions resolved by the freeze review\n\nAll four were answered by the Architect (phase-2 review, item 10) and\nthe answers are adopted above:\n\n1. **The structural `:return` after a tail call**: kept, defined as\n   layout syntax rather than \"invariably unreachable\" (§3.3 item 4);\n   structural branch delimiters after terminal arms are likewise\n   permitted and validated structurally (§3.4 items 8, 10).\n2. **Body-local register ids**: kept, with validated body ownership and\n   scope (§3.4 item 6).\n3. **A carried live claim**: not carried; the window's keys are the\n   membership claim and are validated by recomputation (§4.2).\n4. **Tail effects**: routed directly through `K`; the engine's\n   two restore paths (`engine/resume-from-run-queue`,\n   `engine/resume-continuation`) call `restore-fn(base, entry, value)`\n   and neither requires a current activation, so no trampoline; the closed `tail` state and the semantic restore helper\n   are specified in §2.4.\n\nNothing remains open in this document before freeze. The one item\nthat belongs to the phase-3 implementation brief rather than to the\ndesign is the choice of the independent reference implementation that\n§8.1's `L` is checked against.\n\n## 12. What this does not change\n\nThe Universal AST; code identity (A, as ruled); the walker; the stream\nprotocol and every outcome vocabulary; custody and admission; the de\nBruijn contracts' names and versions (their descriptors lose only the\n`:dim/lift-to` row at cutover, §6); the six invariants' satisfaction, in\nthe Architect's reading: no hidden global state (register counters are\nlowering data; windows, destinations and saved state are explicit), no\nimplicit control flow, no callbacks, no shared mutable state (windows\nare immutable values), interpretation separate from execution, and no\nassumed graphs (the def/use graph is constructed from validated tuples,\nnever from provenance or an unavailable AST).","numLines":136,"startLine":1019,"totalLines":1155}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BJL1nd4G3nw2e5xawj71xs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
