{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BAbT9kGBqMYiXJny5dZfPs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world\n2\t  \"M-next stage E: the world one life of a crash/partition scenario runs\n3\t   in, driven only through `yin.vm.ucf.compose` (linker-dht 14.2.4,\n4\t   UCF 7.11.1 clause 10 and the composition halves of clauses 3 and 8).\n5\t\n6\t   A scenario is a sequence of lives over one root directory.  Every\n7\t   piece of state a later life may read lives on durable file media\n8\t   under that root -- the authority's ledger (a dao.stream.journal.file\n9\t   backend), every holder's progress and reply journal\n10\t   (`compose/file-journals`), the content store (a dao.jing.file\n11\t   content file, the node's carrier for bodies and code) and the side\n12\t   log of at-least-once external IO -- so a life is a fresh runtime:\n13\t   nothing in memory crosses from one life to the next.  The program\n14\t   and source streams are outside custody; each life rebuilds its own\n15\t   instance of them under their fixed identities from the life's spec,\n16\t   the way a receiver attaches a stream by its carried descriptor.\n17\t\n18\t   A life is plain data (`run-life`'s spec) and so is everything it\n19\t   reports, so the same life runs in this process (the isolated-runtime\n20\t   mode every lane has, Dart's only form) or inside a separate operating\n21\t   system process (`yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer`, the JVM and Node process\n22\t   transport) and its report is compared as data either way.\n23\t\n24\t   Kills.  Every durable medium is wrapped mortal: a named cut (the\n25\t   `cuts` table) fires at one exact boundary -- before or after a given\n26\t   journal frame, before or after a given content-store put, or after a\n27\t   composition tick whose state matches -- and from then on the life is\n28\t   dead.  Inside a peer process the cut prints its event and blocks\n29\t   until the parent destroys the process (SIGKILL); in this process it\n30\t   marks every medium dead (no further durable write happens) and\n31\t   unwinds, and the runner releases the locks the dead runtime held --\n32\t   the only thing an operating system does for a killed process.\"\n33\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n34\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n35\t            [dao.jing.file :as jing-file]\n36\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n37\t            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n38\t            [dao.stream.journal.file :as file-journal]\n39\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n40\t            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n41\t                       [\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]]\n42\t                :clj [[clojure.java.io :as io]])\n43\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n44\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n45\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n46\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.admission :as admission]\n47\t            [yin.vm.ucf.compose :as compose]\n48\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as s]))\n49\t\n50\t\n51\t;; =============================================================================\n52\t;; Plain data\n53\t;; =============================================================================\n54\t\n55\t\n56\t(defn- host-bytes?\n57\t  [x]\n58\t  #?(:clj (bytes? x)\n59\t     :cljs (instance? js/Uint8Array x)\n60\t     :cljd (instance? typed/Uint8List x)))\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t(defn ->data\n64\t  \"`x` as plain data every host prints and reads back the same: maps,\n65\t   vectors, sets, scalars.  Host bytes become their blake3 digest\n66\t   ({::bytes hex}), so two byte strings compare equal exactly when their\n67\t   bytes are; anything else that is not data (a handle, a function, a\n68\t   machine) becomes {::opaque true}.\"\n69\t  [x]\n70\t  (cond\n71\t    (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)\n72\t        (number? x) (uuid? x))\n73\t    x\n74\t\n75\t    (host-bytes? x) {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 x)}\n76\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(->data k) (->data v)])) x)\n77\t    (vector? x) (mapv ->data x)\n78\t    (set? x) (into #{} (map ->data) x)\n79\t    (sequential? x) (mapv ->data x)\n80\t    :else {::opaque true}))\n81\t\n82\t\n83\t(defn digest-of\n84\t  \"The digest form ->data gives host bytes `bs`.\"\n85\t  [bs]\n86\t  {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 bs)})\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t;; =============================================================================\n90\t;; Scratch roots\n91\t;; =============================================================================\n92\t\n93\t\n94\t(defn temp-root\n95\t  \"A fresh scratch root under target/.\"\n96\t  []\n97\t  (str \"target/stage-e-\" (random-uuid)))\n98\t\n99\t\n100\t(defn cleanup-root!\n101\t  [dir]\n102\t  #?(:cljd (try (.deleteSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n103\t                (catch Object _ nil))\n104\t     :clj (letfn [(delete-recursively!\n105\t                    [f]\n106\t                    (when (.isDirectory f)\n107\t                      (doseq [child (.listFiles f)]\n108\t                        (delete-recursively! child)))\n109\t                    (.delete f))]\n110\t            (delete-recursively! (io/file dir)))\n111\t     :cljs (try (.rmSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true :force true})\n112\t                (catch :default _ nil))))\n113\t\n114\t\n115\t(defn- ensure-dir!\n116\t  [dir]\n117\t  #?(:cljd (let [d (dart-io/Directory. dir)]\n118\t             (when-not (.existsSync d) (.createSync d .recursive true)))\n119\t     :clj (.mkdirs (io/file dir))\n120\t     :cljs (.mkdirSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true})))\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t(defn paths\n124\t  \"The durable media of the world over `root`.\"\n125\t  [root]\n126\t  {:authority (str root \"/authority\")\n127\t   :journals (str root \"/journals\")\n128\t   :store (str root \"/store.jing\")\n129\t   :side (str root \"/side\")})\n130\t\n131\t\n132\t(defn destroy-authority!\n133\t  \"Permanently lose the authority's state under `root`: its content file\n134\t   is overwritten with bytes that are no content log, the way a lost\n135\t   disk leaves it.  No reopen can recover a ledger from it.\"\n136\t  [root]\n137\t  (let [path (str (:authority (paths root)) \"/\" file-journal/content-name)]\n138\t    #?(:cljd (.writeAsStringSync (dart-io/File. path) \"lost authority state\")\n139\t       :clj (spit path \"lost authority state\")\n140\t       :cljs (.writeFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path \"lost authority state\"))))\n141\t\n142\t\n143\t;; =============================================================================\n144\t;; The life context: events, counters, the cut and the kill\n145\t;; =============================================================================\n146\t\n147\t\n148\t(defn context\n149\t  \"A life's context.  `emit!` takes each event map as it happens (a peer\n150\t   prints it at once); `at-cut` is called when the life's cut fires: a\n151\t   peer's never returns -- the parent kills the process inside it -- and\n152\t   the in-process runner's returns so the life can unwind dead.\"\n153\t  [{:keys [cut fail emit! at-cut]}]\n154\t  {:cut cut\n155\t   :fail fail\n156\t   :failed (atom nil)\n157\t   :emit! (or emit! (fn [_]))\n158\t   :at-cut (or at-cut (fn []))\n159\t   :dead (atom false)\n160\t   :fired (atom nil)\n161\t   :hits (atom {})\n162\t   :attaches (atom 0)\n163\t   :observes (atom 0)\n164\t   :opened (atom [])})\n165\t\n166\t\n167\t(defn killed?\n168\t  [e]\n169\t  (true? (::killed (ex-data e))))\n170\t\n171\t\n172\t(defn- dead-throw!\n173\t  []\n174\t  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a dead runtime wrote nothing\" {::killed true})))\n175\t\n176\t\n177\t(defn- fire!\n178\t  [ctx at]\n179\t  (reset! (:fired ctx) at)\n180\t  (reset! (:dead ctx) true)\n181\t  ((:emit! ctx) {:event :cut :cut (:cut ctx) :at at})\n182\t  ((:at-cut ctx))\n183\t  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: killed at a cut\" {::killed true :cut (:cut ctx)})))\n184\t\n185\t\n186\t;; =============================================================================\n187\t;; The named cuts\n188\t;; =============================================================================\n189\t\n190\t\n191\t(defn- record-is\n192\t  [journal-kind action]\n193\t  (fn [r]\n194\t    (and (= journal-kind (:yin.k/journal r))\n195\t         (or (nil? action) (= action (:yin.k/action r))))))\n196\t\n197\t\n198\t(defn- projection-of\n199\t  [c]\n200\t  (when-some [a (:authority c)]\n201\t    (authority/projection a)))\n202\t\n203\t\n204\t(defn- journal-records-of\n205\t  \"Holder `h`'s whole progress journal, read through a fresh open of its\n206\t   backend (the restart's view).\"\n207\t  [c h]\n208\t  (let [backend (get-in c [:progress h :backend])\n209\t        j (if (some? backend)\n210\t            (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! backend nil))\n211\t            (compose/journal-of c h))]\n212\t    (if (nil? j)\n213\t      []\n214\t      (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor j :dao.stream/oldest))\n215\t             records []]\n216\t        (let [answer (stream/next j cursor)]\n217\t          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n218\t            (recur (:dao.stream/cursor answer) (conj records (:dao.stream/value answer)))\n219\t            records))))))\n220\t\n221\t\n222\t(defn- holder-records-match?\n223\t  [c h pred]\n224\t  (boolean (some pred (journal-records-of c h))))\n225\t\n226\t\n227\t(defn- exit-occurrence\n228\t  [c h]\n229\t  (get-in c [:holders h :exit :occurrence]))\n230\t\n231\t\n232\t(defn- read-values\n233\t  [h]\n234\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n235\t         values []]\n236\t    (let [r (stream/next h cursor)]\n237\t      (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)) (< (count values) 1000))\n238\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)))\n239\t        values))))\n240\t\n241\t\n242\t(defn inbound-of\n243\t  \"The requests of `kind` (every request when nil) that reached holder\n244\t   `h`'s inbound in this life, in stream order.\"\n245\t  [c h kind]\n246\t  (if-some [inbound (get-in c [:inbounds h])]\n247\t    (filterv #(or (nil? kind) (= kind (:yin.k/request %))) (read-values inbound))\n248\t    []))\n249\t\n250\t\n251\t(defn- admission-commit?\n252\t  \"Whether ledger record `r` is the transaction that commits an admitted\n253\t   effect: one of its datoms is the :yin.k/admitted custody fact.\"\n254\t  [r]\n255\t  (boolean (some (fn [d]\n256\t                   (and (sequential? d)\n257\t                        (= :yin.k/custody (nth d 1 nil))\n258\t                        (= :yin.k/admitted (nth d 2 nil))))\n259\t                 (get-in r [:dao.space/transaction :datoms]))))\n260\t\n261\t\n262\t(def cuts\n263\t  \"Every named cut a scenario may ask for: where it fires and when.\n264\t   :site is a journal ([:progress h] or [:reply h]), :authority, :store\n265\t   or :tick; :when is :before or :after the matched write (a tick cut\n266\t   fires after the tick whose composition matches); :match is a\n267\t   predicate over the decoded journal record, the put ({:address a}) or\n268\t   the composition; :nth counts matches (default 1).\"\n269\t  {;; ---- row 7: completion\n270\t   :row7/after-successor-append\n271\t   {:site :tick\n272\t    :match (fn [c]\n273\t             (let [s (exit-occurrence c \"h1\")]\n274\t               (and (some? s)\n275\t                    (holder-records-match?\n276\t                      c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer) %)\n277\t                                   (= s (:yin.k/occurrence %)))))))}\n278\t   :row7/after-resumed-report\n279\t   {:site :tick\n280\t    :match (fn [c]\n281\t             (let [l (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :lease])]\n282\t               (and (some? l)\n283\t                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:leases l :yin.k/result])))))}\n284\t   :row7/after-release-append\n285\t   {:site :tick\n286\t    :match (fn [c]\n287\t             (holder-records-match?\n288\t               c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/release) %)\n289\t                            (= :dao.stream/ok (:yin.k/append %)))))}\n290\t   :row7/after-closure\n291\t   {:site :tick\n292\t    :match (fn [c]\n293\t             (let [o (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :occurrence])]\n294\t               (and (some? o)\n295\t                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed])))))}\n296\t   :row7/while-running\n297\t   {:site :tick\n298\t    :match (fn [c] (= :running (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :phase])))}\n299\t\n300\t   ;; ---- row 4 and clause 8: around the atomic effect commitment (the\n301\t   ;; ledger transaction that records the admitted effect)\n302\t   :row4/before-commit\n303\t   {:site :authority :when :before :match admission-commit?}\n304\t   :row4/after-commit\n305\t   {:site :authority :when :after :match admission-commit?}\n306\t   :row4/before-result-append\n307\t   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n308\t    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n309\t   :row4/admit-uncarried\n310\t   {:site :tick\n311\t    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}\n312\t\n313\t   ;; ---- row 5: the input record\n314\t   :row5/input-uncarried\n315\t   {:site :tick\n316\t    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/input)))}\n317\t   :row5/input-carried\n318\t   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :after\n319\t    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/input (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n320\t\n321\t   ;; ---- row 2 and the D14 journal brackets: the export's phases\n322\t   :export/after-minted\n323\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/minted nil)}\n324\t   :export/after-serve-intent\n325\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/serve)}\n326\t   :export/after-serve-ack\n327\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/serve)}\n328\t   :export/after-store-intent\n329\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/store)}\n330\t   :export/store-put-before\n331\t   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true)}\n332\t   :export/store-put-after\n333\t   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true)}\n334\t   :export/after-store-ack\n335\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/store)}\n336\t   :export/before-fenced\n337\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n338\t   :export/after-fenced\n339\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n340\t   :export/after-offer-intent\n341\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/offer)}\n342\t   :export/after-offer-attempt\n343\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer)}\n344\t   :export/after-offer-ack\n345\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/offer)}\n346\t\n347\t   ;; ---- the inbox retention machine (D15a) and the grant bracket\n348\t   :inbox/before-retention\n349\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n350\t   :inbox/after-retention\n351\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n352\t   :journal/before-proposal-attempt\n353\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/proposal)}\n354\t   :journal/after-proposal-intent\n355\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/proposal)}\n356\t   :journal/after-grant-ack\n357\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/grant)}\n358\t   :journal/after-resumed-intent\n359\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/resumed)}\n360\t   :journal/after-release-intent\n361\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/release)}\n362\t\n363\t   ;; ---- clause 8: after the first commit's reply stands\n364\t   :clause8/committed\n365\t   {:site :tick\n366\t    :match (fn [c]\n367\t             (some #(and (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply %))\n368\t                         (= :committed (get-in % [:yin.k/answer :yin.k/admission])))\n369\t                   (if-some [j (get-in c [:reply-journals \"h1\" :journal])]\n370\t                     (read-values j)\n371\t                     [])))}\n372\t\n373\t   ;; ---- row 6: a lost reply (the process dies before the front's\n374\t   ;; append of the proposal's reply)\n375\t   :row6/proposal-reply-lost\n376\t   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n377\t    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/proposal (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n378\t\n379\t   ;; ---- the freeze's second stored object (the body)\n380\t   :export/body-put-before\n381\t   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n382\t   :export/body-put-after\n383\t   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n384\t\n385\t   ;; ---- clause 3: between assign and discharge\n386\t   :seq/after-assign\n387\t   {:site :tick\n388\t    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}})\n389\t\n390\t\n391\t(defn- cut-spec\n392\t  [ctx]\n393\t  (when-some [k (:cut ctx)]\n394\t    (or (get cuts k)\n395\t        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: unknown cut\" {:cut k})))))\n396\t\n397\t\n398\t(defn- hit!\n399\t  \"Whether the life's cut matches this write at `site` (counted against\n400\t   :nth), answering :before, :after or nil.\"\n401\t  [ctx site subject]\n402\t  (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n403\t    (when (and (some? spec)\n404\t               (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n405\t               (= site (:site spec))\n406\t               ((:match spec) subject))\n407\t      (let [n (get (swap! (:hits ctx) update site (fnil inc 0)) site)]\n408\t        (when (= n (or (:nth spec) 1))\n409\t          (or (:when spec) :after))))))\n410\t\n411\t\n412\t;; =============================================================================\n413\t;; Mortal media\n414\t;; =============================================================================\n415\t\n416\t\n417\t(defn- frame-record\n418\t  [bs]\n419\t  (try\n420\t    (::journal/value (cbor/decode bs))\n421\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n422\t\n423\t\n424\t(defn- fail-hit!\n425\t  \"Whether the life's uncertain-append failure ({:like cut-name\n426\t   :persist? bool}) matches this write at `site`: the first match only.\"\n427\t  [ctx site subject]\n428\t  (when-some [{:keys [like]} (:fail ctx)]\n429\t    (let [spec (get cuts like)]\n430\t      (when (and (nil? @(:failed ctx))\n431\t                 (= site (:site spec))\n432\t                 ((:match spec) subject))\n433\t        (reset! (:failed ctx) {:site site :like like})\n434\t        true))))\n435\t\n436\t\n437\t(defn mortal-backend\n438\t  \"Journal backend `b` at `site`, mortal under `ctx`: once the life is\n439\t   dead every frame write throws having written nothing, and the life's\n440\t   cut, when it names this site, fires before or after its frame.\"\n441\t  [ctx site b]\n442\t  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:backend b])\n443\t  (let [write! (::journal/write-frame! b)\n444\t        truncate! (::journal/truncate! b)]\n445\t    (assoc b\n446\t           ::journal/write-frame!\n447\t           (fn [bs]\n448\t             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n449\t             (when (fail-hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))\n450\t               ;; an uncertain append: the frame lands or not, and the\n451\t               ;; writer is answered a throw either way -- the process\n452\t               ;; lives on, its journal's answer unknown\n453\t               (when (:persist? (:fail ctx)) (write! bs))\n454\t               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :uncertain :site site\n455\t                              :persisted? (boolean (:persist? (:fail ctx)))\n456\t                              :record (->data (frame-record bs))})\n457\t               (throw (ex-info \"stage E: an uncertain append\" {::uncertain true})))\n458\t             (let [hit (hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))]\n459\t               (when (= :before hit)\n460\t                 (fire! ctx {:site site :when :before\n461\t                             :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n462\t               (let [r (write! bs)]\n463\t                 (when (= :after hit)\n464\t                   (fire! ctx {:site site :when :after\n465\t                               :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n466\t                 r)))\n467\t           ::journal/truncate!\n468\t           (fn [n]\n469\t             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n470\t             (truncate! n)))))\n471\t\n472\t\n473\t(defn mortal-store\n474\t  \"Content store `base`, mortal under `ctx`, its puts cut at :store; its\n475\t   gets answer the default for every address in `unreadable` (an\n476\t   accepted checkpoint whose bytes cannot be read).\"\n477\t  [ctx base unreadable]\n478\t  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:store base])\n479\t  (let [put! (:put-bytes-fn base)\n480\t        get! (:get-bytes-fn base)]\n481\t    (assoc base\n482\t           :put-bytes-fn\n483\t           (fn [address bs]\n484\t             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n485\t             (let [hit (hit! ctx :store {:address address})]\n486\t               (when (= :before hit)\n487\t                 (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :before :address address}))\n488\t               (let [r (put! address bs)]\n489\t                 (when (= :after hit)\n490\t                   (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :after :address address}))\n491\t                 r)))\n492\t           :get-bytes-fn\n493\t           (fn\n494\t             ([address] (get! address))\n495\t             ([address default]\n496\t              (if (contains? unreadable address)\n497\t                default\n498\t                (get! address default)))))))\n499\t\n500\t\n501\t(defn- open-file-backend!\n502\t  [dir]\n503\t  (ensure-dir! dir)\n504\t  (let [r (file-journal/backend! dir)]\n505\t    (or (::file-journal/backend r)\n506\t        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a durable journal directory refused\"\n507\t                        {:dir dir :answer r})))))\n508\t\n509\t\n510\t(defn- mortal-journals\n511\t  \"compose/file-journals over `root`, every backend it opens mortal at\n512\t   [:progress h] or [:reply h].\"\n513\t  [ctx root]\n514\t  (let [base (compose/file-journals root)]\n515\t    (assoc base\n516\t           :progress-backend!\n517\t           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:progress h] ((:progress-backend! base) h)))\n518\t           :reply-backend!\n519\t           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:reply h] ((:reply-backend! base) h))))))\n520\t\n521\t\n522\t;; =============================================================================\n523\t;; Streams outside custody\n524\t;; =============================================================================\n525\t\n526\t\n527\t(defn scenario-stream\n528\t  \"A stream outside custody, rebuilt by every life under its fixed\n529\t   `identity`: `values` at integer positions from zero, positions below\n530\t   `floor` evicted (their reads answer gap with the floor as the\n531\t   successor cursor).  Integer positions make a position lifted from one\n532\t   life's instance a valid cursor on the next life's.\"\n533\t  [identity values floor]\n534\t  (let [vs (atom (vec values))]\n535\t    (reify\n536\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n537\t      (descriptor\n538\t        [_]\n539\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n540\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n541\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n542\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n543\t\n544\t\n545\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n546\t\n547\t      (cursor\n548\t        [_ _anchor]\n549\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor floor})\n550\t\n551\t      (next\n552\t        [_ cursor]\n553\t        (let [values @vs]\n554\t          (cond\n555\t            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count values))))\n556\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n557\t            (< cursor floor)\n558\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/cursor floor}\n559\t            (< cursor (count values))\n560\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n561\t             :dao.stream/value (nth values cursor)\n562\t             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n563\t            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n564\t\n565\t\n566\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n567\t\n568\t      (append!\n569\t        [_ x]\n570\t        (swap! vs conj x)\n571\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n572\t\n573\t\n574\t(defn journal-stream\n575\t  \"A durable stream over journal handle `j` under the fixed `identity`:\n576\t   integer positions over the journal's own, so every life reads the\n577\t   whole history any life appended -- the side log of at-least-once\n578\t   external IO.\"\n579\t  [identity j]\n580\t  (let [jid (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor j))]\n581\t    (reify\n582\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n583\t      (descriptor\n584\t        [_]\n585\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n586\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n587\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n588\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n589\t\n590\t\n591\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n592\t\n593\t      (cursor\n594\t        [_ _anchor]\n595\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n596\t\n597\t      (next\n598\t        [_ cursor]\n599\t        (if-not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor))\n600\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n601\t          (let [r (stream/next j {:dao.stream.memory-log/identity jid\n602\t                                  :dao.stream.memory-log/position cursor})]\n603\t            (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n604\t              :dao.stream/ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n605\t                              :dao.stream/value (:dao.stream/value r)\n606\t                              :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n607\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n608\t\n609\t\n610\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n611\t\n612\t      (append!\n613\t        [_ x]\n614\t        (stream/append! j x)))))\n615\t\n616\t\n617\t(defn- answering-inbound\n618\t  \"A log-shaped inbound whose appends answer `@outcome`: :dao.stream/ok\n619\t   lands the request; any other outcome lands nothing (the carrier full,\n620\t   refusing, or failing under the send).\"\n621\t  [identity outcome]\n622\t  (let [values (atom [])]\n623\t    (reify\n624\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n625\t      (descriptor\n626\t        [_]\n627\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n628\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n629\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n630\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n631\t\n632\t\n633\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n634\t\n635\t      (cursor\n636\t        [_ _anchor]\n637\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n638\t\n639\t      (next\n640\t        [_ cursor]\n641\t        (let [vs @values]\n642\t          (cond\n643\t            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n644\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n645\t            (< cursor (count vs))\n646\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n647\t             :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n648\t             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n649\t            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n650\t\n651\t\n652\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n653\t\n654\t      (append!\n655\t        [_ x]\n656\t        (let [o @outcome]\n657\t          (when (= :dao.stream/ok o) (swap! values conj x))\n658\t          {:dao.stream/outcome o})))))\n659\t\n660\t\n661\t(defn- held-inbound\n662\t  \"A log-shaped inbound whose reads answer :blocked while `held` (an\n663\t   atom) is truthy: the holder's requests land, but the authority's\n664\t   front cannot read them -- the holder partitioned from its\n665\t   authority.  Healed, the front reads every request that landed.\"\n666\t  [identity held]\n667\t  (let [values (atom [])]\n668\t    (reify\n669\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n670\t      (descriptor\n671\t        [_]\n672\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n673\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n674\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n675\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n676\t\n677\t\n678\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n679\t\n680\t      (cursor\n681\t        [_ _anchor]\n682\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n683\t\n684\t      (next\n685\t        [_ cursor]\n686\t        (if @held\n687\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}\n688\t          (let [vs @values]\n689\t            (cond\n690\t              (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n691\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n692\t              (< cursor (count vs))\n693\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n694\t               :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n695\t               :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n696\t              :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n697\t\n698\t\n699\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n700\t\n701\t      (append!\n702\t        [_ x]\n703\t        (swap! values conj x)\n704\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n705\t\n706\t\n707\t(defn- log-writer\n708\t  []\n709\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n710\t    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})))\n711\t\n712\t\n713\t;; =============================================================================\n714\t;; Machines and holder seams\n715\t;; =============================================================================\n716\t\n717\t\n718\t(def prog-id \"prog-c\")\n719\t(def source-id \"src-s\")\n720\t(def side-id \"side-x\")\n721\t\n722\t\n723\t(defn- parked-reader-over\n724\t  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: one\n725\t   more delivered value and it halts with :done.\"\n726\t  [source]\n727\t  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n728\t                       (s/then {:type :stream/next, :source (s/v 'c)}\n729\t                               (s/lit :done)))\n730\t        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n731\t        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)]\n732\t    (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'c cref} :yin.k/gate :running))))\n733\t\n734\t\n735\t(defn- reading-writer\n736\t  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: the\n737\t   value it reads is written to the enrolled `target`, then :side to\n738\t   `side`, then it halts with :done.\"\n739\t  [source target side]\n740\t  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n741\t                       (s/let1 'v (s/next-of (s/v 'c))\n742\t                               (s/then {:type :stream/put, :target (s/v 'w),\n743\t                                        :val (s/v 'v)}\n744\t                                       (s/then {:type :stream/put,\n745\t                                                :target (s/v 'x),\n746\t                                                :val (s/lit :side)}\n747\t                                               (s/lit :done)))))\n748\t        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n749\t        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)\n750\t        [wref m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 target)\n751\t        [xref m4] (engine/attach-resource m3 side)]\n752\t    (vm/run (assoc m4 :store {'c cref, 'w wref, 'x xref}\n753\t                   :yin.k/gate :running))))\n754\t\n755\t\n756\t(defn- attach-over\n757\t  [ctx table]\n758\t  (fn [descriptor]\n759\t    (swap! (:attaches ctx) inc)\n760\t    (if-some [h (get table (:dao.stream/identity descriptor))]\n761\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/handle h}\n762\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found})))\n763\t\n764\t\n765\t(defn- observe-over\n766\t  [ctx]\n767\t  (fn [h op arg]\n768\t    (swap! (:observes ctx) inc)\n769\t    (case op\n770\t      :next (stream/next h arg)\n771\t      :cursor (stream/cursor h arg))))\n772\t\n773\t\n774\t(defn- same-id-server\n775\t  []\n776\t  (fn [h]\n777\t    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor h))]\n778\t      {:dao.stream/identity id\n779\t       :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n780\t                            :dao.stream/identity id}})))\n781\t\n782\t\n783\t;; =============================================================================\n784\t;; Opening a life's world\n785\t;; =============================================================================\n786\t\n787\t\n788\t(defn- composition-config\n789\t  [w mode]\n790\t  (cond-> {:mode mode\n791\t           :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n792\t           :store (:store w)\n793\t           :diagnostics (:diagnostics w)\n794\t           :medium \"stage-e\"\n795\t           :clock (fn [] {:s @(:clock w)})}\n796\t    (= :exclusive mode) (assoc :failure-model :process-crash\n797\t                               :backend (:authority-backend w)\n798\t                               :duration {:s 30}\n799\t                               :journals (:journals w))))\n800\t\n801\t\n802\t(defn- world-table\n803\t  \"The holder table and protection of the life's world kind.\"\n804\t  [w]\n805\t  (case (:kind w)\n806\t    :parked {:table (if (= :none (:attach w)) {} {prog-id (:prog w)})\n807\t             :protection {prog-id :at-least-once}}\n808\t    :rows {:table (cond-> {source-id (:source w) side-id (:side w)}\n809\t                    (:target w) (assoc (:target w) (:reader w)))\n810\t           :protection (cond-> {source-id :at-least-once side-id :at-least-once}\n811\t                         (:target w) (assoc (:target w) :enrolled))}))\n812\t\n813\t\n814\t(defn- holder-seams\n815\t  [ctx w]\n816\t  (let [{:keys [table protection]} (world-table w)]\n817\t    {:protection protection\n818\t     :receiver (s/new-machine)\n819\t     :attach! (attach-over ctx table)\n820\t     :observe! (observe-over ctx)\n821\t     :serve! (if (= :parked (:kind w))\n822\t               (fn [_h]\n823\t                 {:dao.stream/identity prog-id\n824\t                  :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n825\t                                       :dao.stream/identity prog-id}})\n826\t               (same-id-server))}))\n827\t\n828\t\n829\t(defn- source-machine\n830\t  [w]\n831\t  (case (:kind w)\n832\t    :parked (parked-reader-over (scenario-stream prog-id [] 0))\n833\t    :rows (reading-writer (:source w) (:reader w) (:side w))))\n834\t\n835\t\n836\t(defn open-world!\n837\t  \"Open the life's world over `spec`: the durable media, mortal under\n838\t   `ctx`, and the composition over them.  Answers the world map with\n839\t   :c the open composition, or :refusal the composition's data refusal.\"\n840\t  [ctx spec]\n841\t  (let [{:keys [root kind mode]} spec\n842\t        mode (or mode :exclusive)\n843\t        p (paths root)\n844\t        _ (ensure-dir! root)\n845\t        partitioned (atom false)\n846\t        authority-backend (when (= :exclusive mode)\n847\t                            (let [b (mortal-backend ctx :authority\n848\t                                                    (open-file-backend! (:authority p)))\n849\t                                  write! (::journal/write-frame! b)]\n850\t                              ;; the protected consumer partitioned from\n851\t                              ;; its authority: every frame write fails\n852\t                              ;; while the flag stands\n853\t                              (assoc b ::journal/write-frame!\n854\t                                     (fn [bs]\n855\t                                       (if @partitioned\n856\t                                         (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the authority is partitioned\" {}))\n857\t                                         (write! bs))))))\n858\t        store (mortal-store ctx (jing-file/create-content-file (:store p))\n859\t                            (set (:unreadable spec)))\n860\t        side-backend (when (= :rows kind)\n861\t                       (mortal-backend ctx :side (open-file-backend! (:side p))))\n862\t        side (when side-backend\n863\t               (journal-stream side-id (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! side-backend nil))))\n864\t        w {:root root\n865\t           :kind kind\n866\t           :mode mode\n867\t           :attach (:attach spec)\n868\t           :clock (atom (or (:clock spec) 1))\n869\t           :store store\n870\t           :diagnostics (log-writer)\n871\t           :authority-backend authority-backend\n872\t           :side-backend side-backend\n873\t           :journals (if (= :exclusive mode)\n874\t                       (mortal-journals ctx (:journals p))\n875\t                       (compose/memory-journals (atom {})))\n876\t           :prog (scenario-stream prog-id (or (:prog spec) []) 0)\n877\t           :source (scenario-stream source-id (or (:source spec) [\"A\"])\n878\t                                    (or (:evict-floor spec) 0))\n879\t           :side side\n880\t           :partitioned partitioned\n881\t           :carrier (atom :dao.stream/ok)\n882\t           :held (atom false)\n883\t           :inbound (:inbound spec)}\n884\t        opened (compose/open! (composition-config w mode))\n885\t        c (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition opened)]\n886\t    (if (nil? c)\n887\t      (assoc w :refusal (->data opened))\n888\t      (let [w (assoc w :c c)]\n889\t        (if (= :rows kind)\n890\t          (let [i (or (:target spec)\n891\t                      (let [e (compose/enroll! c)]\n892\t                        ((:emit! ctx) {:event :enrolled :target (:yin.k/target e)})\n893\t                        (:yin.k/target e)))]\n894\t            (assoc w :target i :reader (compose/target-reader c i)))\n895\t          w)))))\n896\t\n897\t\n898\t(defn release-dead!\n899\t  \"What the operating system does for a killed process, done for a life\n900\t   killed in this process: every file backend and the store it opened\n901\t   released, nothing written.\"\n902\t  [ctx]\n903\t  (doseq [[kind x] @(:opened ctx)]\n904\t    (try\n905\t      (case kind\n906\t        :backend (when (contains? x ::file-journal/close!) (file-journal/close! x))\n907\t        :store ((:close-fn x)))\n908\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n909\t\n910\t\n911\t(defn close-world!\n912\t  \"Release everything a live world holds: the composition (its journal\n913\t   backends), the authority backend, the side log and the store.\"\n914\t  [w]\n915\t  (let [safe (fn [f]\n916\t               (try (f) (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))]\n917\t    (when-some [c (:c w)] (safe #(compose/close! c)))\n918\t    (when-some [b (:authority-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n919\t    (when-some [b (:side-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n920\t    (when-some [close! (get-in w [:store :close-fn])] (safe close!))\n921\t    nil))\n922\t\n923\t\n924\t;; =============================================================================\n925\t;; Reading a live world\n926\t;; =============================================================================\n927\t\n928\t\n929\t(defn- journal-values\n930\t  [j]\n931\t  (if (nil? j)\n932\t    []\n933\t    (read-values j)))\n934\t\n935\t\n936\t(defn replies-of\n937\t  \"Every reply the composition's front wrote into holder `h`'s reply\n938\t   journal (both tenures': the journal is durable).\"\n939\t  [c h]\n940\t  (journal-values (get-in c [:reply-journals h :journal])))\n941\t\n942\t\n943\t(defn holder-summary\n944\t  [st]\n945\t  (->data (merge (select-keys st [:phase :status :detail :occurrence :lease])\n946\t                 {:epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n947\t                  :next-op-seq (get-in st [:machine :yin.k/custody :yin.k/next-op-seq])\n948\t                  :stopped? (:stopped? st)\n949\t                  :machine? (some? (:machine st))})))\n950\t\n951\t\n952\t(defn snapshot\n953\t  \"Everything a check may read of the live world, as data.\"\n954\t  [ctx w]\n955\t  (let [c (:c w)\n956\t        hs (sort (keys (:holders c)))]\n957\t    {:holders (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (holder-summary (get-in c [:holders h]))])) hs)\n958\t     :policy (:yin.k/policy c)\n959\t     :projection (->data (projection-of c))\n960\t     :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (journal-records-of c h))])) hs)\n961\t     :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (replies-of c h))])) hs)\n962\t     :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c h nil))])) hs)\n963\t     :targets (if-some [i (:target w)]\n964\t                {:target (->data i)\n965\t                 :values (->data (read-values (compose/target-reader c i)))}\n966\t                {})\n967\t     :outcomes (if-some [r (compose/outcome-reader c)]\n968\t                 (->data (read-values r))\n969\t                 [])\n970\t     :side (if-some [side (:side w)] (->data (read-values side)) [])\n971\t     :fences (into {}\n972\t                   (keep (fn [r]\n973\t                           (when (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n974\t                             (let [a (:yin.k/address r)\n975\t                                   bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) a nil)]\n976\t                               [a (when bs (digest-of bs))]))))\n977\t                   (mapcat #(journal-records-of c %) hs))\n978\t     :diagnostics (->data (read-values (:diagnostics w)))\n979\t     :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration c))\n980\t     :counts {:attaches @(:attaches ctx) :observes @(:observes ctx)}\n981\t     :clock @(:clock w)}))\n982\t\n983\t\n984\t;; =============================================================================\n985\t;; The life's program: plain-data operations over the composition\n986\t;; =============================================================================\n987\t\n988\t\n989\t(defn- durable-records\n990\t  \"Holder `h`'s progress journal: through the composition when this life\n991\t   composes `h`, else read from its durable directory (a holder a\n992\t   previous life ran).\"\n993\t  [w h]\n994\t  (if (contains? (get-in w [:c :holders]) h)\n995\t    (journal-records-of (:c w) h)\n996\t    (let [b (open-file-backend! (str (:journals (paths (:root w))) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]\n997\t      (try\n998\t        (journal-values (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil)))\n999\t        (finally (file-journal/close! b))))))\n1000\t\n1001\t\n1002\t(defn- checkpoint-from\n1003\t  \"The checkpoint a candidate is added over, read from the durable\n1004\t   journal of `of` and the store: :fence the source's export, :successor\n1005\t   the exit's successor, or an explicit {:address a}.\"\n1006\t  [w {:keys [kind of address]}]\n1007\t  (let [records (durable-records w of)\n1008\t        fence (fn [o]\n1009\t                (some (fn [r]\n1010\t                        (when (and (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n1011\t                                   (or (nil? o) (= o (:yin.k/occurrence r))))\n1012\t                          r))\n1013\t                      records))\n1014\t        address (case kind\n1015\t                  :fence (:yin.k/address (fence nil))\n1016\t                  :successor (let [mint (last (filter\n1017\t                                                (fn [r]\n1018\t                                                  (and (= :yin.k/minted (:yin.k/journal r))\n1019\t                                                       (= :yin.k/successor (:yin.k/role r))))\n1020\t                                                records))]\n1021\t                               (:yin.k/address (fence (:yin.k/occurrence mint))))\n1022\t                  :variant (:address (:variant w))\n1023\t                  :address address)\n1024\t        bs (when address ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) address nil))]\n1025\t    (when (nil? bs)\n1026\t      (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the checkpoint is absent from the store\"\n1027\t                      {:checkpoint {:kind kind :of of :address (->data address)}})))\n1028\t    {:address address :bytes bs}))\n1029\t\n1030\t\n1031\t(defn- inbound-for\n1032\t  \"Holder `h`'s inbound, when the life's spec names one: :answering, a\n1033\t   carrier whose appends answer the life's carrier outcome; :held, a\n1034\t   stream the front cannot read while the life holds the partition.\"\n1035\t  [w h]\n1036\t  (case (get (:inbound w) h)\n1037\t    :answering {:inbound (answering-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:carrier w))}\n1038\t    :held {:inbound (held-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:held w))}\n1039\t    nil))\n1040\t\n1041\t\n1042\t(defn- offer-variant!\n1043\t  \"A second encoding of the occurrence holder `h` fenced: the same body\n1044\t   in different canonical bytes (another id counter), put in the store\n1045\t   and offered through `h`'s own inbound.  Answers {:address :bytes}.\"\n1046\t  [w h]\n1047\t  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w {:kind :fence :of h})\n1048\t        body (cbor/decode bytes)\n1049\t        o (get-in body [:yin.k/custody :yin.k/occurrence])\n1050\t        v-bytes (cbor/encode (assoc body :yin.k/id-counter 9))\n1051\t        v-address (keyword \"segment\" (str \"blake3-\" (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 v-bytes)))]\n1052\t    ((:put-bytes-fn (:store w)) v-address v-bytes)\n1053\t    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n1054\t                    {:yin.k/request :yin.k/offer\n1055\t                     :yin.k/request-id [:stage-e/variant (str address)]\n1056\t                     :yin.k/id v-address\n1057\t                     :yin.k/bytes v-bytes\n1058\t                     :yin.k/medium \"stage-e\"})\n1059\t    {:address v-address :bytes v-bytes :occurrence o}))\n1060\t\n1061\t\n1062\t(defn- holder-config\n1063\t  [ctx w extra]\n1064\t  (merge (holder-seams ctx w) extra))\n1065\t\n1066\t\n1067\t(defn- add-source\n1068\t  [ctx w h]\n1069\t  (update w :c compose/source h (holder-config ctx w (merge {:machine (source-machine w)}\n1070\t                                                            (inbound-for w h)))))\n1071\t\n1072\t\n1073\t(defn- add-candidate\n1074\t  [ctx w h checkpoint opts]\n1075\t  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w checkpoint)\n1076\t        seams (holder-config ctx w (merge {:bytes bytes :address address}\n1077\t                                          (inbound-for w h)))\n1078\t        seams (if (= :none (:attach opts))\n1079\t                (assoc seams :attach! (fn [_] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found}))\n1080\t                seams)]\n1081\t    (update w :c compose/holder h seams)))\n1082\t\n1083\t\n1084\t(defn- dead?\n1085\t  [ctx]\n1086\t  @(:dead ctx))\n1087\t\n1088\t\n1089\t(defn- tick!\n1090\t  \"One tick of `f` over the world's composition; the life's tick cut is\n1091\t   checked after it.  A dead life ends here.\"\n1092\t  [ctx w f]\n1093\t  (let [c' (f (:c w))\n1094\t        w (assoc w :c c')]\n1095\t    (when (dead? ctx) (dead-throw!))\n1096\t    (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n1097\t      (when (and (some? spec) (= :tick (:site spec)) (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n1098\t                 ((:match spec) c'))\n1099\t        (fire! ctx {:site :tick\n1100\t                    :holders (into {} (map (fn [[h st]] [h (holder-summary st)])) (:holders c'))\n1101\t                    :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c' h nil))]))\n1102\t                                   (keys (:holders c')))})))\n1103\t    w))\n1104\t\n1105\t\n1106\t(def ^:private planes\n1107\t  {:step compose/step\n1108\t   :control compose/control-step\n1109\t   :program compose/program-step})\n1110\t\n1111\t\n1112\t(defn- phase?\n1113\t  [w h phase]\n1114\t  (= phase (get-in w [:c :holders h :phase])))\n1115\t\n1116\t\n1117\t(defn- until\n1118\t  \"Ticks of `plane` until `pred` holds of the world or `n` are spent;\n1119\t   answers [world held?].\"\n1120\t  [ctx w plane pred n]\n1121\t  (loop [w w k 0]\n1122\t    (if (pred w)\n1123\t      [w true]\n1124\t      (if (>= k n)\n1125\t        [w false]\n1126\t        (recur (tick! ctx w (get planes plane)) (inc k))))))\n1127\t\n1128\t\n1129\t(defn- admit-request\n1130\t  [rid target envelope]\n1131\t  {:yin.k/request :yin.k/admit\n1132\t   :yin.k/request-id rid\n1133\t   :yin.k/target target\n1134\t   :yin.k/fenced-envelope envelope})\n1135\t\n1136\t\n1137\t(defn- envelope\n1138\t  [lease epoch op-id value]\n1139\t  {:yin.k/envelope :yin.k/fenced-v1\n1140\t   :yin.k/incarnation lease\n1141\t   :yin.k/epoch epoch\n1142\t   :yin.k/op-id op-id\n1143\t   :yin.k/value value})\n1144\t\n1145\t\n1146\t(defn- holder-binding\n1147\t  [w h]\n1148\t  (let [st (get-in w [:c :holders h])]\n1149\t    {:lease (:lease st)\n1150\t     :epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n1151\t     :occurrence (:occurrence st)}))\n1152\t\n1153\t\n1154\t(defn- resolve-arg\n1155\t  \"Operation arguments may name a holder's live binding: [:binding h k].\"\n1156\t  [w x]\n1157\t  (if (and (vector? x) (= :binding (first x)))\n1158\t    (get (holder-binding w (nth x 1)) (nth x 2))\n1159\t    x))\n1160\t\n1161\t\n1162\t(defn- admit!\n1163\t  \"Append an authored admit to holder `h`'s inbound and run control ticks\n1164\t   until its reply lands (or `n` are spent).\"\n1165\t  [ctx w h {:keys [rid target lease epoch op-id value await?]}]\n1166\t  (let [target (cond (= :other target) (:other w)\n1167\t                     (some? target) (resolve-arg w target)\n1168\t                     :else (:target w))\n1169\t        lease (resolve-arg w lease)\n1170\t        epoch (resolve-arg w epoch)\n1171\t        op-id (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (resolve-arg w v)])) op-id)\n1172\t        n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n1173\t    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n1174\t                    (admit-request rid target (envelope lease epoch op-id value)))\n1175\t    (if (false? await?)\n1176\t      (tick! ctx w compose/control-step)\n1177\t      (first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)))))\n1178\t\n1179\t\n1180\t(defn- run-op\n1181\t  \"One operation of a life's program; answers [world report-additions].\"\n1182\t  [ctx w [op & args]]\n1183\t  (case op\n1184\t    :source [(add-source ctx w (first args)) nil]\n1185\t    :candidate (let [[h checkpoint opts] args]\n1186\t                 [(add-candidate ctx w h checkpoint opts) nil])\n1187\t    :until (let [[h phase n plane] args\n1188\t                 [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step) #(phase? % h phase) n)]\n1189\t             [w {:until [[h phase held?]]}])\n1190\t    :until-status (let [[h status n] args\n1191\t                        [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n1192\t                                         #(= status (get-in % [:c :holders h :status])) n)]\n1193\t                    [w {:until [[h status held?]]}])\n1194\t    :until-inbound (let [[h kind n plane] args\n1195\t                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n1196\t                                          #(seq (inbound-of (:c %) h kind)) n)]\n1197\t                     [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n1198\t    :until-reply (let [[h kind n plane] args\n1199\t                       [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n1200\t                                        #(some (fn [r] (= kind (:yin.k/reply r)))\n1201\t                                               (replies-of (:c %) h))\n1202\t                                        n)]\n1203\t                   [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n1204\t    :until-some (let [[phase n] args\n1205\t                      [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n1206\t                                       (fn [w]\n1207\t                                         (some #(= phase (:phase %))\n1208\t                                               (vals (get-in w [:c :holders]))))\n1209\t                                       n)]\n1210\t                  [w {:until [[:some phase held?]]}])\n1211\t    :until-journal (let [[h kind action n plane] args\n1212\t                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n1213\t                                          #(holder-records-match?\n1214\t                                             (:c %) h (record-is kind action))\n1215\t                                          n)]\n1216\t                     [w {:until [[h kind action held?]]}])\n1217\t    :ticks (let [[n plane] args]\n1218\t             [(reduce (fn [w _] (tick! ctx w (get planes (or plane :step)))) w (range n)) nil])\n1219\t    :hand-off [(update w :c compose/hand-off (first args)) nil]\n1220\t    :abort [(update w :c compose/abort (first args)) nil]\n1221\t    :clock (do (reset! (:clock w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1222\t    :append-prog (do (stream/append! (:prog w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1223\t    :admit (let [[h req] args] [(admit! ctx w h req) nil])\n1224\t    :enroll-other (let [e (compose/enroll! (:c w))]\n1225\t                    [(assoc w :other (:yin.k/target e)) {:other (->data (:yin.k/target e))}])\n1226\t    :snapshot (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n1227\t                ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key (first args) :snapshot snap})\n1228\t                [w {:snapshots {(first args) snap}}])\n1229\t    :binding (let [b (->data (holder-binding w (first args)))]\n1230\t               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :binding :holder (first args) :binding b})\n1231\t               [w {:bindings {(first args) b}}])\n1232\t    :inject (let [[h request] args\n1233\t                  n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n1234\t              (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h]) request)\n1235\t              [(first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)) nil])\n1236\t    :offer-variant (let [[h] args\n1237\t                         v (offer-variant! w h)]\n1238\t                     ((:emit! ctx) {:event :variant :address (:address v)})\n1239\t                     [(assoc w :variant v) {:variant (->data (:address v))}])\n1240\t    :carrier (do (reset! (:carrier w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1241\t    :hold (do (reset! (:held w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1242\t    :partition-authority (do (reset! (:partitioned w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1243\t    :die (fire! ctx {:site :explicit :at (first args)})\n1244\t    :at-open (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n1245\t               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key :at-open :snapshot snap})\n1246\t               [w {:at-open snap}])))\n1247\t\n1248\t\n1249\t(defn- merge-report\n1250\t  [report additions]\n1251\t  (merge-with (fn [a b] (if (and (map? a) (map? b)) (merge a b) (into a b)))\n1252\t              report additions))\n1253\t\n1254\t\n1255\t(defn- fork-row\n1256\t  \"A fork per host: fork runs when selected and is labelled fork, and an\n1257\t   exclusive requirement over a memory authority is refused, never\n1258\t   downgraded.\"\n1259\t  [ctx spec]\n1260\t  (let [refused (compose/open! {:mode :exclusive\n1261\t                                :failure-model :process-crash\n1262\t                                :backend (journal/memory-backend (atom []) nil)\n1263\t                                :duration {:s 30}\n1264\t                                :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n1265\t                                :store (jing-file/create-content-file\n1266\t                                         (str (:root spec) \"/refused.jing\"))\n1267\t                                :diagnostics (log-writer)\n1268\t                                :medium \"stage-e\"\n1269\t                                :clock (fn [] {:s 1})\n1270\t                                :journals (compose/file-journals\n1271\t                                            (str (:root spec) \"/refused\"))})\n1272\t        w (open-world! ctx (assoc spec :mode :fork :kind :parked))]\n1273\t    (try\n1274\t      (let [w (add-source ctx w \"h1\")\n1275\t            [w held?] (until ctx w :step #(phase? % \"h1\" :lifted) 12)]\n1276\t        {:refused (->data (dissoc refused :yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition))\n1277\t         :refused-composed? (some? (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition refused))\n1278\t         :fork {:held? held?\n1279\t                :policy (:yin.k/policy (:c w))\n1280\t                :status-policy (:yin.k/policy (compose/status (:c w)))\n1281\t                :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration (:c w)))\n1282\t                :holder (holder-summary (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\"]))\n1283\t                :address (->data (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\" :detail :yin.k/address]))\n1284\t                :journal (->data (journal-records-of (:c w) \"h1\"))\n1285\t                :offers (->data (inbound-of (:c w) \"h1\" :yin.k/offer))\n1286\t                :fronts (count (:fronts (:c w)))\n1287\t                :outcome-reader? (some? (compose/outcome-reader (:c w)))}})\n1288\t      (finally (close-world! w)))))\n1289\t\n1290\t\n1291\t(defn run-life\n1292\t  \"Run one life of `spec` under `ctx` and answer its report (plain data).\n1293\t\n1294\t   spec:\n1295\t     :root     the scenario root (the durable media)\n1296\t     :kind     :parked (the parked-reader source of rows 1, 2, 6, 7) or\n1297\t               :rows (the reading-writer source over an enrolled target\n1298\t               of rows 3, 4, 5, 8)\n1299\t     :target   the enrolled target a :rows life reuses (absent: enroll,\n1300\t               emitting {:event :enrolled})\n1301\t     :clock    the life's starting clock reading, in seconds\n1302\t     :prog     the program stream's values this life sees\n1303\t     :source   the source stream's values; :evict-floor its eviction\n1304\t     :unreadable addresses the store cannot read\n1305\t     :attach   :none for an attach table that holds nothing\n1306\t     :ops      the life's program, a vector of operations (run-op)\n1307\t     :lose-authority true to destroy the authority's state first\n1308\t     :fork-row true for the per-host fork row instead\n1309\t\n1310\t   The cut, when any, is the context's.  A dead life throws ::killed\n1311\t   out of here; the caller (peer or in-process runner) decides what a\n1312\t   kill means.\"\n1313\t  [ctx spec]\n1314\t  (when (:lose-authority spec)\n1315\t    (destroy-authority! (:root spec)))\n1316\t  (cond\n1317\t    (:fork-row spec)\n1318\t    (fork-row ctx spec)\n1319\t\n1320\t    ;; a lost ledger the durable backend itself refuses to open never\n1321\t    ;; reaches the composition: fail stop, reported as data\n1322\t    (and (:lose-authority spec)\n1323\t         (not= :dao.stream/ok\n1324\t               (:dao.stream/outcome\n1325\t                 (let [r (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec))))]\n1326\t                   (when-some [b (::file-journal/backend r)] (file-journal/close! b))\n1327\t                   r))))\n1328\t    {:refusal {:stage :authority-backend\n1329\t               :answer (->data (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec)))))}}\n1330\t\n1331\t    :else\n1332\t    (let [w (open-world! ctx spec)]\n1333\t      (if-some [refusal (:refusal w)]\n1334\t        (do (close-world! w)\n1335\t            {:refusal refusal})\n1336\t        (let [result (atom w)]\n1337\t          (try\n1338\t            (let [[w report] (reduce (fn [[w report] op]\n1339\t                                       (let [[w additions] (run-op ctx w op)]\n1340\t                                         (reset! result w)\n1341\t                                         [w (merge-report report additions)]))\n1342\t                                     [w {}]\n1343\t                                     (:ops spec))]\n1344\t              (reset! result w)\n1345\t              (assoc report :final (snapshot ctx w)))\n1346\t            (finally\n1347\t              (when-not (dead? ctx)\n1348\t                (close-world! @result)))))))))\n1349\t\n1350\t\n1351\t;; =============================================================================\n1352\t;; Inspection: the durable state after every life, read without mutating it\n1353\t;; =============================================================================\n1354\t\n1355\t\n1356\t(defn inspect\n1357\t  \"Read the durable state under `root` without mutating it: the\n1358\t   authority's projection through `authority/open!` (no reclaim, unlike\n1359\t   the grantor's reopen), the enrolled `targets`' committed values, the\n1360\t   outcome projection, each holder's progress and reply journal, and the\n1361\t   side log.\"\n1362\t  [{:keys [root holders targets]}]\n1363\t  (let [p (paths root)\n1364\t        backend (::file-journal/backend (file-journal/backend! (:authority p)))\n1365\t        opened (if backend (authority/open! backend nil) {:yin.k/status :backend-refused})\n1366\t        a (::authority/authority opened)\n1367\t        open-journal (fn [dir]\n1368\t                       (let [b (open-file-backend! dir)\n1369\t                             j (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil))]\n1370\t                         [b j]))\n1371\t        read-dir (fn [dir]\n1372\t                   (let [[b j] (open-journal dir)]\n1373\t                     (try (->data (journal-values j))\n1374\t                          (finally (file-journal/close! b)))))]\n1375\t    (try\n1376\t      {:status (:yin.k/status opened)\n1377\t       :projection (->data (when a (authority/projection a)))\n1378\t       :targets (into {}\n1379\t                      (map (fn [i]\n1380\t                             [(->data i) (if-some [r (when a (authority/target-reader a i))]\n1381\t                                           (->data (read-values r))\n1382\t                                           :absent)]))\n1383\t                      targets)\n1384\t       :outcomes (if a (->data (read-values (admission/outcome-reader a))) [])\n1385\t       :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]))\n1386\t                       holders)\n1387\t       :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-reply\"))]))\n1388\t                      holders)\n1389\t       :side (read-dir (:side p))}\n1390\t      (finally\n1391\t        (when a (authority/close! a))\n1392\t        (when backend (file-journal/close! backend))))))\n1393\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"a9c50d42-fa8f-4699-a12f-e6f22ec99991","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:32:26.412Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_world.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world\n  \"M-next stage E: the world one life of a crash/partition scenario runs\n   in, driven only through `yin.vm.ucf.compose` (linker-dht 14.2.4,\n   UCF 7.11.1 clause 10 and the composition halves of clauses 3 and 8).\n\n   A scenario is a sequence of lives over one root directory.  Every\n   piece of state a later life may read lives on durable file media\n   under that root -- the authority's ledger (a dao.stream.journal.file\n   backend), every holder's progress and reply journal\n   (`compose/file-journals`), the content store (a dao.jing.file\n   content file, the node's carrier for bodies and code) and the side\n   log of at-least-once external IO -- so a life is a fresh runtime:\n   nothing in memory crosses from one life to the next.  The program\n   and source streams are outside custody; each life rebuilds its own\n   instance of them under their fixed identities from the life's spec,\n   the way a receiver attaches a stream by its carried descriptor.\n\n   A life is plain data (`run-life`'s spec) and so is everything it\n   reports, so the same life runs in this process (the isolated-runtime\n   mode every lane has, Dart's only form) or inside a separate operating\n   system process (`yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer`, the JVM and Node process\n   transport) and its report is compared as data either way.\n\n   Kills.  Every durable medium is wrapped mortal: a named cut (the\n   `cuts` table) fires at one exact boundary -- before or after a given\n   journal frame, before or after a given content-store put, or after a\n   composition tick whose state matches -- and from then on the life is\n   dead.  Inside a peer process the cut prints its event and blocks\n   until the parent destroys the process (SIGKILL); in this process it\n   marks every medium dead (no further durable write happens) and\n   unwinds, and the runner releases the locks the dead runtime held --\n   the only thing an operating system does for a killed process.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.jing.file :as jing-file]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n            [dao.stream.journal.file :as file-journal]\n            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n                       [\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]]\n                :clj [[clojure.java.io :as io]])\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.admission :as admission]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.compose :as compose]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Plain data\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- host-bytes?\n  [x]\n  #?(:clj (bytes? x)\n     :cljs (instance? js/Uint8Array x)\n     :cljd (instance? typed/Uint8List x)))\n\n\n(defn ->data\n  \"`x` as plain data every host prints and reads back the same: maps,\n   vectors, sets, scalars.  Host bytes become their blake3 digest\n   ({::bytes hex}), so two byte strings compare equal exactly when their\n   bytes are; anything else that is not data (a handle, a function, a\n   machine) becomes {::opaque true}.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)\n        (number? x) (uuid? x))\n    x\n\n    (host-bytes? x) {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 x)}\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(->data k) (->data v)])) x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv ->data x)\n    (set? x) (into #{} (map ->data) x)\n    (sequential? x) (mapv ->data x)\n    :else {::opaque true}))\n\n\n(defn digest-of\n  \"The digest form ->data gives host bytes `bs`.\"\n  [bs]\n  {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 bs)})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Scratch roots\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn temp-root\n  \"A fresh scratch root under target/.\"\n  []\n  (str \"target/stage-e-\" (random-uuid)))\n\n\n(defn cleanup-root!\n  [dir]\n  #?(:cljd (try (.deleteSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n                (catch Object _ nil))\n     :clj (letfn [(delete-recursively!\n                    [f]\n                    (when (.isDirectory f)\n                      (doseq [child (.listFiles f)]\n                        (delete-recursively! child)))\n                    (.delete f))]\n            (delete-recursively! (io/file dir)))\n     :cljs (try (.rmSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true :force true})\n                (catch :default _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn- ensure-dir!\n  [dir]\n  #?(:cljd (let [d (dart-io/Directory. dir)]\n             (when-not (.existsSync d) (.createSync d .recursive true)))\n     :clj (.mkdirs (io/file dir))\n     :cljs (.mkdirSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true})))\n\n\n(defn paths\n  \"The durable media of the world over `root`.\"\n  [root]\n  {:authority (str root \"/authority\")\n   :journals (str root \"/journals\")\n   :store (str root \"/store.jing\")\n   :side (str root \"/side\")})\n\n\n(defn destroy-authority!\n  \"Permanently lose the authority's state under `root`: its content file\n   is overwritten with bytes that are no content log, the way a lost\n   disk leaves it.  No reopen can recover a ledger from it.\"\n  [root]\n  (let [path (str (:authority (paths root)) \"/\" file-journal/content-name)]\n    #?(:cljd (.writeAsStringSync (dart-io/File. path) \"lost authority state\")\n       :clj (spit path \"lost authority state\")\n       :cljs (.writeFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path \"lost authority state\"))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The life context: events, counters, the cut and the kill\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn context\n  \"A life's context.  `emit!` takes each event map as it happens (a peer\n   prints it at once); `at-cut` is called when the life's cut fires: a\n   peer's never returns -- the parent kills the process inside it -- and\n   the in-process runner's returns so the life can unwind dead.\"\n  [{:keys [cut fail emit! at-cut]}]\n  {:cut cut\n   :fail fail\n   :failed (atom nil)\n   :emit! (or emit! (fn [_]))\n   :at-cut (or at-cut (fn []))\n   :dead (atom false)\n   :fired (atom nil)\n   :hits (atom {})\n   :attaches (atom 0)\n   :observes (atom 0)\n   :opened (atom [])})\n\n\n(defn killed?\n  [e]\n  (true? (::killed (ex-data e))))\n\n\n(defn- dead-throw!\n  []\n  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a dead runtime wrote nothing\" {::killed true})))\n\n\n(defn- fire!\n  [ctx at]\n  (reset! (:fired ctx) at)\n  (reset! (:dead ctx) true)\n  ((:emit! ctx) {:event :cut :cut (:cut ctx) :at at})\n  ((:at-cut ctx))\n  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: killed at a cut\" {::killed true :cut (:cut ctx)})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The named cuts\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- record-is\n  [journal-kind action]\n  (fn [r]\n    (and (= journal-kind (:yin.k/journal r))\n         (or (nil? action) (= action (:yin.k/action r))))))\n\n\n(defn- projection-of\n  [c]\n  (when-some [a (:authority c)]\n    (authority/projection a)))\n\n\n(defn- journal-records-of\n  \"Holder `h`'s whole progress journal, read through a fresh open of its\n   backend (the restart's view).\"\n  [c h]\n  (let [backend (get-in c [:progress h :backend])\n        j (if (some? backend)\n            (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! backend nil))\n            (compose/journal-of c h))]\n    (if (nil? j)\n      []\n      (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor j :dao.stream/oldest))\n             records []]\n        (let [answer (stream/next j cursor)]\n          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n            (recur (:dao.stream/cursor answer) (conj records (:dao.stream/value answer)))\n            records))))))\n\n\n(defn- holder-records-match?\n  [c h pred]\n  (boolean (some pred (journal-records-of c h))))\n\n\n(defn- exit-occurrence\n  [c h]\n  (get-in c [:holders h :exit :occurrence]))\n\n\n(defn- read-values\n  [h]\n  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n         values []]\n    (let [r (stream/next h cursor)]\n      (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)) (< (count values) 1000))\n        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)))\n        values))))\n\n\n(defn inbound-of\n  \"The requests of `kind` (every request when nil) that reached holder\n   `h`'s inbound in this life, in stream order.\"\n  [c h kind]\n  (if-some [inbound (get-in c [:inbounds h])]\n    (filterv #(or (nil? kind) (= kind (:yin.k/request %))) (read-values inbound))\n    []))\n\n\n(defn- admission-commit?\n  \"Whether ledger record `r` is the transaction that commits an admitted\n   effect: one of its datoms is the :yin.k/admitted custody fact.\"\n  [r]\n  (boolean (some (fn [d]\n                   (and (sequential? d)\n                        (= :yin.k/custody (nth d 1 nil))\n                        (= :yin.k/admitted (nth d 2 nil))))\n                 (get-in r [:dao.space/transaction :datoms]))))\n\n\n(def cuts\n  \"Every named cut a scenario may ask for: where it fires and when.\n   :site is a journal ([:progress h] or [:reply h]), :authority, :store\n   or :tick; :when is :before or :after the matched write (a tick cut\n   fires after the tick whose composition matches); :match is a\n   predicate over the decoded journal record, the put ({:address a}) or\n   the composition; :nth counts matches (default 1).\"\n  {;; ---- row 7: completion\n   :row7/after-successor-append\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (let [s (exit-occurrence c \"h1\")]\n               (and (some? s)\n                    (holder-records-match?\n                      c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer) %)\n                                   (= s (:yin.k/occurrence %)))))))}\n   :row7/after-resumed-report\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (let [l (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :lease])]\n               (and (some? l)\n                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:leases l :yin.k/result])))))}\n   :row7/after-release-append\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (holder-records-match?\n               c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/release) %)\n                            (= :dao.stream/ok (:yin.k/append %)))))}\n   :row7/after-closure\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (let [o (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :occurrence])]\n               (and (some? o)\n                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed])))))}\n   :row7/while-running\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (= :running (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :phase])))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 4 and clause 8: around the atomic effect commitment (the\n   ;; ledger transaction that records the admitted effect)\n   :row4/before-commit\n   {:site :authority :when :before :match admission-commit?}\n   :row4/after-commit\n   {:site :authority :when :after :match admission-commit?}\n   :row4/before-result-append\n   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n   :row4/admit-uncarried\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 5: the input record\n   :row5/input-uncarried\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/input)))}\n   :row5/input-carried\n   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :after\n    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/input (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 2 and the D14 journal brackets: the export's phases\n   :export/after-minted\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/minted nil)}\n   :export/after-serve-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/serve)}\n   :export/after-serve-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/serve)}\n   :export/after-store-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/store)}\n   :export/store-put-before\n   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true)}\n   :export/store-put-after\n   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true)}\n   :export/after-store-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/store)}\n   :export/before-fenced\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n   :export/after-fenced\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n   :export/after-offer-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/offer)}\n   :export/after-offer-attempt\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer)}\n   :export/after-offer-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/offer)}\n\n   ;; ---- the inbox retention machine (D15a) and the grant bracket\n   :inbox/before-retention\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n   :inbox/after-retention\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n   :journal/before-proposal-attempt\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/proposal)}\n   :journal/after-proposal-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/proposal)}\n   :journal/after-grant-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/grant)}\n   :journal/after-resumed-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/resumed)}\n   :journal/after-release-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/release)}\n\n   ;; ---- clause 8: after the first commit's reply stands\n   :clause8/committed\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (some #(and (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply %))\n                         (= :committed (get-in % [:yin.k/answer :yin.k/admission])))\n                   (if-some [j (get-in c [:reply-journals \"h1\" :journal])]\n                     (read-values j)\n                     [])))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 6: a lost reply (the process dies before the front's\n   ;; append of the proposal's reply)\n   :row6/proposal-reply-lost\n   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/proposal (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n\n   ;; ---- the freeze's second stored object (the body)\n   :export/body-put-before\n   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n   :export/body-put-after\n   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n\n   ;; ---- clause 3: between assign and discharge\n   :seq/after-assign\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}})\n\n\n(defn- cut-spec\n  [ctx]\n  (when-some [k (:cut ctx)]\n    (or (get cuts k)\n        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: unknown cut\" {:cut k})))))\n\n\n(defn- hit!\n  \"Whether the life's cut matches this write at `site` (counted against\n   :nth), answering :before, :after or nil.\"\n  [ctx site subject]\n  (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n    (when (and (some? spec)\n               (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n               (= site (:site spec))\n               ((:match spec) subject))\n      (let [n (get (swap! (:hits ctx) update site (fnil inc 0)) site)]\n        (when (= n (or (:nth spec) 1))\n          (or (:when spec) :after))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Mortal media\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- frame-record\n  [bs]\n  (try\n    (::journal/value (cbor/decode bs))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n\n\n(defn- fail-hit!\n  \"Whether the life's uncertain-append failure ({:like cut-name\n   :persist? bool}) matches this write at `site`: the first match only.\"\n  [ctx site subject]\n  (when-some [{:keys [like]} (:fail ctx)]\n    (let [spec (get cuts like)]\n      (when (and (nil? @(:failed ctx))\n                 (= site (:site spec))\n                 ((:match spec) subject))\n        (reset! (:failed ctx) {:site site :like like})\n        true))))\n\n\n(defn mortal-backend\n  \"Journal backend `b` at `site`, mortal under `ctx`: once the life is\n   dead every frame write throws having written nothing, and the life's\n   cut, when it names this site, fires before or after its frame.\"\n  [ctx site b]\n  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:backend b])\n  (let [write! (::journal/write-frame! b)\n        truncate! (::journal/truncate! b)]\n    (assoc b\n           ::journal/write-frame!\n           (fn [bs]\n             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n             (when (fail-hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))\n               ;; an uncertain append: the frame lands or not, and the\n               ;; writer is answered a throw either way -- the process\n               ;; lives on, its journal's answer unknown\n               (when (:persist? (:fail ctx)) (write! bs))\n               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :uncertain :site site\n                              :persisted? (boolean (:persist? (:fail ctx)))\n                              :record (->data (frame-record bs))})\n               (throw (ex-info \"stage E: an uncertain append\" {::uncertain true})))\n             (let [hit (hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))]\n               (when (= :before hit)\n                 (fire! ctx {:site site :when :before\n                             :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n               (let [r (write! bs)]\n                 (when (= :after hit)\n                   (fire! ctx {:site site :when :after\n                               :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n                 r)))\n           ::journal/truncate!\n           (fn [n]\n             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n             (truncate! n)))))\n\n\n(defn mortal-store\n  \"Content store `base`, mortal under `ctx`, its puts cut at :store; its\n   gets answer the default for every address in `unreadable` (an\n   accepted checkpoint whose bytes cannot be read).\"\n  [ctx base unreadable]\n  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:store base])\n  (let [put! (:put-bytes-fn base)\n        get! (:get-bytes-fn base)]\n    (assoc base\n           :put-bytes-fn\n           (fn [address bs]\n             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n             (let [hit (hit! ctx :store {:address address})]\n               (when (= :before hit)\n                 (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :before :address address}))\n               (let [r (put! address bs)]\n                 (when (= :after hit)\n                   (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :after :address address}))\n                 r)))\n           :get-bytes-fn\n           (fn\n             ([address] (get! address))\n             ([address default]\n              (if (contains? unreadable address)\n                default\n                (get! address default)))))))\n\n\n(defn- open-file-backend!\n  [dir]\n  (ensure-dir! dir)\n  (let [r (file-journal/backend! dir)]\n    (or (::file-journal/backend r)\n        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a durable journal directory refused\"\n                        {:dir dir :answer r})))))\n\n\n(defn- mortal-journals\n  \"compose/file-journals over `root`, every backend it opens mortal at\n   [:progress h] or [:reply h].\"\n  [ctx root]\n  (let [base (compose/file-journals root)]\n    (assoc base\n           :progress-backend!\n           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:progress h] ((:progress-backend! base) h)))\n           :reply-backend!\n           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:reply h] ((:reply-backend! base) h))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Streams outside custody\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn scenario-stream\n  \"A stream outside custody, rebuilt by every life under its fixed\n   `identity`: `values` at integer positions from zero, positions below\n   `floor` evicted (their reads answer gap with the floor as the\n   successor cursor).  Integer positions make a position lifted from one\n   life's instance a valid cursor on the next life's.\"\n  [identity values floor]\n  (let [vs (atom (vec values))]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor floor})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (let [values @vs]\n          (cond\n            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count values))))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n            (< cursor floor)\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/cursor floor}\n            (< cursor (count values))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n             :dao.stream/value (nth values cursor)\n             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (swap! vs conj x)\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n\n\n(defn journal-stream\n  \"A durable stream over journal handle `j` under the fixed `identity`:\n   integer positions over the journal's own, so every life reads the\n   whole history any life appended -- the side log of at-least-once\n   external IO.\"\n  [identity j]\n  (let [jid (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor j))]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (if-not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor))\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n          (let [r (stream/next j {:dao.stream.memory-log/identity jid\n                                  :dao.stream.memory-log/position cursor})]\n            (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n              :dao.stream/ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n                              :dao.stream/value (:dao.stream/value r)\n                              :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (stream/append! j x)))))\n\n\n(defn- answering-inbound\n  \"A log-shaped inbound whose appends answer `@outcome`: :dao.stream/ok\n   lands the request; any other outcome lands nothing (the carrier full,\n   refusing, or failing under the send).\"\n  [identity outcome]\n  (let [values (atom [])]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (let [vs @values]\n          (cond\n            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n            (< cursor (count vs))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n             :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (let [o @outcome]\n          (when (= :dao.stream/ok o) (swap! values conj x))\n          {:dao.stream/outcome o})))))\n\n\n(defn- held-inbound\n  \"A log-shaped inbound whose reads answer :blocked while `held` (an\n   atom) is truthy: the holder's requests land, but the authority's\n   front cannot read them -- the holder partitioned from its\n   authority.  Healed, the front reads every request that landed.\"\n  [identity held]\n  (let [values (atom [])]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (if @held\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}\n          (let [vs @values]\n            (cond\n              (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n              (< cursor (count vs))\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n               :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n               :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n              :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (swap! values conj x)\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n\n\n(defn- log-writer\n  []\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Machines and holder seams\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(def prog-id \"prog-c\")\n(def source-id \"src-s\")\n(def side-id \"side-x\")\n\n\n(defn- parked-reader-over\n  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: one\n   more delivered value and it halts with :done.\"\n  [source]\n  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n                       (s/then {:type :stream/next, :source (s/v 'c)}\n                               (s/lit :done)))\n        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)]\n    (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'c cref} :yin.k/gate :running))))\n\n\n(defn- reading-writer\n  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: the\n   value it reads is written to the enrolled `target`, then :side to\n   `side`, then it halts with :done.\"\n  [source target side]\n  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n                       (s/let1 'v (s/next-of (s/v 'c))\n                               (s/then {:type :stream/put, :target (s/v 'w),\n                                        :val (s/v 'v)}\n                                       (s/then {:type :stream/put,\n                                                :target (s/v 'x),\n                                                :val (s/lit :side)}\n                                               (s/lit :done)))))\n        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)\n        [wref m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 target)\n        [xref m4] (engine/attach-resource m3 side)]\n    (vm/run (assoc m4 :store {'c cref, 'w wref, 'x xref}\n                   :yin.k/gate :running))))\n\n\n(defn- attach-over\n  [ctx table]\n  (fn [descriptor]\n    (swap! (:attaches ctx) inc)\n    (if-some [h (get table (:dao.stream/identity descriptor))]\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/handle h}\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found})))\n\n\n(defn- observe-over\n  [ctx]\n  (fn [h op arg]\n    (swap! (:observes ctx) inc)\n    (case op\n      :next (stream/next h arg)\n      :cursor (stream/cursor h arg))))\n\n\n(defn- same-id-server\n  []\n  (fn [h]\n    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor h))]\n      {:dao.stream/identity id\n       :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                            :dao.stream/identity id}})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Opening a life's world\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- composition-config\n  [w mode]\n  (cond-> {:mode mode\n           :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n           :store (:store w)\n           :diagnostics (:diagnostics w)\n           :medium \"stage-e\"\n           :clock (fn [] {:s @(:clock w)})}\n    (= :exclusive mode) (assoc :failure-model :process-crash\n                               :backend (:authority-backend w)\n                               :duration {:s 30}\n                               :journals (:journals w))))\n\n\n(defn- world-table\n  \"The holder table and protection of the life's world kind.\"\n  [w]\n  (case (:kind w)\n    :parked {:table (if (= :none (:attach w)) {} {prog-id (:prog w)})\n             :protection {prog-id :at-least-once}}\n    :rows {:table (cond-> {source-id (:source w) side-id (:side w)}\n                    (:target w) (assoc (:target w) (:reader w)))\n           :protection (cond-> {source-id :at-least-once side-id :at-least-once}\n                         (:target w) (assoc (:target w) :enrolled))}))\n\n\n(defn- holder-seams\n  [ctx w]\n  (let [{:keys [table protection]} (world-table w)]\n    {:protection protection\n     :receiver (s/new-machine)\n     :attach! (attach-over ctx table)\n     :observe! (observe-over ctx)\n     :serve! (if (= :parked (:kind w))\n               (fn [_h]\n                 {:dao.stream/identity prog-id\n                  :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                       :dao.stream/identity prog-id}})\n               (same-id-server))}))\n\n\n(defn- source-machine\n  [w]\n  (case (:kind w)\n    :parked (parked-reader-over (scenario-stream prog-id [] 0))\n    :rows (reading-writer (:source w) (:reader w) (:side w))))\n\n\n(defn open-world!\n  \"Open the life's world over `spec`: the durable media, mortal under\n   `ctx`, and the composition over them.  Answers the world map with\n   :c the open composition, or :refusal the composition's data refusal.\"\n  [ctx spec]\n  (let [{:keys [root kind mode]} spec\n        mode (or mode :exclusive)\n        p (paths root)\n        _ (ensure-dir! root)\n        partitioned (atom false)\n        authority-backend (when (= :exclusive mode)\n                            (let [b (mortal-backend ctx :authority\n                                                    (open-file-backend! (:authority p)))\n                                  write! (::journal/write-frame! b)]\n                              ;; the protected consumer partitioned from\n                              ;; its authority: every frame write fails\n                              ;; while the flag stands\n                              (assoc b ::journal/write-frame!\n                                     (fn [bs]\n                                       (if @partitioned\n                                         (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the authority is partitioned\" {}))\n                                         (write! bs))))))\n        store (mortal-store ctx (jing-file/create-content-file (:store p))\n                            (set (:unreadable spec)))\n        side-backend (when (= :rows kind)\n                       (mortal-backend ctx :side (open-file-backend! (:side p))))\n        side (when side-backend\n               (journal-stream side-id (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! side-backend nil))))\n        w {:root root\n           :kind kind\n           :mode mode\n           :attach (:attach spec)\n           :clock (atom (or (:clock spec) 1))\n           :store store\n           :diagnostics (log-writer)\n           :authority-backend authority-backend\n           :side-backend side-backend\n           :journals (if (= :exclusive mode)\n                       (mortal-journals ctx (:journals p))\n                       (compose/memory-journals (atom {})))\n           :prog (scenario-stream prog-id (or (:prog spec) []) 0)\n           :source (scenario-stream source-id (or (:source spec) [\"A\"])\n                                    (or (:evict-floor spec) 0))\n           :side side\n           :partitioned partitioned\n           :carrier (atom :dao.stream/ok)\n           :held (atom false)\n           :inbound (:inbound spec)}\n        opened (compose/open! (composition-config w mode))\n        c (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition opened)]\n    (if (nil? c)\n      (assoc w :refusal (->data opened))\n      (let [w (assoc w :c c)]\n        (if (= :rows kind)\n          (let [i (or (:target spec)\n                      (let [e (compose/enroll! c)]\n                        ((:emit! ctx) {:event :enrolled :target (:yin.k/target e)})\n                        (:yin.k/target e)))]\n            (assoc w :target i :reader (compose/target-reader c i)))\n          w)))))\n\n\n(defn release-dead!\n  \"What the operating system does for a killed process, done for a life\n   killed in this process: every file backend and the store it opened\n   released, nothing written.\"\n  [ctx]\n  (doseq [[kind x] @(:opened ctx)]\n    (try\n      (case kind\n        :backend (when (contains? x ::file-journal/close!) (file-journal/close! x))\n        :store ((:close-fn x)))\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn close-world!\n  \"Release everything a live world holds: the composition (its journal\n   backends), the authority backend, the side log and the store.\"\n  [w]\n  (let [safe (fn [f]\n               (try (f) (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))]\n    (when-some [c (:c w)] (safe #(compose/close! c)))\n    (when-some [b (:authority-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n    (when-some [b (:side-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n    (when-some [close! (get-in w [:store :close-fn])] (safe close!))\n    nil))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Reading a live world\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- journal-values\n  [j]\n  (if (nil? j)\n    []\n    (read-values j)))\n\n\n(defn replies-of\n  \"Every reply the composition's front wrote into holder `h`'s reply\n   journal (both tenures': the journal is durable).\"\n  [c h]\n  (journal-values (get-in c [:reply-journals h :journal])))\n\n\n(defn holder-summary\n  [st]\n  (->data (merge (select-keys st [:phase :status :detail :occurrence :lease])\n                 {:epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n                  :next-op-seq (get-in st [:machine :yin.k/custody :yin.k/next-op-seq])\n                  :stopped? (:stopped? st)\n                  :machine? (some? (:machine st))})))\n\n\n(defn snapshot\n  \"Everything a check may read of the live world, as data.\"\n  [ctx w]\n  (let [c (:c w)\n        hs (sort (keys (:holders c)))]\n    {:holders (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (holder-summary (get-in c [:holders h]))])) hs)\n     :policy (:yin.k/policy c)\n     :projection (->data (projection-of c))\n     :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (journal-records-of c h))])) hs)\n     :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (replies-of c h))])) hs)\n     :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c h nil))])) hs)\n     :targets (if-some [i (:target w)]\n                {:target (->data i)\n                 :values (->data (read-values (compose/target-reader c i)))}\n                {})\n     :outcomes (if-some [r (compose/outcome-reader c)]\n                 (->data (read-values r))\n                 [])\n     :side (if-some [side (:side w)] (->data (read-values side)) [])\n     :fences (into {}\n                   (keep (fn [r]\n                           (when (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n                             (let [a (:yin.k/address r)\n                                   bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) a nil)]\n                               [a (when bs (digest-of bs))]))))\n                   (mapcat #(journal-records-of c %) hs))\n     :diagnostics (->data (read-values (:diagnostics w)))\n     :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration c))\n     :counts {:attaches @(:attaches ctx) :observes @(:observes ctx)}\n     :clock @(:clock w)}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The life's program: plain-data operations over the composition\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- durable-records\n  \"Holder `h`'s progress journal: through the composition when this life\n   composes `h`, else read from its durable directory (a holder a\n   previous life ran).\"\n  [w h]\n  (if (contains? (get-in w [:c :holders]) h)\n    (journal-records-of (:c w) h)\n    (let [b (open-file-backend! (str (:journals (paths (:root w))) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]\n      (try\n        (journal-values (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil)))\n        (finally (file-journal/close! b))))))\n\n\n(defn- checkpoint-from\n  \"The checkpoint a candidate is added over, read from the durable\n   journal of `of` and the store: :fence the source's export, :successor\n   the exit's successor, or an explicit {:address a}.\"\n  [w {:keys [kind of address]}]\n  (let [records (durable-records w of)\n        fence (fn [o]\n                (some (fn [r]\n                        (when (and (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n                                   (or (nil? o) (= o (:yin.k/occurrence r))))\n                          r))\n                      records))\n        address (case kind\n                  :fence (:yin.k/address (fence nil))\n                  :successor (let [mint (last (filter\n                                                (fn [r]\n                                                  (and (= :yin.k/minted (:yin.k/journal r))\n                                                       (= :yin.k/successor (:yin.k/role r))))\n                                                records))]\n                               (:yin.k/address (fence (:yin.k/occurrence mint))))\n                  :variant (:address (:variant w))\n                  :address address)\n        bs (when address ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) address nil))]\n    (when (nil? bs)\n      (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the checkpoint is absent from the store\"\n                      {:checkpoint {:kind kind :of of :address (->data address)}})))\n    {:address address :bytes bs}))\n\n\n(defn- inbound-for\n  \"Holder `h`'s inbound, when the life's spec names one: :answering, a\n   carrier whose appends answer the life's carrier outcome; :held, a\n   stream the front cannot read while the life holds the partition.\"\n  [w h]\n  (case (get (:inbound w) h)\n    :answering {:inbound (answering-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:carrier w))}\n    :held {:inbound (held-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:held w))}\n    nil))\n\n\n(defn- offer-variant!\n  \"A second encoding of the occurrence holder `h` fenced: the same body\n   in different canonical bytes (another id counter), put in the store\n   and offered through `h`'s own inbound.  Answers {:address :bytes}.\"\n  [w h]\n  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w {:kind :fence :of h})\n        body (cbor/decode bytes)\n        o (get-in body [:yin.k/custody :yin.k/occurrence])\n        v-bytes (cbor/encode (assoc body :yin.k/id-counter 9))\n        v-address (keyword \"segment\" (str \"blake3-\" (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 v-bytes)))]\n    ((:put-bytes-fn (:store w)) v-address v-bytes)\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n                    {:yin.k/request :yin.k/offer\n                     :yin.k/request-id [:stage-e/variant (str address)]\n                     :yin.k/id v-address\n                     :yin.k/bytes v-bytes\n                     :yin.k/medium \"stage-e\"})\n    {:address v-address :bytes v-bytes :occurrence o}))\n\n\n(defn- holder-config\n  [ctx w extra]\n  (merge (holder-seams ctx w) extra))\n\n\n(defn- add-source\n  [ctx w h]\n  (update w :c compose/source h (holder-config ctx w (merge {:machine (source-machine w)}\n                                                            (inbound-for w h)))))\n\n\n(defn- add-candidate\n  [ctx w h checkpoint opts]\n  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w checkpoint)\n        seams (holder-config ctx w (merge {:bytes bytes :address address}\n                                          (inbound-for w h)))\n        seams (if (= :none (:attach opts))\n                (assoc seams :attach! (fn [_] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found}))\n                seams)]\n    (update w :c compose/holder h seams)))\n\n\n(defn- dead?\n  [ctx]\n  @(:dead ctx))\n\n\n(defn- tick!\n  \"One tick of `f` over the world's composition; the life's tick cut is\n   checked after it.  A dead life ends here.\"\n  [ctx w f]\n  (let [c' (f (:c w))\n        w (assoc w :c c')]\n    (when (dead? ctx) (dead-throw!))\n    (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n      (when (and (some? spec) (= :tick (:site spec)) (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n                 ((:match spec) c'))\n        (fire! ctx {:site :tick\n                    :holders (into {} (map (fn [[h st]] [h (holder-summary st)])) (:holders c'))\n                    :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c' h nil))]))\n                                   (keys (:holders c')))})))\n    w))\n\n\n(def ^:private planes\n  {:step compose/step\n   :control compose/control-step\n   :program compose/program-step})\n\n\n(defn- phase?\n  [w h phase]\n  (= phase (get-in w [:c :holders h :phase])))\n\n\n(defn- until\n  \"Ticks of `plane` until `pred` holds of the world or `n` are spent;\n   answers [world held?].\"\n  [ctx w plane pred n]\n  (loop [w w k 0]\n    (if (pred w)\n      [w true]\n      (if (>= k n)\n        [w false]\n        (recur (tick! ctx w (get planes plane)) (inc k))))))\n\n\n(defn- admit-request\n  [rid target envelope]\n  {:yin.k/request :yin.k/admit\n   :yin.k/request-id rid\n   :yin.k/target target\n   :yin.k/fenced-envelope envelope})\n\n\n(defn- envelope\n  [lease epoch op-id value]\n  {:yin.k/envelope :yin.k/fenced-v1\n   :yin.k/incarnation lease\n   :yin.k/epoch epoch\n   :yin.k/op-id op-id\n   :yin.k/value value})\n\n\n(defn- holder-binding\n  [w h]\n  (let [st (get-in w [:c :holders h])]\n    {:lease (:lease st)\n     :epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n     :occurrence (:occurrence st)}))\n\n\n(defn- resolve-arg\n  \"Operation arguments may name a holder's live binding: [:binding h k].\"\n  [w x]\n  (if (and (vector? x) (= :binding (first x)))\n    (get (holder-binding w (nth x 1)) (nth x 2))\n    x))\n\n\n(defn- admit!\n  \"Append an authored admit to holder `h`'s inbound and run control ticks\n   until its reply lands (or `n` are spent).\"\n  [ctx w h {:keys [rid target lease epoch op-id value await?]}]\n  (let [target (cond (= :other target) (:other w)\n                     (some? target) (resolve-arg w target)\n                     :else (:target w))\n        lease (resolve-arg w lease)\n        epoch (resolve-arg w epoch)\n        op-id (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (resolve-arg w v)])) op-id)\n        n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n                    (admit-request rid target (envelope lease epoch op-id value)))\n    (if (false? await?)\n      (tick! ctx w compose/control-step)\n      (first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)))))\n\n\n(defn- run-op\n  \"One operation of a life's program; answers [world report-additions].\"\n  [ctx w [op & args]]\n  (case op\n    :source [(add-source ctx w (first args)) nil]\n    :candidate (let [[h checkpoint opts] args]\n                 [(add-candidate ctx w h checkpoint opts) nil])\n    :until (let [[h phase n plane] args\n                 [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step) #(phase? % h phase) n)]\n             [w {:until [[h phase held?]]}])\n    :until-status (let [[h status n] args\n                        [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n                                         #(= status (get-in % [:c :holders h :status])) n)]\n                    [w {:until [[h status held?]]}])\n    :until-inbound (let [[h kind n plane] args\n                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n                                          #(seq (inbound-of (:c %) h kind)) n)]\n                     [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n    :until-reply (let [[h kind n plane] args\n                       [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n                                        #(some (fn [r] (= kind (:yin.k/reply r)))\n                                               (replies-of (:c %) h))\n                                        n)]\n                   [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n    :until-some (let [[phase n] args\n                      [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n                                       (fn [w]\n                                         (some #(= phase (:phase %))\n                                               (vals (get-in w [:c :holders]))))\n                                       n)]\n                  [w {:until [[:some phase held?]]}])\n    :until-journal (let [[h kind action n plane] args\n                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n                                          #(holder-records-match?\n                                             (:c %) h (record-is kind action))\n                                          n)]\n                     [w {:until [[h kind action held?]]}])\n    :ticks (let [[n plane] args]\n             [(reduce (fn [w _] (tick! ctx w (get planes (or plane :step)))) w (range n)) nil])\n    :hand-off [(update w :c compose/hand-off (first args)) nil]\n    :abort [(update w :c compose/abort (first args)) nil]\n    :clock (do (reset! (:clock w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :append-prog (do (stream/append! (:prog w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :admit (let [[h req] args] [(admit! ctx w h req) nil])\n    :enroll-other (let [e (compose/enroll! (:c w))]\n                    [(assoc w :other (:yin.k/target e)) {:other (->data (:yin.k/target e))}])\n    :snapshot (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n                ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key (first args) :snapshot snap})\n                [w {:snapshots {(first args) snap}}])\n    :binding (let [b (->data (holder-binding w (first args)))]\n               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :binding :holder (first args) :binding b})\n               [w {:bindings {(first args) b}}])\n    :inject (let [[h request] args\n                  n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n              (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h]) request)\n              [(first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)) nil])\n    :offer-variant (let [[h] args\n                         v (offer-variant! w h)]\n                     ((:emit! ctx) {:event :variant :address (:address v)})\n                     [(assoc w :variant v) {:variant (->data (:address v))}])\n    :carrier (do (reset! (:carrier w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :hold (do (reset! (:held w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :partition-authority (do (reset! (:partitioned w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :die (fire! ctx {:site :explicit :at (first args)})\n    :at-open (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key :at-open :snapshot snap})\n               [w {:at-open snap}])))\n\n\n(defn- merge-report\n  [report additions]\n  (merge-with (fn [a b] (if (and (map? a) (map? b)) (merge a b) (into a b)))\n              report additions))\n\n\n(defn- fork-row\n  \"A fork per host: fork runs when selected and is labelled fork, and an\n   exclusive requirement over a memory authority is refused, never\n   downgraded.\"\n  [ctx spec]\n  (let [refused (compose/open! {:mode :exclusive\n                                :failure-model :process-crash\n                                :backend (journal/memory-backend (atom []) nil)\n                                :duration {:s 30}\n                                :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n                                :store (jing-file/create-content-file\n                                         (str (:root spec) \"/refused.jing\"))\n                                :diagnostics (log-writer)\n                                :medium \"stage-e\"\n                                :clock (fn [] {:s 1})\n                                :journals (compose/file-journals\n                                            (str (:root spec) \"/refused\"))})\n        w (open-world! ctx (assoc spec :mode :fork :kind :parked))]\n    (try\n      (let [w (add-source ctx w \"h1\")\n            [w held?] (until ctx w :step #(phase? % \"h1\" :lifted) 12)]\n        {:refused (->data (dissoc refused :yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition))\n         :refused-composed? (some? (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition refused))\n         :fork {:held? held?\n                :policy (:yin.k/policy (:c w))\n                :status-policy (:yin.k/policy (compose/status (:c w)))\n                :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration (:c w)))\n                :holder (holder-summary (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\"]))\n                :address (->data (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\" :detail :yin.k/address]))\n                :journal (->data (journal-records-of (:c w) \"h1\"))\n                :offers (->data (inbound-of (:c w) \"h1\" :yin.k/offer))\n                :fronts (count (:fronts (:c w)))\n                :outcome-reader? (some? (compose/outcome-reader (:c w)))}})\n      (finally (close-world! w)))))\n\n\n(defn run-life\n  \"Run one life of `spec` under `ctx` and answer its report (plain data).\n\n   spec:\n     :root     the scenario root (the durable media)\n     :kind     :parked (the parked-reader source of rows 1, 2, 6, 7) or\n               :rows (the reading-writer source over an enrolled target\n               of rows 3, 4, 5, 8)\n     :target   the enrolled target a :rows life reuses (absent: enroll,\n               emitting {:event :enrolled})\n     :clock    the life's starting clock reading, in seconds\n     :prog     the program stream's values this life sees\n     :source   the source stream's values; :evict-floor its eviction\n     :unreadable addresses the store cannot read\n     :attach   :none for an attach table that holds nothing\n     :ops      the life's program, a vector of operations (run-op)\n     :lose-authority true to destroy the authority's state first\n     :fork-row true for the per-host fork row instead\n\n   The cut, when any, is the context's.  A dead life throws ::killed\n   out of here; the caller (peer or in-process runner) decides what a\n   kill means.\"\n  [ctx spec]\n  (when (:lose-authority spec)\n    (destroy-authority! (:root spec)))\n  (cond\n    (:fork-row spec)\n    (fork-row ctx spec)\n\n    ;; a lost ledger the durable backend itself refuses to open never\n    ;; reaches the composition: fail stop, reported as data\n    (and (:lose-authority spec)\n         (not= :dao.stream/ok\n               (:dao.stream/outcome\n                 (let [r (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec))))]\n                   (when-some [b (::file-journal/backend r)] (file-journal/close! b))\n                   r))))\n    {:refusal {:stage :authority-backend\n               :answer (->data (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec)))))}}\n\n    :else\n    (let [w (open-world! ctx spec)]\n      (if-some [refusal (:refusal w)]\n        (do (close-world! w)\n            {:refusal refusal})\n        (let [result (atom w)]\n          (try\n            (let [[w report] (reduce (fn [[w report] op]\n                                       (let [[w additions] (run-op ctx w op)]\n                                         (reset! result w)\n                                         [w (merge-report report additions)]))\n                                     [w {}]\n                                     (:ops spec))]\n              (reset! result w)\n              (assoc report :final (snapshot ctx w)))\n            (finally\n              (when-not (dead? ctx)\n                (close-world! @result)))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Inspection: the durable state after every life, read without mutating it\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn inspect\n  \"Read the durable state under `root` without mutating it: the\n   authority's projection through `authority/open!` (no reclaim, unlike\n   the grantor's reopen), the enrolled `targets`' committed values, the\n   outcome projection, each holder's progress and reply journal, and the\n   side log.\"\n  [{:keys [root holders targets]}]\n  (let [p (paths root)\n        backend (::file-journal/backend (file-journal/backend! (:authority p)))\n        opened (if backend (authority/open! backend nil) {:yin.k/status :backend-refused})\n        a (::authority/authority opened)\n        open-journal (fn [dir]\n                       (let [b (open-file-backend! dir)\n                             j (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil))]\n                         [b j]))\n        read-dir (fn [dir]\n                   (let [[b j] (open-journal dir)]\n                     (try (->data (journal-values j))\n                          (finally (file-journal/close! b)))))]\n    (try\n      {:status (:yin.k/status opened)\n       :projection (->data (when a (authority/projection a)))\n       :targets (into {}\n                      (map (fn [i]\n                             [(->data i) (if-some [r (when a (authority/target-reader a i))]\n                                           (->data (read-values r))\n                                           :absent)]))\n                      targets)\n       :outcomes (if a (->data (read-values (admission/outcome-reader a))) [])\n       :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]))\n                       holders)\n       :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-reply\"))]))\n                      holders)\n       :side (read-dir (:side p))}\n      (finally\n        (when a (authority/close! a))\n        (when backend (file-journal/close! backend))))))\n","numLines":1393,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1393}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BAbT9kGBqMYiXJny5dZfPs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G3JtiNrJjdC5uvwpbw7ttm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-process-test\n2\t  \"M-next stage E across real processes: every scenario of\n3\t   yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-scenarios over the ordered JVM/Node host pairs of\n4\t   linker-dht 14.1.1 -- JVM to JVM and Node to Node as the same-host\n5\t   controls, JVM to Node and Node to JVM across hosts -- each life its\n6\t   own operating-system process (yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer) over the\n7\t   scenario's durable file media, each cut a real kill: the peer prints\n8\t   the cut and blocks, and this harness destroys it forcibly (SIGKILL)\n9\t   there.  Nothing crosses between lives but the bytes on disk: the\n10\t   authority's ledger, the journals, the content store's canonical\n11\t   bodies and the side log.\n12\t\n13\t   The Node peer is required: it is compiled here, before the first\n14\t   Node life (shadow-cljs's :vm-bench node-script build with the peer as\n15\t   its main, to target/stage-e-peer.js), so this gate cannot skip; a\n16\t   failed build fails the test.  The JVM peer runs from classes this\n17\t   harness compiles ahead of time into a fresh directory, so each JVM\n18\t   life starts in seconds.\n19\t\n20\t   No port is used and none is reserved.  Real processes are polled\n21\t   with bounded deadlines; every process is destroyed in a finally.  No\n22\t   wall-clock sleep is taken: time inside the protocol advances only by\n23\t   the clock readings a life's spec appends as ticks.\n24\t\n25\t   Each scenario run appends one line to the durability record\n26\t   (target/stage-e-durability.edn): the scenario, the host pair, and for\n27\t   every life its host, pid, cut and whether it was killed.\"\n28\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n29\t            [clojure.java.io :as io]\n30\t            [clojure.java.shell :as shell]\n31\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n32\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n33\t            [yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-scenarios :as sc])\n34\t  (:import (java.util.concurrent LinkedBlockingQueue TimeUnit)))\n35\t\n36\t\n37\t(def ^:private life-ms\n38\t  \"Bound on one life, from process start to its done or cut event.\"\n39\t  180000)\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(def pairs\n43\t  \"The ordered source/receiver host pairs this harness runs: the two\n44\t   same-host controls and both cross-host orders.\"\n45\t  [[:jvm :jvm] [:jvm :node] [:node :jvm] [:node :node]])\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t;; =============================================================================\n49\t;; The peers\n50\t;; =============================================================================\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t(def ^:private node-peer \"target/stage-e-peer.js\")\n54\t\n55\t\n56\t(def ^:private classes-dir\n57\t  (str \"target/stage-e-classes-\" (random-uuid)))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(defn- run-build!\n61\t  [what command]\n62\t  (let [{:keys [exit out err]} (apply shell/sh command)]\n63\t    (when-not (zero? exit)\n64\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"stage E: the \" what \" build failed\")\n65\t                      {:command command :exit exit :out out :err err})))))\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(def ^:private node-built\n69\t  (delay\n70\t    (run-build! \"Node peer\"\n71\t                [\"clj\" \"-M:cljs\" \"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"compile\" \"vm-bench\"\n72\t                 \"--config-merge\"\n73\t                 (str \"{:main yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer/main :output-to \\\"\" node-peer \"\\\"}\")])\n74\t    (when-not (.exists (io/file node-peer))\n75\t      (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the Node peer build wrote nothing\" {:path node-peer})))\n76\t    true))\n77\t\n78\t\n79\t(defn- java-bin\n80\t  []\n81\t  (str (System/getProperty \"java.home\") \"/bin/java\"))\n82\t\n83\t\n84\t(def ^:private jvm-built\n85\t  (delay\n86\t    (.mkdirs (io/file classes-dir))\n87\t    (run-build! \"JVM peer classes\"\n88\t                [(java-bin) \"-cp\" (str classes-dir java.io.File/pathSeparator\n89\t                                       (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\"))\n90\t                 \"clojure.main\" \"-e\"\n91\t                 (str \"(binding [*compile-path* \\\"\" classes-dir \"\\\"]\"\n92\t                      \" (compile 'yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer))\")])\n93\t    true))\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t(defn- command\n97\t  [host spec-path]\n98\t  (case host\n99\t    :jvm (do @jvm-built\n100\t             [(java-bin) \"-cp\" (str classes-dir java.io.File/pathSeparator\n101\t                                    (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\"))\n102\t              \"clojure.main\" \"-m\" \"yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer\" spec-path])\n103\t    :node (do @node-built\n104\t              [\"node\" node-peer spec-path])))\n105\t\n106\t\n107\t;; =============================================================================\n108\t;; One life, one process\n109\t;; =============================================================================\n110\t\n111\t\n112\t(defn- line-pump\n113\t  \"A daemon thread that puts every stdout line of `process` on a queue,\n114\t   then ::eof.\"\n115\t  [process]\n116\t  (let [q (LinkedBlockingQueue.)\n117\t        t (Thread. ^Runnable\n118\t           (fn []\n119\t             (try\n120\t               (with-open [r (io/reader (.getInputStream process))]\n121\t                 (doseq [line (line-seq r)]\n122\t                   (.put q line)))\n123\t               (catch Throwable _ nil)\n124\t               (finally (.put q ::eof)))))]\n125\t    (.setDaemon t true)\n126\t    (.start t)\n127\t    q))\n128\t\n129\t\n130\t(defn- parse-event\n131\t  [line]\n132\t  (when (str/starts-with? line \"E|\")\n133\t    (edn/read-string (subs line 2))))\n134\t\n135\t\n136\t(defn- destroy!\n137\t  [process]\n138\t  (.destroyForcibly process)\n139\t  (.waitFor process 30 TimeUnit/SECONDS))\n140\t\n141\t\n142\t(defn run-life-in-process!\n143\t  \"Run one life of `spec` as a peer process on `host`: answer the same\n144\t   result shape as the in-