{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012JGRydZsQDejh92U5sqCrC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.ledger-fixtures\n2\t  \"The cross-host ledger fixture of M-next C slice C12: one arbitration\n3\t   ledger holding every fact kind of yin.vm.ucf.ledger, built by a\n4\t   portable script (`build`) and pinned as its journal frames.\n5\t\n6\t   The pins live in test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v1.txt: a first\n7\t   line `ledger-v1`, a second `projection <digest>`, the BLAKE3 hex of\n8\t   the canonical bytes of the projection the frames fold to, then one\n9\t   journal frame per line as lowercase hex, header first.  Regenerate\n10\t   the file from a one-off JVM script with the string `render` returns,\n11\t   saved to `path`; the test proves on every host that the file equals\n12\t   `render`, so every host's rebuild has the pinned bytes.\n13\t\n14\t   Nothing here writes a file.\"\n15\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n16\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n17\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n18\t            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as cfx]\n19\t            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n20\t            [dao.lease :as lease]\n21\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n22\t            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n23\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n24\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n25\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.admission :as admission]\n26\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion :as completion]\n27\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant :as grant]\n28\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.input :as input]\n29\t            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint-fixtures :as fx]\n30\t            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]))\n31\t\n32\t\n33\t(def path\n34\t  \"The fixture file, relative to the repository root.\"\n35\t  \"test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v1.txt\")\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t(def arb \"arb-c12\")\n39\t\n40\t(def duration {:s 30})\n41\t\n42\t\n43\t;; The root, its continuation successor and a stranger occurrence.\n44\t(def r \"0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001\")\n45\t\n46\t(def s1 \"0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002\")\n47\t\n48\t(def x \"0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004\")\n49\t\n50\t\n51\t;; =============================================================================\n52\t;; World: the requests a holder and the composition make\n53\t;; =============================================================================\n54\t\n55\t(defn header-frame\n56\t  \"The journal header frame naming identity `i`.\"\n57\t  ([] (header-frame arb))\n58\t  ([i]\n59\t   (cbor/encode {:dao.stream.journal/header {:version 1 :identity i}})))\n60\t\n61\t\n62\t(defn origin\n63\t  [o l]\n64\t  {:yin.k/occurrence o :dao.lease/lease l :yin.k/emitter \"holder-a\"})\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t(defn park\n68\t  \"A blocked root of occurrence `o` with counter `n` and origin `org`,\n69\t   nil for a first park.\"\n70\t  ([o n] (park o n nil))\n71\t  ([o n org]\n72\t   (cond-> (assoc (get fx/fixtures \"first-park\")\n73\t                  :yin.k/occurrence o\n74\t                  :yin.k/next-op-seq n\n75\t                  :yin.k/arbitration {:dao.stream/identity arb\n76\t                                      :dao.stream/descriptor\n77\t                                      {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/journal}})\n78\t     (some? org) (assoc :yin.k/origin org))))\n79\t\n80\t\n81\t(defn halted\n82\t  \"A halted result of occurrence `o` under lease `l`.\"\n83\t  [o l]\n84\t  (assoc (get fx/fixtures \"halted-root\") :yin.k/origin (origin o l)))\n85\t\n86\t\n87\t(defn world\n88\t  \"A fresh world: the authority's frames (an atom), its content store and\n89\t   a diagnostic stream.\"\n90\t  []\n91\t  {:frames (atom [(header-frame)])\n92\t   :store (mem/create-content-mem)\n93\t   :diag (:dao.stream/handle\n94\t           (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n95\t                                ringbuffer/capacity-key 64}))})\n96\t\n97\t\n98\t(defn offer!\n99\t  [{:keys [a store]} b]\n100\t  (let [bs (cbor/encode b)]\n101\t    (grant/offer! a store (fx/segment-address bs) bs \"carrier\")))\n102\t\n103\t\n104\t(defn grant!\n105\t  [{:keys [a]} o l h]\n106\t  (stream/append! (grant/writer a)\n107\t                  (lease/grant l (custody/subject o) h duration\n108\t                               {:dao.lease/proposal (str \"p-\" l)})))\n109\t\n110\t\n111\t(defn lapse!\n112\t  [{:keys [a]} l cause]\n113\t  (stream/append! (grant/writer a) (lease/lapsed l cause)))\n114\t\n115\t\n116\t(defn refuse!\n117\t  \"The hook's refusal of `proposer`'s proposal pid, through the writer.\"\n118\t  [{:keys [a]} proposer pid]\n119\t  (stream/append! (grant/writer a)\n120\t                  (assoc (lease/refusal pid) :yin.k/proposer proposer)))\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t(defn report!\n124\t  \"holder-a reports body `b` as o's successor under l.\"\n125\t  [{:keys [a]} o l b]\n126\t  (let [bs (cbor/encode b)]\n127\t    (completion/report! a \"holder-a\"\n128\t                        (completion/resumed o l (fx/segment-address bs))\n129\t                        bs)))\n130\t\n131\t\n132\t(defn envelope\n133\t  [l e o n v]\n134\t  {:yin.k/envelope :yin.k/fenced-v1\n135\t   :yin.k/incarnation l\n136\t   :yin.k/epoch e\n137\t   :yin.k/op-id {:yin.k/occurrence o :yin.k/seq n}\n138\t   :yin.k/value v})\n139\t\n140\t\n141\t(defn admit!\n142\t  [{:keys [a store i diag]} l e o n v]\n143\t  (admission/admit! a store i \"holder-a\" (envelope l e o n v) diag))\n144\t\n145\t\n146\t(defn record!\n147\t  [{:keys [a]} o l e k observed]\n148\t  (input/record-input! a \"holder-a\"\n149\t                       (input/request o l e k\n150\t                                      {:yin.k/kind :yin.k/read :yin.k/name \"s\"}\n151\t                                      observed)))\n152\t\n153\t\n154\t(defn read-ok\n155\t  [v pos]\n156\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n157\t   :dao.stream/value v\n158\t   :dao.stream/cursor {:position pos}})\n159\t\n160\t\n161\t;; =============================================================================\n162\t;; The script\n163\t;; =============================================================================\n164\t\n165\t(defn answer\n166\t  \"One request's answer as a status keyword.\"\n167\t  [rep]\n168\t  (or (:yin.k/status rep) (:yin.k/admission rep) (:dao.stream/outcome rep)))\n169\t\n170\t\n171\t(def script-answers\n172\t  \"The answer each step of `build` gives, in order.\"\n173\t  [:committed                           ; enroll target i\n174\t   :committed                           ; offer r\n175\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-1 on r\n176\t   :recorded                            ; input 0 of r\n177\t   :committed                           ; admit (r 0)\n178\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; refuse holder-b's p-b\n179\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; reclaim lease-1, epoch 1\n180\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-2 on r\n181\t   :committed                           ; report s1\n182\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; release lease-2: r completes\n183\t   :committed                           ; offer s1\n184\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-3 on s1\n185\t   :committed                           ; report a halted result\n186\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; release lease-3: s1 terminates\n187\t   :committed                           ; offer x\n188\t   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-4 on x\n189\t   :committed                           ; admit (x 0) :v\n190\t   :intent-conflict                     ; admit (x 0) :w: x quarantined\n191\t   :committed])                         ; close target i\n192\t\n193\t\n194\t(defn build\n195\t  \"Run the script on a fresh memory-backed authority.  Answers the world\n196\t   with `:answers`, one per step, and the authority, left open.\"\n197\t  []\n198\t  (let [w0 (world)\n199\t        a (::authority/authority\n200\t            (authority/open! (journal/memory-backend (:frames w0) nil)))\n201\t        enrolled (authority/enroll! a)\n202\t        w (assoc w0 :a a :i (:yin.k/target enrolled))\n203\t        steps [#(offer! w (park r 0))\n204\t               #(grant! w r \"lease-1\" \"holder-a\")\n205\t               #(record! w r \"lease-1\" 0 0 (read-ok 7 1))\n206\t               #(admit! w \"lease-1\" 0 r 0 :v)\n207\t               #(refuse! w \"holder-b\" \"p-b\")\n208\t               #(lapse! w \"lease-1\" :policy)\n209\t               #(grant! w r \"lease-2\" \"holder-a\")\n210\t               #(report! w r \"lease-2\" (park s1 3 (origin r \"lease-2\")))\n211\t               #(lapse! w \"lease-2\" :release)\n212\t               #(offer! w (park s1 3 (origin r \"lease-2\")))\n213\t               #(grant! w s1 \"lease-3\" \"holder-a\")\n214\t               #(report! w s1 \"lease-3\" (halted s1 \"lease-3\"))\n215\t               #(lapse! w \"lease-3\" :release)\n216\t               #(offer! w (park x 0))\n217\t               #(grant! w x \"lease-4\" \"holder-a\")\n218\t               #(admit! w \"lease-4\" 0 x 0 :v)\n219\t               #(admit! w \"lease-4\" 0 x 0 :w)\n220\t               #(authority/close-target! a (:i w))]]\n221\t    (assoc w :answers (into [(answer enrolled)] (map #(answer (%))) steps))))\n222\t\n223\t\n224\t;; =============================================================================\n225\t;; Rendering and reading\n226\t;; =============================================================================\n227\t\n228\t(defn digest\n229\t  \"The BLAKE3 hex of the canonical bytes of projection `p`.\"\n230\t  [p]\n231\t  (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 (cbor/encode p)))\n232\t\n233\t\n234\t(defn hex\n235\t  [bs]\n236\t  (cfx/bytes->hex bs))\n237\t\n238\t\n239\t(defn render\n240\t  \"The fixture file's text, computed from `build` on this host.\"\n241\t  []\n242\t  (let [{:keys [a frames]} (build)]\n243\t    (str \"ledger-v1\\n\"\n244\t         \"projection \" (digest (authority/projection a)) \"\\n\"\n245\t         (str/join (map #(str (hex %) \"\\n\") @frames)))))\n246\t\n247\t\n248\t(defn read-file\n249\t  \"The fixture file as `{:digest d :frames [bytes ...]}`.\"\n250\t  []\n251\t  (let [[magic pin & frames] (remove str/blank?\n252\t                                     (str/split-lines (cfx/read-path path)))]\n253\t    (when-not (= \"ledger-v1\" magic)\n254\t      (throw (ex-info \"not a ledger-v1 fixture\" {:path path})))\n255\t    {:digest (subs pin (count \"projection \"))\n256\t     :frames (mapv cfx/hex->bytes frames)}))\n257\t\n258\t\n259\t(defn read-text\n260\t  \"The fixture file's text.\"\n261\t  []\n262\t  (cfx/read-path path))\n263\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"330d8937-6822-4441-9085-88bc6daf4d84","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:32:28.658Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/test/yin/vm/ucf/ledger_fixtures.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.ledger-fixtures\n  \"The cross-host ledger fixture of M-next C slice C12: one arbitration\n   ledger holding every fact kind of yin.vm.ucf.ledger, built by a\n   portable script (`build`) and pinned as its journal frames.\n\n   The pins live in test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v1.txt: a first\n   line `ledger-v1`, a second `projection <digest>`, the BLAKE3 hex of\n   the canonical bytes of the projection the frames fold to, then one\n   journal frame per line as lowercase hex, header first.  Regenerate\n   the file from a one-off JVM script with the string `render` returns,\n   saved to `path`; the test proves on every host that the file equals\n   `render`, so every host's rebuild has the pinned bytes.\n\n   Nothing here writes a file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as cfx]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [dao.lease :as lease]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.admission :as admission]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion :as completion]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant :as grant]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.input :as input]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint-fixtures :as fx]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]))\n\n\n(def path\n  \"The fixture file, relative to the repository root.\"\n  \"test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v1.txt\")\n\n\n(def arb \"arb-c12\")\n\n(def duration {:s 30})\n\n\n;; The root, its continuation successor and a stranger occurrence.\n(def r \"0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001\")\n\n(def s1 \"0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002\")\n\n(def x \"0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004\")\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; World: the requests a holder and the composition make\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn header-frame\n  \"The journal header frame naming identity `i`.\"\n  ([] (header-frame arb))\n  ([i]\n   (cbor/encode {:dao.stream.journal/header {:version 1 :identity i}})))\n\n\n(defn origin\n  [o l]\n  {:yin.k/occurrence o :dao.lease/lease l :yin.k/emitter \"holder-a\"})\n\n\n(defn park\n  \"A blocked root of occurrence `o` with counter `n` and origin `org`,\n   nil for a first park.\"\n  ([o n] (park o n nil))\n  ([o n org]\n   (cond-> (assoc (get fx/fixtures \"first-park\")\n                  :yin.k/occurrence o\n                  :yin.k/next-op-seq n\n                  :yin.k/arbitration {:dao.stream/identity arb\n                                      :dao.stream/descriptor\n                                      {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/journal}})\n     (some? org) (assoc :yin.k/origin org))))\n\n\n(defn halted\n  \"A halted result of occurrence `o` under lease `l`.\"\n  [o l]\n  (assoc (get fx/fixtures \"halted-root\") :yin.k/origin (origin o l)))\n\n\n(defn world\n  \"A fresh world: the authority's frames (an atom), its content store and\n   a diagnostic stream.\"\n  []\n  {:frames (atom [(header-frame)])\n   :store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   :diag (:dao.stream/handle\n           (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n                                ringbuffer/capacity-key 64}))})\n\n\n(defn offer!\n  [{:keys [a store]} b]\n  (let [bs (cbor/encode b)]\n    (grant/offer! a store (fx/segment-address bs) bs \"carrier\")))\n\n\n(defn grant!\n  [{:keys [a]} o l h]\n  (stream/append! (grant/writer a)\n                  (lease/grant l (custody/subject o) h duration\n                               {:dao.lease/proposal (str \"p-\" l)})))\n\n\n(defn lapse!\n  [{:keys [a]} l cause]\n  (stream/append! (grant/writer a) (lease/lapsed l cause)))\n\n\n(defn refuse!\n  \"The hook's refusal of `proposer`'s proposal pid, through the writer.\"\n  [{:keys [a]} proposer pid]\n  (stream/append! (grant/writer a)\n                  (assoc (lease/refusal pid) :yin.k/proposer proposer)))\n\n\n(defn report!\n  \"holder-a reports body `b` as o's successor under l.\"\n  [{:keys [a]} o l b]\n  (let [bs (cbor/encode b)]\n    (completion/report! a \"holder-a\"\n                        (completion/resumed o l (fx/segment-address bs))\n                        bs)))\n\n\n(defn envelope\n  [l e o n v]\n  {:yin.k/envelope :yin.k/fenced-v1\n   :yin.k/incarnation l\n   :yin.k/epoch e\n   :yin.k/op-id {:yin.k/occurrence o :yin.k/seq n}\n   :yin.k/value v})\n\n\n(defn admit!\n  [{:keys [a store i diag]} l e o n v]\n  (admission/admit! a store i \"holder-a\" (envelope l e o n v) diag))\n\n\n(defn record!\n  [{:keys [a]} o l e k observed]\n  (input/record-input! a \"holder-a\"\n                       (input/request o l e k\n                                      {:yin.k/kind :yin.k/read :yin.k/name \"s\"}\n                                      observed)))\n\n\n(defn read-ok\n  [v pos]\n  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   :dao.stream/value v\n   :dao.stream/cursor {:position pos}})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The script\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn answer\n  \"One request's answer as a status keyword.\"\n  [rep]\n  (or (:yin.k/status rep) (:yin.k/admission rep) (:dao.stream/outcome rep)))\n\n\n(def script-answers\n  \"The answer each step of `build` gives, in order.\"\n  [:committed                           ; enroll target i\n   :committed                           ; offer r\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-1 on r\n   :recorded                            ; input 0 of r\n   :committed                           ; admit (r 0)\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; refuse holder-b's p-b\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; reclaim lease-1, epoch 1\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-2 on r\n   :committed                           ; report s1\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; release lease-2: r completes\n   :committed                           ; offer s1\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-3 on s1\n   :committed                           ; report a halted result\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; release lease-3: s1 terminates\n   :committed                           ; offer x\n   :dao.stream/ok                       ; grant lease-4 on x\n   :committed                           ; admit (x 0) :v\n   :intent-conflict                     ; admit (x 0) :w: x quarantined\n   :committed])                         ; close target i\n\n\n(defn build\n  \"Run the script on a fresh memory-backed authority.  Answers the world\n   with `:answers`, one per step, and the authority, left open.\"\n  []\n  (let [w0 (world)\n        a (::authority/authority\n            (authority/open! (journal/memory-backend (:frames w0) nil)))\n        enrolled (authority/enroll! a)\n        w (assoc w0 :a a :i (:yin.k/target enrolled))\n        steps [#(offer! w (park r 0))\n               #(grant! w r \"lease-1\" \"holder-a\")\n               #(record! w r \"lease-1\" 0 0 (read-ok 7 1))\n               #(admit! w \"lease-1\" 0 r 0 :v)\n               #(refuse! w \"holder-b\" \"p-b\")\n               #(lapse! w \"lease-1\" :policy)\n               #(grant! w r \"lease-2\" \"holder-a\")\n               #(report! w r \"lease-2\" (park s1 3 (origin r \"lease-2\")))\n               #(lapse! w \"lease-2\" :release)\n               #(offer! w (park s1 3 (origin r \"lease-2\")))\n               #(grant! w s1 \"lease-3\" \"holder-a\")\n               #(report! w s1 \"lease-3\" (halted s1 \"lease-3\"))\n               #(lapse! w \"lease-3\" :release)\n               #(offer! w (park x 0))\n               #(grant! w x \"lease-4\" \"holder-a\")\n               #(admit! w \"lease-4\" 0 x 0 :v)\n               #(admit! w \"lease-4\" 0 x 0 :w)\n               #(authority/close-target! a (:i w))]]\n    (assoc w :answers (into [(answer enrolled)] (map #(answer (%))) steps))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Rendering and reading\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn digest\n  \"The BLAKE3 hex of the canonical bytes of projection `p`.\"\n  [p]\n  (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 (cbor/encode p)))\n\n\n(defn hex\n  [bs]\n  (cfx/bytes->hex bs))\n\n\n(defn render\n  \"The fixture file's text, computed from `build` on this host.\"\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [a frames]} (build)]\n    (str \"ledger-v1\\n\"\n         \"projection \" (digest (authority/projection a)) \"\\n\"\n         (str/join (map #(str (hex %) \"\\n\") @frames)))))\n\n\n(defn read-file\n  \"The fixture file as `{:digest d :frames [bytes ...]}`.\"\n  []\n  (let [[magic pin & frames] (remove str/blank?\n                                     (str/split-lines (cfx/read-path path)))]\n    (when-not (= \"ledger-v1\" magic)\n      (throw (ex-info \"not a ledger-v1 fixture\" {:path path})))\n    {:digest (subs pin (count \"projection \"))\n     :frames (mapv cfx/hex->bytes frames)}))\n\n\n(defn read-text\n  \"The fixture file's text.\"\n  []\n  (cfx/read-path path))\n","numLines":263,"startLine":1,"totalLines":263}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012JGRydZsQDejh92U5sqCrC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
