{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F2afjD3Rjuhyhc7i5Ed4wn","type":"tool_result","content":"1315\t;; =============================================================================\n1316\t;; Export (14.1.2 lift): the whole blocked task as canonical bytes\n1317\t;; =============================================================================\n1318\t\n1319\t(defn- module-decls\n1320\t  \"The module declarations the completion walk asks for: each linked\n1321\t   module of the registry under its manifest address.\"\n1322\t  [vm]\n1323\t  (into {}\n1324\t        (map (fn [[m entry]]\n1325\t               [m {:yin.k/manifest (:address entry)}]))\n1326\t        (module/module-entries (:modules vm))))\n1327\t\n1328\t\n1329\t(defn- export-refusals\n1330\t  \"The completion walk's refusals as one data outcome.\"\n1331\t  [refusals]\n1332\t  (when-some [r (first refusals)]\n1333\t    (refuse! (if (= :yin.k/not-quiescent (:kind r))\n1334\t               :yin.k/not-quiescent\n1335\t               :yin.k/non-portable)\n1336\t             (assoc (dissoc r :kind) :yin.k/kind (:kind r)))))\n1337\t\n1338\t\n1339\t(defn- snapshot-module-stores\n1340\t  \"The encoded store snapshot of every module the encoding reached,\n1341\t   exactly as it stands in the task at export, mutations included,\n1342\t   walked in the same canonical order the task store is. Version 1's\n1343\t   fixed point corrects omitted transitive stores; canonical-order's\n1344\t   scratch census never populated this export's found map. Published\n1345\t   version 0 retains its one-pass bytes; only recovery closes its graph.\"\n1346\t  [vm encode found]\n1347\t  (when-some [m (first (remove #(contains? (:module-stores vm) %)\n1348\t                               (sort-by str (:stores @found))))]\n1349\t    (non-portable! :missing-module-store {engine/store-of-key m}))\n1350\t  (let [snapshot (fn [module-id]\n1351\t                   (when-not (contains? (:module-stores vm) module-id)\n1352\t                     (non-portable! :missing-module-store {engine/store-of-key module-id}))\n1353\t                   (into {}\n1354\t                         (map (fn [[key value]] [(encode key) (encode value)]))\n1355\t                         (ordered found key (get (:module-stores vm) module-id))))]\n1356\t    (if (or (:jing-codec @found) (:full-census @found))\n1357\t      (loop [stores {}]\n1358\t        (if-some [module-id (first (sort-by str (set/difference (:stores @found)\n1359\t                                                                (set (keys stores)))))]\n1360\t          (recur (assoc stores module-id (snapshot module-id)))\n1361\t          stores))\n1362\t      (into {} (map (fn [module-id] [module-id (snapshot module-id)]))\n1363\t            (sort-by str (:stores @found))))))\n1364\t\n1365\t\n1366\t(defn- bytes-address\n1367\t  \"The jing segment address of the exact emitted `bytes`, the scheme a\n1368\t   receiver verifies fetched bytes against (`jing/segment-bytes-match?`).\"\n1369\t  [bytes]\n1370\t  (let [algo jing/default-hash-algorithm]\n1371\t    (keyword \"segment\"\n1372\t             (str (get-in jing/registry [algo :address-id]) \"-\"\n1373\t                  (jing/digest-bytes algo bytes)))))\n1374\t\n1375\t\n1376\t(defn- header-of\n1377\t  \"The custody header keys the root body of `kind` carries, from the\n1378\t   caller's `header`: a blocked or parked root takes the occurrence,\n1379\t   arbitration, counter and the exclusive policy, and the origin when\n1380\t   the header names one; a halted root takes the origin alone, its other\n1381\t   values ignored.  A nil value is an absent key.\"\n1382\t  [header kind]\n1383\t  (into {}\n1384\t        (filter (comp some? val))\n1385\t        (if (= :halted kind)\n1386\t          (select-keys header [:yin.k/origin])\n1387\t          (assoc (select-keys header [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration\n1388\t                                      :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin])\n1389\t                 :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive))))\n1390\t\n1391\t\n1392\t(defn export-task\n1393\t  \"The lift of 14.1.2: `vm`, a blocked or halted task at a safepoint,\n1394\t   as canonical bytes under their content address.  Answers\n1395\t   `{:status :ok :kind k :body b :bytes encoded :address a}` with `k`\n1396\t   `:blocked`, `:parked` or `:halted`, or the S7.9 data outcome of the\n1397\t   first refusal -- `:yin.k/not-quiescent` for queued work,\n1398\t   `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` for an undeclared pc, `:yin.k/non-portable`\n1399\t   for a value or reference that cannot cross, `:yin.k/unsatisfied`\n1400\t   for a stream that cannot be served, a cursor that cannot survive\n1401\t   the canonical codec, or -- when `opts` names cursor profiles that\n1402\t   do not cover the cells -- a claim the body cannot make.\n1403\t   `serve!` is the exporter's remote-table entry, exactly\n1404\t   `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s.  A task that holds an `:observe` entry, an\n1405\t   entry or cell carrying `:yin.k/held`, an unminted cursor cell, a\n1406\t   pending close, or a cursorless `:link-request` entry -- itself or any\n1407\t   install child -- refuses `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n1408\t   `:reason-mismatch` before anything is lifted, the same holds\n1409\t   `yin.vm.ucf.holder.export/enter` refuses (UCF 7.4.1, 7.4.3).\n1410\t\n1411\t   `opts` may name `:header`, the version-1 custody header\n1412\t   (`yin.vm.ucf.holder.export/prepare` validates its shape): occurrence,\n1413\t   arbitration, next-op-seq, origin when the task has a predecessor, and\n1414\t   `:yin.k/enrolled`, the set of enrolled stream identities, which is a\n1415\t   lift input and never travels.  No header is the version-0 fork lift,\n1416\t   byte for byte as before; a header is the version-1 exclusive lift in\n1417\t   `dao.jing.cbor`, with `:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive` added here.\n1418\t   The root carries the header by its kind (blocked or parked: all of\n1419\t   it; halted: the origin alone; an install child: none), refuses\n1420\t   `:op-seq-exhausted` at 2^52-1, `:unprotected-pending` and a stream\n1421\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` by the enrolled set, orders every map and set\n1422\t   by canonical key bytes, and before answering runs the version-1\n1423\t   inspector over its own bytes and address and then `validate-body`:\n1424\t   whatever either refuses is the lift's refusal, and nothing is\n1425\t   answered.  `:serve-keyed`, `(f [path resource-id] handle)`, replaces\n1426\t   `serve!` and retains each answer under the task path and the\n1427\t   resource id.\n1428\t\n1429\t   `:version 2` selects the version-2 body of the four execution\n1430\t   profiles (semantic, stack, register, walker), the profile being the\n1431\t   kernel's own: no header is the fork, a header the exclusive lift, and\n1432\t   the roles are structural (the v2 amendment, section 3).  The\n1433\t   composition chooses it; it is never inferred, and without it the lift\n1434\t   is exactly the version-0 or version-1 lift as before.\"\n1435\t  ([vm serve!]\n1436\t   (export-task vm serve! nil))\n1437\t  ([vm serve! opts]\n1438\t   (call!\n1439\t     (fn []\n1440\t       (when (seq (:ready-queue vm))\n1441\t         (refuse! :yin.k/not-quiescent\n1442\t                  {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue vm))}))\n1443\t       (when-some [h (unliftable-hold vm)]\n1444\t         (non-portable! :reason-mismatch h))\n1445\t       (let [header (:header opts)\n1446\t             child? (::child opts)\n1447\t             v2? (= 2 (:version opts))\n1448\t             engine (when v2? (engine-of vm))\n1449\t             ;; `jing-codec?` names the jing wire and the exclusive-style\n1450\t             ;; lift, not \"version 1\": version 2 selects it too, and the\n1451\t             ;; version is dispatched separately, by `v2?` and the body's\n1452\t             ;; validated structural role (v2 amendment, section 10).\n1453\t             jing-codec? (boolean (or (some? header) (::jing-codec opts) v2?))\n1454\t             keyed (or (:serve-keyed opts) (fn [_ h] (serve! h)))\n1455\t             ;; grounded: ClojureDart compiles a many-key assoc onto nil\n1456\t             ;; as a conj, whose answer is a list no dissoc accepts\n1457\t             opts (assoc (or opts {})\n1458\t                         :path (or (:path opts) [])\n1459\t                         ::jing-codec jing-codec?\n1460\t                         ::enrolled (or (:yin.k/enrolled header)\n1461\t                                        (::enrolled opts)\n1462\t                                        #{})\n1463\t                         :serve-keyed keyed)\n1464\t             serve! (fn [id h] (keyed [(:path opts) id] h))\n1465\t             {:keys [encode-bytes decode-bytes]}\n1466\t             (if jing-codec?\n1467\t               {:encode-bytes jing.cbor/encode :decode-bytes jing.cbor/decode}\n1468\t               {:encode-bytes cbor/encode :decode-bytes cbor/decode})\n1469\t             walked (if (and v2? (not= :semantic engine))\n1470\t                      (census-v2 engine vm)\n1471\t                      (completion/complete\n1472\t                        {:vm vm\n1473\t                         :cursor-profile (constantly :dao.stream.remote/v1)\n1474\t                         :modules (module-decls vm)}))\n1475\t             _ (export-refusals (:yin.k/refusals walked))\n1476\t             ;; the pending-child gap the walk cannot close itself: an\n1477\t             ;; obligation a live install child will bind when it\n1478\t             ;; completes is discharged by the child this body carries\n1479\t             ;; beside the waiter, not by a store the emitter holds\n1480\t             installing (into #{}\n1481\t                              (mapcat (fn [[m inst]]\n1482\t                                        (map (fn [x]\n1483\t                                               (symbol (str (name m) \"/\"\n1484\t                                                            (name x))))\n1485\t                                             (get-in inst\n1486\t                                                     [:response :manifest\n1487\t                                                      :yin.module/exports])))\n1488\t                                      (:installs vm)))\n1489\t             missing (update (:yin.k/missing walked) :obligations\n1490\t                             #(set/difference (set %) installing))\n1491\t             discovery (cond\n1492\t                         (seq (:segments missing)) :blocked\n1493\t                         (some seq (vals (dissoc missing :segments)))\n1494\t                         :incomplete\n1495\t                         :else :complete)]\n1496\t         (when-not (= :complete discovery)\n1497\t           (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n1498\t                    {:yin.k/discovery discovery\n1499\t                     :yin.k/missing missing}))\n1500\t         (let [value (:value vm)\n1501\t               active (and (map? value)\n1502\t                           (= :parked-continuation (:type value))\n1503\t                           (contains? (:parked vm) (:id value)))\n1504\t               active-rec (when active (get (:parked vm) (:id value)))\n1505\t               kind (cond\n1506\t                      active :parked\n1507\t                      (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? vm) :halted\n1508\t                      (seq (:wait-set vm)) :blocked\n1509\t                      :else (not-at-safepoint!\n1510\t                              (get-in vm [:control :pc])))\n1511\t               _ (when (and (= :halted kind) (seq (:wait-set vm)))\n1512\t                   (non-portable! :inconsistent-halt {}))\n1513\t               _ (when (and jing-codec? (not child?) (not= :halted kind)\n1514\t                            (let [n (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)]\n1515\t                              (and (jing.cbor/numeric? n)\n1516\t                                   (jing.cbor/num= n checkpoint