{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AXtVTjESzL6KpAkTLLMQTD","type":"tool_result","content":"3249\t;; =============================================================================\n3250\t;; The version-aware reader (M-next D7): two codecs, one grammar each\n3251\t;; =============================================================================\n3252\t\n3253\t(def ^:private codec-versions\n3254\t  \"The body-version contract of each accepting codec, the two-codec\n3255\t   split of the D plan's residual 3: stage-1 `dao.stream.cbor` bytes are\n3256\t   version 0 only -- that wire is frozen -- and `dao.jing.cbor` canonical\n3257\t   bytes are version 1 only, the stream codec's tag-39 identifiers being\n3258\t   refused by jing's decoder.  Scalar overlap between the codecs\n3259\t   establishes no body compatibility; which codec accepted decides.\"\n3260\t  {:stream #{0} :jing #{1 2}})\n3261\t\n3262\t\n3263\t(defn- decode-two\n3264\t  \"Reader step 1: the version-1 decode first (jing), then the version-0\n3265\t   decode (the stream codec).  Answers `{:codec c :body b}` for the\n3266\t   first codec that accepted the bytes; bytes neither decodes are\n3267\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`.\"\n3268\t  [bytes]\n3269\t  (letfn [(attempt\n3270\t            [decode]\n3271\t            (try {:body (decode bytes)}\n3272\t                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n3273\t                   nil)))]\n3274\t    (or (when-some [r (attempt jing.cbor/decode)]\n3275\t          (assoc r :codec :jing))\n3276\t        (when-some [r (attempt cbor/decode)]\n3277\t          (assoc r :codec :stream))\n3278\t        (undecodable! {:yin.k/kind :bytes}))))\n3279\t\n3280\t\n3281\t(defn- require-tag!\n3282\t  \"Reader step 2: the S7.5.1 tag, before any version or address rule.\"\n3283\t  [body]\n3284\t  (when-not (and (map? body) (true? (get body handoff-tag)))\n3285\t    (undecodable! {:yin.k/kind :body})))\n3286\t\n3287\t\n3288\t(defn- version-gate!\n3289\t  \"Reader step 3, before the address check (UCF 7.2.1): the version\n3290\t   contract of the codec that accepted the bytes.  A version the codec\n3291\t   does not speak, an absent version, or one not of the integer kind is\n3292\t   `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, carrying the version as found and the\n3293\t   supported set.  Under `opts`' `:exclusive` a version-0 body is the\n3294\t   same refusal: a reader that requires exclusive custody never\n3295\t   downgrades a fork into it.\"\n3296\t  [codec body opts install-child?]\n3297\t  (let [supported (get codec-versions codec)\n3298\t        v (get body :yin.k/version)]\n3299\t    (when-not (and (jing.cbor/numeric? v)\n3300\t                   (= :integer (jing.cbor/numeric-kind v))\n3301\t                   (contains? supported v))\n3302\t      (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n3303\t               {:yin.k/version v :yin.k/supported supported}))\n3304\t    (when (and (:exclusive opts)\n3305\t               (if (v2-body? body)\n3306\t                 ;; version 2 is a fork exactly when it carries no custody\n3307\t                 ;; header key, and only a root is a custody subject\n3308\t                 (and (not install-child?)\n3309\t                      (not-any? #(contains? body %)\n3310\t                                [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence\n3311\t                                 :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/origin\n3312\t                                 :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\n3313\t                 (not= 1 v)))\n3314\t      (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n3315\t               {:yin.k/version v\n3316\t                :yin.k/supported #{1 2}\n3317\t                :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive}))))\n3318\t\n3319\t\n3320\t(defn- custody-inspect!\n3321\t  \"Reader step 4, version 1 only: `checkpoint/inspect` over the claimed\n3322\t   address and the exact bytes -- the address (`:yin.k/hash-mismatch`)\n3323\t   first, then the custody grammar, including an entry for every install\n3324\t   pending.  The address is the one `opts` names, the address the bytes\n3325\t   were fetched under; unnamed, it is the address of the bytes\n3326\t   themselves.  A structural failure here is never reinterpreted as\n3327\t   version 0: the accepting codec is already fixed.  Answers the\n3328\t   operation baseline D10's lower will consume.\"\n3329\t  [bytes opts]\n3330\t  (let [address (or (:address opts) (bytes-address bytes))\n3331\t        r (checkpoint/inspect address bytes)]\n3332\t    (when (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n3333\t      (refuse! (:yin.k/status r) (dissoc r :yin.k/status)))\n3334\t    r))\n3335\t\n3336\t\n3337\t(defn- task-bodies\n3338\t  [body]\n3339\t  (tree-seq #(seq (:yin.k/installs %))\n3340\t            #(map :yin.k/child (vals (:yin.k/installs %))) body))\n3341\t\n3342\t\n3343\t(defn- accept-grant!\n3344\t  [body opts]\n3345\t  (let [grant (:grant opts)\n3346\t        evidence (:evidence grant)]\n3347\t    (when-not (and (or (nil? grant) (map? grant))\n3348\t                   (or (nil? evidence) (map? evidence)))\n3349\t      (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower grant or evidence\" {})))\n3350\t    (when-not evidence\n3351\t      (refuse! :yin.k/awaiting-grant {}))\n3352\t    (when-not (= :yin.k/ready (:yin.k/status evidence))\n3353\t      (refuse! (if (= :yin.k/awaiting-grant (:yin.k/status evidence))\n3354\t                 :yin.k/awaiting-grant :yin.k/unsatisfied)\n3355\t               (dissoc evidence :yin.k/status)))\n3356\t    (let [binding (:yin.k/binding evidence)\n3357\t          prefix (:yin.k/prefix evidence)\n3358\t          tenure (:tenure grant)\n3359\t          occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence body)\n3360\t          lease (:dao.lease/lease grant)\n3361\t          holder (:dao.lease/holder grant)\n3362\t          frontier (:yin.k/frontier prefix)\n3363\t          records (:yin.k/inputs prefix)]\n3364\t      (when-not (and (map? binding) (map? tenure))\n3365\t        (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower binding or tenure\" {})))\n3366\t      (when (or (nil? prefix) (:yin.k/status prefix))\n3367\t        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n3368\t                 {:yin.k/reason (or (:yin.k/reason prefix) :unavailable)}))\n3369\t      (when-not (and (some? (:address opts))\n3370\t                     (= (:checkpoint grant) (:address opts))\n3371\t                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence binding))\n3372\t                     (some? lease) (= lease (:dao.lease/lease binding))\n3373\t                     (some? holder) (= holder (:dao.lease/holder binding))\n3374\t                     (= (get-in body [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity])\n3375\t                        (get-in binding [:yin.k/transaction :yin.k/arbitration]))\n3376\t                     (custody/exact? (:yin.k/epoch binding))\n3377\t                     (true? (:live tenure))\n3378\t                     (number? (:now tenure)) (number? (:bound tenure))\n3379\t                     (< (:now tenure) (:bound tenure))\n3380\t                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence prefix))\n3381\t                     (= lease (:dao.lease/lease prefix))\n3382\t                     (custody/exact? frontier) (vector? records)\n3383\t                     (= frontier (count records))\n3384\t                     (every? true? (map-indexed\n3385\t                                     (fn [index record]\n3386\t                                       (and (custody/exact? (:yin.k/input-seq record))\n3387\t                                            (= index (:yin.k/input-seq record))))\n3388\t                                     records)))\n3389\t        (refuse! :yin.k/not-holder {}))\n3390\t      (let [classes (:protection opts)\n3391\t            enrolled (:yin.k/enrolled evidence)]\n3392\t        (when-not (and (map? classes)\n3393\t                       (every? #{:enrolled :at-least-once :fail-stop} (vals classes))\n3394\t                       (set? enrolled))\n3395\t          (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower protection or enrollment\" {})))\n3396\t        (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n3397\t                marker (body-markers task)]\n3398\t          (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity marker)\n3399\t                class (get classes identity)]\n3400\t            (when-not (and class (= (= class :enrolled)\n3401\t                                    (contains? enrolled identity)))\n3402\t              (unsatisfied! identity))))\n3403\t        (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n3404\t                frame (:yin.k/frames task)\n3405\t                :let [pending (:yin.k/pending frame)\n3406\t                      reason (:yin.k/reason pending)]\n3407\t                :when (contains? #{:put :ffi-request :link-request} reason)]\n3408\t          (let [marker (if (= :put reason) (:yin.k/stream pending)\n3409\t                           (:yin.k/request pending))\n3410\t                identity (:dao.stream/identity marker)]\n3411\t            (when-not (= (= :enrolled (get classes identity))\n3412\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op-id))\n3413\t              (unsatisfied! identity))))\n3414\t        {:yin.k/occurrence occurrence\n3415\t         :dao.lease/lease lease :dao.lease/holder holder\n3416\t         :yin.k/epoch (:yin.k/epoch binding)\n3417\t         :yin.k/arbitration (:yin.k/arbitration body)\n3418\t         :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq body)\n3419\t         :protection classes :input {:next 0 :prefix prefix}\n3420\t         :tenure {:bound (:bound tenure)}}))))\n3421\t\n3422\t\n3423\t(defn- isolated-receiver\n3424\t  [recv]\n3425\t  (reduce (fn [machine [module-name entry]]\n3426\t            (update machine :modules module/assoc-module module-name\n3427\t                    entry))\n3428\t          (-> recv\n3429\t              (assoc :store {} :module-stores {} :parked {} :installs {})\n3430\t              (assoc-in [:modules :modules] {})\n3431\t              (dissoc :yin.k/custody :yin.k/gate :yin.k/closes :yin.k/issued\n3432\t                      :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids :yin.k/recovery-waits))\n3433\t          (filter (fn [[_ entry]] (nil? (:address entry)))\n3434\t                  (module/module-entries (:modules recv)))))\n3435\t\n3436\t\n3437\t(defn- primitives-satisfied!\n3438\t  \"Every primitive any task of the tree names exists in `recv`'s own\n3439\t   registry under an equal profile, or the lower is `:yin.k/unsatisfied`\n3440\t   naming it: judged on the bytes' markers before one attachment is made,\n3441\t   never found missing at decode time.\"\n3442\t  [recv body]\n3443\t  (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n3444\t          root (reachable-values task)\n3445\t          marker (tagged-of :yin.k/primitive root)]\n3446\t    (let [n (:yin.k/name marker)\n3447\t          entry (get (:primitives recv) n)]\n3448\t      (when-not (and (some? entry)\n3449\t                     (= (:yin.k/profile marker)\n3450\t                        (:yin.k/profile (vm/profile-of (:primitives recv) n))))\n3451\t        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/name n})))))\n3452\t\n3453\t\n3454\t(defn- resume-task*\n3455\t  \"The lower of 14.1.2 behind the version-aware reader of M-next D7:\n3456\t   `bytes`, a handoff body this namespace minted, resumed into a fresh\n3457\t   task over `recv` -- a machine of the receiver's own composition.\n3458\t   Before any attachment or restoration, in this order: the two-codec\n3459\t   decode (jing first, then the stream codec; neither accepting is\n3460\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`), the tag, the version gate of the accepting\n3461\t   codec (`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, before the address check), and --\n3462\t   version 1 only -- `checkpoint/inspect` over the address `opts` names\n3463\t   (`:yin.k/hash-mismatch`, then the custody grammar); then the full\n3464\t   recursive grammar of `validate-body`, the contract stamp and the\n3465\t   restoration itself.  `opts` may name `:exclusive` (a version-0 body\n3466\t   is then refused; without it such a body still lowers as a fork) and\n3467\t   `:address`. A blocked or parked version-1 root additionally requires\n3468\t   `:grant` (checkpoint, lease, holder, evidence and current tenure) and\n3469\t   `:protection` keyed by portable stream identity. Grant consistency and\n3470\t   recursive protection checks precede all attachments. Missing evidence\n3471\t   answers `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`, invalid binding `:yin.k/not-holder`,\n3472\t   and unavailable evidence or protection mismatch `:yin.k/unsatisfied`.\n3473\t   Accepted custody restores the body's operation counter exactly and\n3474\t   starts input replay at zero. Halted version-1 results need no grant\n3475\t   and are gated ended. Install children are resumed as children, their pass\n3476\t   skipping the custody step their root already ran.  Answers\n3477\t   `{:status :ok :kind k :vm resumed}` or the first data refusal:\n3478\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` bytes or grammar, `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`\n3479\t   stamp or version, `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` address or code,\n3480\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` a stream that cannot be attached or a primitive\n3481\t   the receiver cannot answer.  Nothing partially runnable is ever\n3482\t   exposed: the machine value is assembled only after every restoration\n3483\t   step passes.  `attach!` is the receiver's own `:dao.stream/attach`\n3484\t   dispatch, exactly `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s; a version-0 resume is a\n3485\t   fork.\"\n3486\t  ([recv bytes attach!]\n3487\t   (resume-task recv bytes attach! nil))\n3488\t  ([recv bytes attach! opts install-child?]\n3489\t   (resume-task* recv bytes attach! opts install-child? false))\n3490\t  ([recv bytes attach! opts install-child? fenced?]\n3491\t   (call!\n3492\t     (fn []\n3493\t       (let [{:keys [codec body]} (decode-two bytes)\n3494\t             _ (require-tag! body)\n3495\t             _ (version-gate! codec body opts install-child?)\n3496\t             v2? (v2-body? body)\n3497\t             _ (when (and (or v2? (= 1 (:yin.k/version body)))\n3498\t                          (not install-child?))\n3499\t                 (custody-inspect! bytes opts))\n3500\t             _ (validate-body body)\n3501\t             engine (when v2? (ucf/profile-engine (:yin.k/contract body)))\n3502\t             _ (if v2?\n3503\t                 (when-not (= engine (engine-of recv))\n3504\t                   (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n3505\t                            {:yin.k/contract (:yin.k/contract body)\n3506\t                             :yin.k/supported ucf/supported-profiles}))\n3507\t                 (when-not (= ucf/contract-stamp\n3508\t                              (:yin.k/contract body))\n3509\t                   (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n3510\t                            {:yin.k/contract (:yin.k/contract body)})))\n3511\t             _ (when v2?\n3512\t                 (primitives-satisfied! recv body))\n3513\t             kind (:yin.k/kind body)\n3514\t             ;; a version-2 tree is a fork exactly when its root carries no\n3515\t             ;; custody header key; its children inherit the root's role\n3516\t             tree-fork? (if install-child?\n3517\t                          (boolean (::fork opts))\n3518\t                          (and v2? (not-any? #(contains? body %)\n3519\t                                             [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence\n3520\t                                              :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/origin\n3521\t                                              :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n3522\t             opts (assoc opts ::fork tree-fork?)\n3523\t             version-one? (or (= 1 (:yin.k/version body))\n3524\t                              (and v2? (not tree-fork?)))\n3525\t             custody-state (when (and version-one? (not install-child?) (not fenced?)\n3526\t                                      (not= :halted kind))\n3527\t                             (accept-grant! body opts))\n3528\t             cells (:yin.k/cells body)\n3529\t             pendings (mapv :yin.k/pending\n3530\t                            (or (:yin.k/frames body) []))\n3531\t             recv' (cond\n3532\t                     (= :walker engine)\n3533\t                     (walker/attach-rows\n3534\t                       (walker/clear-code (isolated-receiver recv))\n3535\t                       (:yin.k/code body)\n3536\t                       vm/ast-contract)\n3537\t                     (pc-profile? engine)\n3538\t                     ((if (= :stack engine) stack/rebuild register/rebuild)\n3539\t                      (isolated-receiver recv)\n3540\t                      (mapv (:yin.k/code body) (:yin.k/layout body)))\n3541\t                     :else\n3542\t                     (reduce (fn [r [_a v]] (module/attach-module r v))\n3543\t                             (cond\n3544\t                               (= :semantic engine)\n3545\t                               ;; the receiver's own code layout is cleared\n3546\t                               ;; before the body's is rebuilt (v2, 9)\n3547\t                               (assoc (isolated-receiver recv)\n3548\t                                      :code {} :code-aliases {} :program nil)\n3549\t                               (or version-one? v2? fenced?)\n3550\t                               (isolated-receiver recv)\n3551\t                               :else recv)\n3552\t                             (:yin.k/code body)))\n3553\t             handles (attach-all! attach! (body-markers body))\n3554\t             used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys\n3555\t                              (keys (:resources recv))))\n3556\t             streams (into {}\n3557\t                           (map (fn [identity]\n3558\t                                  [identity (fresh-key used)]))\n3559\t                           (sort-by str (keys handles)))\n3560\t             resources (into {}\n3561\t                             (map (fn [[identity k]]\n3562\t                                    [k (get handles identity)]))\n3563\t                             streams)\n3564\t             cell-keys (into {}\n3565\t                             (map (fn [cid] [cid (fresh-key used)]))\n3566\t                             (sort-by str (keys cells)))\n3567\t             cell-resources (into {}\n3568\t                                  (map (fn [[cid k]]\n3569\t                                         [k\n3570\t                                          {:stream-id\n3571\t                                           (streams\n3572\t                                             (get-in cells\n3573\t                                                     [cid :yin.k/stream\n3574\t                                                      :dao.stream/identity]))\n3575\t                                           :cursor\n3576\t                                           (get-in cells\n3577\t                                                   [cid\n3578\t                                                    :yin.k/position])}]))\n3579\t                                  cell-keys)\n3580\t             frame-hooks (atom nil)\n3581\t             decode (value-decoder recv' streams cell-keys frame-hooks)\n3582\t             aliases (:code-aliases recv')\n3583\t             decode-regs (if v2?\n3584\t                           (partial decode-registers-v2 engine decode\n3585\t                                    {:aliases aliases\n3586\t                                     :code (:yin.k/code body)\n3587\t                                     :node-of (partial walker/row-node recv')})\n3588\t                           (partial decode-registers decode aliases))\n3589\t             parked-cache (atom {})\n3590\t             resolving (atom #{})\n3591\t             resolve-parked\n3592\t             (fn [pid]\n3593\t               (or (get @parked-cache pid)\n3594\t                   (do (when (contains? @resolving pid)\n3595\t                         (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable\n3596\t                                        {:yin.k/hint :parked-cycle}))\n3597\t                       (swap! resolving conj pid)\n3598\t                       (let [rec (assoc (decode-regs\n3599\t                                          (get-in body [:yin.k/parked pid]))\n3600\t                                        :type :parked-continuation\n3601\t                                        :id pid)]\n3602\t                         (swap! parked-cache assoc pid rec)\n3603\t                         (swap! resolving disj pid)\n3604\t                         rec))))\n3605\t             _ (when v2?\n3606\t                 (reset! frame-hooks {:parked resolve-parked\n3607\t                                      :reified decode-regs}))\n3608\t             ;; the isolated slice installs through `store-put`, so a\n3609\t             ;; reserved key inside a tampered body refuses here exactly\n3610\t             ;; as a program write would (Rule R), before the checked\n3611\t             ;; store lands on the receiver in one write\n3612\t             store (reduce (fn [s [k v]]\n3613\t                             (engine/store-put s (decode k) (decode v)))\n3614\t                           (or (:store recv') {})\n3615\t                           (:yin.k/store body))\n3616\t             module-stores (into {}\n3617\t                                 (map (fn [[m s]]\n3618\t                                        [m (into {}\n3619\t                                                 (map (fn [[k v]]\n3620\t                                                        [(decode k)\n3621\t                                                         (decode v)]))\n3622\t                                                 s)]))\n3623\t                                 (:yin.k/module-stores body))\n3624\t             parked (into {}\n3625\t                          (map (fn [[pid r]]\n3626\t                                 [pid (if v2?\n3627\t                                        (resolve-parked pid)\n3628\t                                        (assoc\n3629\t                                          (decode-registers decode aliases r)\n3630\t                                          :type :parked-continuation\n3631\t                                          :id pid))]))\n3632\t                          (:yin.k/parked body))\n3633\t             installs (resume-installs recv' body attach! opts fenced?)\n3634\t             registers (mapv (fn [frame]\n3635\t                               (decode-regs (:yin.k/registers frame)))\n3636\t                             (or (:yin.k/frames body) []))\n3637\t             raw-entries (mapv (fn [pending ctx]\n3638\t                                 (cond-> (lower-frame! engine decode streams cells cell-keys\n3639\t                                                       pending ctx)\n3640\t                                   (and version-one? (contains? pending :yin.k/op-id))\n3641\t                                   (assoc :op-id (:yin.k/op-id pending))))\n3642\t                               pendings registers)\n3643\t             [entries issued] (if version-one?\n3644\t                                (reduce (fn [[acc issue] entry]\n3645\t                                          (if (= :put (:reason entry))\n3646\t                                            [(conj acc (assoc entry :yin.k/issue issue)) (inc issue)]\n3647\t                                            [(conj acc entry) issue]))\n3648\t                                        [[] 0]\n3649\t                                        raw-entries)\n3650\t                                [raw-entries nil])\n3651\t             machine (cond-> (-> recv'\n3652\t                                 (assoc :store store\n3653\t                                        :module-stores (merge (:module-stores recv')\n3654\t                                                              module-stores)\n3655\t                                        :parked (merge (:parked recv') parked)\n3656\t                                        :installs (merge (:installs recv') installs)\n3657\t                                        :resources (merge (:resources recv')\n3658\t                                                          resources\n3659\t                                                          cell-resources\n3660\t                                                          (when (or fenced? (= :walker engine))\n3661\t                                                            (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n3662\t                                                                      (if (= :ffi-request (:yin.k/reason pending))\n3663\t                                                                        (assoc acc\n3664\t                                                                               vm/call-in-stream-key\n3665\t                                                                               (get resources (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request :dao.stream/identity])))\n3666\t                                                                               vm/call-out-stream-key\n3667\t                                                                               (get resources (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/response :dao.stream/identity])))\n3668\t                                                                               vm/call-out-cursor-key\n3669\t                                                                               (get cell-resources (cell-keys (:yin.k/response-cell pending))))\n3670\t                                                                        acc))\n3671\t                                                                    {} pendings))\n3672\t                                                          (link-pair-resources\n3673\t                                                            streams resources\n3674\t                                                            pendings))\n3675\t                                        :id-counter (max (or (:id-counter recv') 0)\n3676\t                                                         (or (:yin.k/id-counter body)\n3677\t                                                             0))\n3678\t                                        :ready-queue []\n3679\t                                        :control nil\n3680\t                                        :k nil))\n3681\t                       (pc-profile? engine)\n3682\t                       (assoc :free-env (decode-env-v2 decode (:yin.k/free-env body)))\n3683\t                       version-one?\n3684\t                       (assoc :yin.k/issued issued\n3685\t                              :yin.k/gate (if (and (not install-child?)\n3686\t                                                   (= :halted kind))\n3687\t                                            :ended :running))\n3688\t                       fenced? (assoc :yin.k/gate :exporting\n3689\t                                      :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids\n3690\t                                      (into (into {} (map (fn [[cell-id resource-id]]\n3691\t                                                            [resource-id cell-id])) cell-keys)\n3692\t                                            (keep (fn [pending]\n3693\t                                                    (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\n3694\t                                                                     (:yin.k/reason pending))\n3695\t                                                      [[module/link-response-resource\n3696\t                                                        (get-in cells [(:yin.k/cell pending) :yin.k/position])]\n3697\t                                                       (:yin.k/cell pending)])))\n3698\t                                            pendings)\n3699\t                                      :id-counter (or (:yin.k/id-counter body) 0))\n3700\t                       custody-state (assoc :yin.k/custody custody-state))]\n3701\t         (cond-> {:status :ok\n3702\t                  :kind kind\n3703\t                  :vm (case kind\n3704\t                        :halted\n3705\t                        (assoc machine\n3706\t                               :halted? true :blocked? false\n3707\t                               :value (decode (:yin.k/result body))\n3708\t                               :wait-set [])\n3709\t\n3710\t                        ;; the parked activation waits on nothing; every other\n3711\t                        ;; carried frame is still an ordered wait (UCF 7.4.3)\n3712\t                        :parked\n3713\t                        (assoc machine\n3714\t                               :halted? true :blocked? false\n3715\t                               :value (get parked (:yin.k/parked-id body))\n3716\t                               :wait-set entries)\n3717\t\n3718\t                        (assoc machine\n3719\t                               :halted? false :blocked? true\n3720\t                               :value :yin/blocked\n3721\t                               :wait-set entries))}\n3722\t           fenced? (update :vm (fn [restored]\n3723\t                                 (assoc restored\n3724\t                                        :yin.k/recovery-waits (:wait-set restored)\n3725\t                                        :wait-set [])))))))))\n3726\t\n3727\t\n3728\t(defn rehydrate-fenced-body\n3729\t  \"Administrative reconstruction of a validated handoff snapshot.\n3730\t   Unlike resume-task, never admits execution or restores custody. Root\n3731\t   and install children remain exporting with waits outside the scheduler.\"\n3732\t  [receiver bytes attach! address]\n3733\t  (resume-task* receiver bytes attach! {:address address} false true))\n3734\t\n3735\t\n3736\t(defn inspect-recovery-body\n3737\t  \"Validate an embedded export snapshot before administrative attachment.\"\n3738\t  ([bytes address header]\n3739\t   (inspect-recovery-body bytes address header true))\n3740\t  ([bytes address header complete?]\n3741\t   (call!\n3742\t     (fn []\n3743\t       (let [{:keys [codec body]} (decode-two bytes)]\n3744\t         (require-tag! body)\n3745\t         (version-gate! codec body nil false)\n3746\t         (when (or (v2-body? body) (= 1 (:yin.k/version body)))\n3747\t           (custody-inspect! bytes {:address address}))\n3748\t         (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes)\n3749\t           (refuse! :yin.k/hash-mismatch {}))\n3750\t         (validate-body body)\n3751\t         (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n3752\t                 root (reachable-values task)\n3753\t                 closure (tagged-of :yin.k/closure root)\n3754\t                 :let [store-of (:yin.k/store-of closure)]\n3755\t                 :when (and complete? (some? store-of))]\n3756\t           (when-not (contains? (:yin.k/module-stores task) store-of)\n3757\t             (non-portable! :missing-module-store {engine/store-of-key store-of})))\n3758\t         (when-not (and (if (v2-body? body)\n3759\t                          (some? (ucf/profile-engine (:yin.k/contract body)))\n3760\t                          (= ucf/contract-stamp (:yin.k/contract body)))\n3761\t                        (= (some? header)\n3762\t                           (if (v2-body? body)\n3763\t                             (boolean (some #(contains? body %)\n3764\t                                            [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence\n3765\t                                             :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/origin\n3766\t                                             :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\n3767\t                             (= 1 (:yin.k/version body))))\n3768\t                        (or (nil? header)\n3769\t                            (and (map? header) (set? (:yin.k/enrolled header))\n3770\t                                 (every? (fn [[key value]] (= value (get body key)))\n3771\t                                         (header-of header (:yin.k/kind body))))))\n3772\t           (undecodable! {:yin.k/reason :recovery-header}))\n3773\t         {:status :ok :body body\n3774\t          :descriptors (set (map :dao.stream/descriptor\n3775\t                                 (mapcat body-markers (task-bodies body))))})))))\n3776\t\n3777\t\n3778\t(defn resume-task\n3779\t  \"Public entry for 14.1.2 lower.\"\n3780\t  ([recv bytes attach!]\n3781\t   (resume-task recv bytes attach! nil))\n3782\t  ([recv bytes attach! opts]\n3783\t   (resume-task* recv bytes attach! (dissoc opts ::install-child) false)))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"555831a0-d9a6-4ffb-8df4-9c9fcaf278ef","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:32:32.972Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc","content":";; =============================================================================\n;; The version-aware reader (M-next D7): two codecs, one grammar each\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private codec-versions\n  \"The body-version contract of each accepting codec, the two-codec\n   split of the D plan's residual 3: stage-1 `dao.stream.cbor` bytes are\n   version 0 only -- that wire is frozen -- and `dao.jing.cbor` canonical\n   bytes are version 1 only, the stream codec's tag-39 identifiers being\n   refused by jing's decoder.  Scalar overlap between the codecs\n   establishes no body compatibility; which codec accepted decides.\"\n  {:stream #{0} :jing #{1 2}})\n\n\n(defn- decode-two\n  \"Reader step 1: the version-1 decode first (jing), then the version-0\n   decode (the stream codec).  Answers `{:codec c :body b}` for the\n   first codec that accepted the bytes; bytes neither decodes are\n   `:yin.k/undecodable`.\"\n  [bytes]\n  (letfn [(attempt\n            [decode]\n            (try {:body (decode bytes)}\n                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n                   nil)))]\n    (or (when-some [r (attempt jing.cbor/decode)]\n          (assoc r :codec :jing))\n        (when-some [r (attempt cbor/decode)]\n          (assoc r :codec :stream))\n        (undecodable! {:yin.k/kind :bytes}))))\n\n\n(defn- require-tag!\n  \"Reader step 2: the S7.5.1 tag, before any version or address rule.\"\n  [body]\n  (when-not (and (map? body) (true? (get body handoff-tag)))\n    (undecodable! {:yin.k/kind :body})))\n\n\n(defn- version-gate!\n  \"Reader step 3, before the address check (UCF 7.2.1): the version\n   contract of the codec that accepted the bytes.  A version the codec\n   does not speak, an absent version, or one not of the integer kind is\n   `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, carrying the version as found and the\n   supported set.  Under `opts`' `:exclusive` a version-0 body is the\n   same refusal: a reader that requires exclusive custody never\n   downgrades a fork into it.\"\n  [codec body opts install-child?]\n  (let [supported (get codec-versions codec)\n        v (get body :yin.k/version)]\n    (when-not (and (jing.cbor/numeric? v)\n                   (= :integer (jing.cbor/numeric-kind v))\n                   (contains? supported v))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n               {:yin.k/version v :yin.k/supported supported}))\n    (when (and (:exclusive opts)\n               (if (v2-body? body)\n                 ;; version 2 is a fork exactly when it carries no custody\n                 ;; header key, and only a root is a custody subject\n                 (and (not install-child?)\n                      (not-any? #(contains? body %)\n                                [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence\n                                 :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/origin\n                                 :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\n                 (not= 1 v)))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n               {:yin.k/version v\n                :yin.k/supported #{1 2}\n                :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive}))))\n\n\n(defn- custody-inspect!\n  \"Reader step 4, version 1 only: `checkpoint/inspect` over the claimed\n   address and the exact bytes -- the address (`:yin.k/hash-mismatch`)\n   first, then the custody grammar, including an entry for every install\n   pending.  The address is the one `opts` names, the address the bytes\n   were fetched under; unnamed, it is the address of the bytes\n   themselves.  A structural failure here is never reinterpreted as\n   version 0: the accepting codec is already fixed.  Answers the\n   operation baseline D10's lower will consume.\"\n  [bytes opts]\n  (let [address (or (:address opts) (bytes-address bytes))\n        r (checkpoint/inspect address bytes)]\n    (when (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n      (refuse! (:yin.k/status r) (dissoc r :yin.k/status)))\n    r))\n\n\n(defn- task-bodies\n  [body]\n  (tree-seq #(seq (:yin.k/installs %))\n            #(map :yin.k/child (vals (:yin.k/installs %))) body))\n\n\n(defn- accept-grant!\n  [body opts]\n  (let [grant (:grant opts)\n        evidence (:evidence grant)]\n    (when-not (and (or (nil? grant) (map? grant))\n                   (or (nil? evidence) (map? evidence)))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower grant or evidence\" {})))\n    (when-not evidence\n      (refuse! :yin.k/awaiting-grant {}))\n    (when-not (= :yin.k/ready (:yin.k/status evidence))\n      (refuse! (if (= :yin.k/awaiting-grant (:yin.k/status evidence))\n                 :yin.k/awaiting-grant :yin.k/unsatisfied)\n               (dissoc evidence :yin.k/status)))\n    (let [binding (:yin.k/binding evidence)\n          prefix (:yin.k/prefix evidence)\n          tenure (:tenure grant)\n          occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence body)\n          lease (:dao.lease/lease grant)\n          holder (:dao.lease/holder grant)\n          frontier (:yin.k/frontier prefix)\n          records (:yin.k/inputs prefix)]\n      (when-not (and (map? binding) (map? tenure))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower binding or tenure\" {})))\n      (when (or (nil? prefix) (:yin.k/status prefix))\n        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n                 {:yin.k/reason (or (:yin.k/reason prefix) :unavailable)}))\n      (when-not (and (some? (:address opts))\n                     (= (:checkpoint grant) (:address opts))\n                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence binding))\n                     (some? lease) (= lease (:dao.lease/lease binding))\n                     (some? holder) (= holder (:dao.lease/holder binding))\n                     (= (get-in body [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity])\n                        (get-in binding [:yin.k/transaction :yin.k/arbitration]))\n                     (custody/exact? (:yin.k/epoch binding))\n                     (true? (:live tenure))\n                     (number? (:now tenure)) (number? (:bound tenure))\n                     (< (:now tenure) (:bound tenure))\n                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence prefix))\n                     (= lease (:dao.lease/lease prefix))\n                     (custody/exact? frontier) (vector? records)\n                     (= frontier (count records))\n                     (every? true? (map-indexed\n                                     (fn [index record]\n                                       (and (custody/exact? (:yin.k/input-seq record))\n                                            (= index (:yin.k/input-seq record))))\n                                     records)))\n        (refuse! :yin.k/not-holder {}))\n      (let [classes (:protection opts)\n            enrolled (:yin.k/enrolled evidence)]\n        (when-not (and (map? classes)\n                       (every? #{:enrolled :at-least-once :fail-stop} (vals classes))\n                       (set? enrolled))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower protection or enrollment\" {})))\n        (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n                marker (body-markers task)]\n          (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity marker)\n                class (get classes identity)]\n            (when-not (and class (= (= class :enrolled)\n                                    (contains? enrolled identity)))\n              (unsatisfied! identity))))\n        (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n                frame (:yin.k/frames task)\n                :let [pending (:yin.k/pending frame)\n                      reason (:yin.k/reason pending)]\n                :when (contains? #{:put :ffi-request :link-request} reason)]\n          (let [marker (if (= :put reason) (:yin.k/stream pending)\n                           (:yin.k/request pending))\n                identity (:dao.stream/identity marker)]\n            (when-not (= (= :enrolled (get classes identity))\n                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op-id))\n              (unsatisfied! identity))))\n        {:yin.k/occurrence occurrence\n         :dao.lease/lease lease :dao.lease/holder holder\n         :yin.k/epoch (:yin.k/epoch binding)\n         :yin.k/arbitration (:yin.k/arbitration body)\n         :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq body)\n         :protection classes :input {:next 0 :prefix prefix}\n         :tenure {:bound (:bound tenure)}}))))\n\n\n(defn- isolated-receiver\n  [recv]\n  (reduce (fn [machine [module-name entry]]\n            (update machine :modules module/assoc-module module-name\n                    entry))\n          (-> recv\n              (assoc :store {} :module-stores {} :parked {} :installs {})\n              (assoc-in [:modules :modules] {})\n              (dissoc :yin.k/custody :yin.k/gate :yin.k/closes :yin.k/issued\n                      :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids :yin.k/recovery-waits))\n          (filter (fn [[_ entry]] (nil? (:address entry)))\n                  (module/module-entries (:modules recv)))))\n\n\n(defn- primitives-satisfied!\n  \"Every primitive any task of the tree names exists in `recv`'s own\n   registry under an equal profile, or the lower is `:yin.k/unsatisfied`\n   naming it: judged on the bytes' markers before one attachment is made,\n   never found missing at decode time.\"\n  [recv body]\n  (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n          root (reachable-values task)\n          marker (tagged-of :yin.k/primitive root)]\n    (let [n (:yin.k/name marker)\n          entry (get (:primitives recv) n)]\n      (when-not (and (some? entry)\n                     (= (:yin.k/profile marker)\n                        (:yin.k/profile (vm/profile-of (:primitives recv) n))))\n        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/name n})))))\n\n\n(defn- resume-task*\n  \"The lower of 14.1.2 behind the version-aware reader of M-next D7:\n   `bytes`, a handoff body this namespace minted, resumed into a fresh\n   task over `recv` -- a machine of the receiver's own composition.\n   Before any attachment or restoration, in this order: the two-codec\n   decode (jing first, then the stream codec; neither accepting is\n   `:yin.k/undecodable`), the tag, the version gate of the accepting\n   codec (`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, before the address check), and --\n   version 1 only -- `checkpoint/inspect` over the address `opts` names\n   (`:yin.k/hash-mismatch`, then the custody grammar); then the full\n   recursive grammar of `validate-body`, the contract stamp and the\n   restoration itself.  `opts` may name `:exclusive` (a version-0 body\n   is then refused; without it such a body still lowers as a fork) and\n   `:address`. A blocked or parked version-1 root additionally requires\n   `:grant` (checkpoint, lease, holder, evidence and current tenure) and\n   `:protection` keyed by portable stream identity. Grant consistency and\n   recursive protection checks precede all attachments. Missing evidence\n   answers `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`, invalid binding `:yin.k/not-holder`,\n   and unavailable evidence or protection mismatch `:yin.k/unsatisfied`.\n   Accepted custody restores the body's operation counter exactly and\n   starts input replay at zero. Halted version-1 results need no grant\n   and are gated ended. Install children are resumed as children, their pass\n   skipping the custody step their root already ran.  Answers\n   `{:status :ok :kind k :vm resumed}` or the first data refusal:\n   `:yin.k/undecodable` bytes or grammar, `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`\n   stamp or version, `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` address or code,\n   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` a stream that cannot be attached or a primitive\n   the receiver cannot answer.  Nothing partially runnable is ever\n   exposed: the machine value is assembled only after every restoration\n   step passes.  `attach!` is the receiver's own `:dao.stream/attach`\n   dispatch, exactly `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s; a version-0 resume is a\n   fork.\"\n  ([recv bytes attach!]\n   (resume-task recv bytes attach! nil))\n  ([recv bytes attach! opts install-child?]\n   (resume-task* recv bytes attach! opts install-child? false))\n  ([recv bytes attach! opts install-child? fenced?]\n   (call!\n     (fn []\n       (let [{:keys [codec body]} (decode-two bytes)\n             _ (require-tag! body)\n             _ (version-gate! codec body opts install-child?)\n             v2? (v2-body? body)\n             _ (when (and (or v2? (= 1 (:yin.k/version body)))\n                          (not install-child?))\n                 (custody-inspect! bytes opts))\n             _ (validate-body body)\n             engine (when v2? (ucf/profile-engine (:yin.k/contract body)))\n             _ (if v2?\n                 (when-not (= engine (engine-of recv))\n                   (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n                            {:yin.k/contract (:yin.k/contract body)\n                             :yin.k/supported ucf/supported-profiles}))\n                 (when-not (= ucf/contract-stamp\n                              (:yin.k/contract body))\n                   (refuse! :yin.k/profile-mismatch\n                            {:yin.k/contract (:yin.k/contract body)})))\n             _ (when v2?\n                 (primitives-satisfied! recv body))\n             kind (:yin.k/kind body)\n             ;; a version-2 tree is a fork exactly when its root carries no\n             ;; custody header key; its children inherit the root's role\n             tree-fork? (if install-child?\n                          (boolean (::fork opts))\n                          (and v2? (not-any? #(contains? body %)\n                                             [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence\n                                              :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/origin\n                                              :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n             opts (assoc opts ::fork tree-fork?)\n             version-one? (or (= 1 (:yin.k/version body))\n                              (and v2? (not tree-fork?)))\n             custody-state (when (and version-one? (not install-child?) (not fenced?)\n                                      (not= :halted kind))\n                             (accept-grant! body opts))\n             cells (:yin.k/cells body)\n             pendings (mapv :yin.k/pending\n                            (or (:yin.k/frames body) []))\n             recv' (cond\n                     (= :walker engine)\n                     (walker/attach-rows\n                       (walker/clear-code (isolated-receiver recv))\n                       (:yin.k/code body)\n                       vm/ast-contract)\n                     (pc-profile? engine)\n                     ((if (= :stack engine) stack/rebuild register/rebuild)\n                      (isolated-receiver recv)\n                      (mapv (:yin.k/code body) (:yin.k/layout body)))\n                     :else\n                     (reduce (fn [r [_a v]] (module/attach-module r v))\n                             (cond\n                               (= :semantic engine)\n                               ;; the receiver's own code layout is cleared\n                               ;; before the body's is rebuilt (v2, 9)\n                               (assoc (isolated-receiver recv)\n                                      :code {} :code-aliases {} :program nil)\n                               (or version-one? v2? fenced?)\n                               (isolated-receiver recv)\n                               :else recv)\n                             (:yin.k/code body)))\n             handles (attach-all! attach! (body-markers body))\n             used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys\n                              (keys (:resources recv))))\n             streams (into {}\n                           (map (fn [identity]\n                                  [identity (fresh-key used)]))\n                           (sort-by str (keys handles)))\n             resources (into {}\n                             (map (fn [[identity k]]\n                                    [k (get handles identity)]))\n                             streams)\n             cell-keys (into {}\n                             (map (fn [cid] [cid (fresh-key used)]))\n                             (sort-by str (keys cells)))\n             cell-resources (into {}\n                                  (map (fn [[cid k]]\n                                         [k\n                                          {:stream-id\n                                           (streams\n                                             (get-in cells\n                                                     [cid :yin.k/stream\n                                                      :dao.stream/identity]))\n                                           :cursor\n                                           (get-in cells\n                                                   [cid\n                                                    :yin.k/position])}]))\n                                  cell-keys)\n             frame-hooks (atom nil)\n             decode (value-decoder recv' streams cell-keys frame-hooks)\n             aliases (:code-aliases recv')\n             decode-regs (if v2?\n                           (partial decode-registers-v2 engine decode\n                                    {:aliases aliases\n                                     :code (:yin.k/code body)\n                                     :node-of (partial walker/row-node recv')})\n                           (partial decode-registers decode aliases))\n             parked-cache (atom {})\n             resolving (atom #{})\n             resolve-parked\n             (fn [pid]\n               (or (get @parked-cache pid)\n                   (do (when (contains? @resolving pid)\n                         (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable\n                                        {:yin.k/hint :parked-cycle}))\n                       (swap! resolving conj pid)\n                       (let [rec (assoc (decode-regs\n                                          (get-in body [:yin.k/parked pid]))\n                                        :type :parked-continuation\n                                        :id pid)]\n                         (swap! parked-cache assoc pid rec)\n                         (swap! resolving disj pid)\n                         rec))))\n             _ (when v2?\n                 (reset! frame-hooks {:parked resolve-parked\n                                      :reified decode-regs}))\n             ;; the isolated slice installs through `store-put`, so a\n             ;; reserved key inside a tampered body refuses here exactly\n             ;; as a program write would (Rule R), before the checked\n             ;; store lands on the receiver in one write\n             store (reduce (fn [s [k v]]\n                             (engine/store-put s (decode k) (decode v)))\n                           (or (:store recv') {})\n                           (:yin.k/store body))\n             module-stores (into {}\n                                 (map (fn [[m s]]\n                                        [m (into {}\n                                                 (map (fn [[k v]]\n                                                        [(decode k)\n                                                         (decode v)]))\n                                                 s)]))\n                                 (:yin.k/module-stores body))\n             parked (into {}\n                          (map (fn [[pid r]]\n                                 [pid (if v2?\n                                        (resolve-parked pid)\n                                        (assoc\n                                          (decode-registers decode aliases r)\n                                          :type :parked-continuation\n                                          :id pid))]))\n                          (:yin.k/parked body))\n             installs (resume-installs recv' body attach! opts fenced?)\n             registers (mapv (fn [frame]\n                               (decode-regs (:yin.k/registers frame)))\n                             (or (:yin.k/frames body) []))\n             raw-entries (mapv (fn [pending ctx]\n                                 (cond-> (lower-frame! engine decode streams cells cell-keys\n                                                       pending ctx)\n                                   (and version-one? (contains? pending :yin.k/op-id))\n                                   (assoc :op-id (:yin.k/op-id pending))))\n                               pendings registers)\n             [entries issued] (if version-one?\n                                (reduce (fn [[acc issue] entry]\n                                          (if (= :put (:reason entry))\n                                            [(conj acc (assoc entry :yin.k/issue issue)) (inc issue)]\n                                            [(conj acc entry) issue]))\n                                        [[] 0]\n                                        raw-entries)\n                                [raw-entries nil])\n             machine (cond-> (-> recv'\n                                 (assoc :store store\n                                        :module-stores (merge (:module-stores recv')\n                                                              module-stores)\n                                        :parked (merge (:parked recv') parked)\n                                        :installs (merge (:installs recv') installs)\n                                        :resources (merge (:resources recv')\n                                                          resources\n                                                          cell-resources\n                                                          (when (or fenced? (= :walker engine))\n                                                            (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n                                                                      (if (= :ffi-request (:yin.k/reason pending))\n                                                                        (assoc acc\n                                                                               vm/call-in-stream-key\n                                                                               (get resources (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request :dao.stream/identity])))\n                                                                               vm/call-out-stream-key\n                                                                               (get resources (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/response :dao.stream/identity])))\n                                                                               vm/call-out-cursor-key\n                                                                               (get cell-resources (cell-keys (:yin.k/response-cell pending))))\n                                                                        acc))\n                                                                    {} pendings))\n                                                          (link-pair-resources\n                                                            streams resources\n                                                            pendings))\n                                        :id-counter (max (or (:id-counter recv') 0)\n                                                         (or (:yin.k/id-counter body)\n                                                             0))\n                                        :ready-queue []\n                                        :control nil\n                                        :k nil))\n                       (pc-profile? engine)\n                       (assoc :free-env (decode-env-v2 decode (:yin.k/free-env body)))\n                       version-one?\n                       (assoc :yin.k/issued issued\n                              :yin.k/gate (if (and (not install-child?)\n                                                   (= :halted kind))\n                                            :ended :running))\n                       fenced? (assoc :yin.k/gate :exporting\n                                      :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids\n                                      (into (into {} (map (fn [[cell-id resource-id]]\n                                                            [resource-id cell-id])) cell-keys)\n                                            (keep (fn [pending]\n                                                    (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\n                                                                     (:yin.k/reason pending))\n                                                      [[module/link-response-resource\n                                                        (get-in cells [(:yin.k/cell pending) :yin.k/position])]\n                                                       (:yin.k/cell pending)])))\n                                            pendings)\n                                      :id-counter (or (:yin.k/id-counter body) 0))\n                       custody-state (assoc :yin.k/custody custody-state))]\n         (cond-> {:status :ok\n                  :kind kind\n                  :vm (case kind\n                        :halted\n                        (assoc machine\n                               :halted? true :blocked? false\n                               :value (decode (:yin.k/result body))\n                               :wait-set [])\n\n                        ;; the parked activation waits on nothing; every other\n                        ;; carried frame is still an ordered wait (UCF 7.4.3)\n                        :parked\n                        (assoc machine\n                               :halted? true :blocked? false\n                               :value (get parked (:yin.k/parked-id body))\n                               :wait-set entries)\n\n                        (assoc machine\n                               :halted? false :blocked? true\n                               :value :yin/blocked\n                               :wait-set entries))}\n           fenced? (update :vm (fn [restored]\n                                 (assoc restored\n                                        :yin.k/recovery-waits (:wait-set restored)\n                                        :wait-set [])))))))))\n\n\n(defn rehydrate-fenced-body\n  \"Administrative reconstruction of a validated handoff snapshot.\n   Unlike resume-task, never admits execution or restores custody. Root\n   and install children remain exporting with waits outside the scheduler.\"\n  [receiver bytes attach! address]\n  (resume-task* receiver bytes attach! {:address address} false true))\n\n\n(defn inspect-recovery-body\n  \"Validate an embedded export snapshot before administrative attachment.\"\n  ([bytes address header]\n   (inspect-recovery-body bytes address header true))\n  ([bytes address header complete?]\n   (call!\n     (fn []\n       (let [{:keys [codec body]} (decode-two bytes)]\n         (require-tag! body)\n         (version-gate! codec body nil false)\n         (when (or (v2-body? body) (= 1 (:yin.k/version body)))\n           (custody-inspect! bytes {:address address}))\n         (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes)\n           (refuse! :yin.k/hash-mismatch {}))\n         (validate-body body)\n         (doseq [task (task-bodies body)\n                 root (reachable-values task)\n                 closure (tagged-of :yin.k/closure root)\n                 :let [store-of (:yin.k/store-of closure)]\n                 :when (and complete? (some? store-of))]\n           (when-not (contains? (:yin.k/module-stores task) store-of)\n             (non-portable! :missing-module-store {engine/store-of-key store-of})))\n         (when-not (and (if (v2-body? body)\n                          (some? (ucf/profile-engine (:yin.k/contract body)))\n                          (= ucf/contract-stamp (:yin.k/contract body)))\n                        (= (some? header)\n                           (if (v2-body? body)\n                             (boolean (some #(contains? body %)\n                                            [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence\n                                             :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/origin\n                                             :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\n                             (= 1 (:yin.k/version body))))\n                        (or (nil? header)\n                            (and (map? header) (set? (:yin.k/enrolled header))\n                                 (every? (fn [[key value]] (= value (get body key)))\n                                         (header-of header (:yin.k/kind body))))))\n           (undecodable! {:yin.k/reason :recovery-header}))\n         {:status :ok :body body\n          :descriptors (set (map :dao.stream/descriptor\n                                 (mapcat body-markers (task-bodies body))))})))))\n\n\n(defn resume-task\n  \"Public entry for 14.1.2 lower.\"\n  ([recv bytes attach!]\n   (resume-task recv bytes attach! nil))\n  ([recv bytes attach! opts]\n   (resume-task* recv bytes attach! (dissoc opts ::install-child) false)))","