{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LbuGEZWJned7Ydw3svrKdy","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t\n151\t\n152\t;; =============================================================================\n153\t;; Inherited ids (slice C9)\n154\t;; =============================================================================\n155\t\n156\t(defn- predecessor\n157\t  \"The occurrence whose completion edge goes to occurrence `s`, or nil.\n158\t   A terminal edge names a result, not a successor, so it is no one's\n159\t   predecessor.\"\n160\t  [p s]\n161\t  (some (fn [[o occ]]\n162\t          (when (= s (get-in occ [:yin.k/closed :yin.k/successor])) o))\n163\t        (:occurrences p)))\n164\t\n165\t\n166\t(defn ancestor?\n167\t  \"True when occurrence `a` is an ancestor of occurrence `o` through the\n168\t   completion edges of projection p: the predecessor of o, or one of its\n169\t   ancestors.  No ancestry runs through a terminal edge or an orphan,\n170\t   and no occurrence is its own ancestor.  Derived, nothing indexed: each\n171\t   step back scans the occurrences, so a check costs O(chain length x\n172\t   occurrences) plus one content-store read per inherited admission, all\n173\t   under the authority lock (a C12 cost note).\"\n174\t  [p a o]\n175\t  ;; the fold keeps the chain acyclic; the count only bounds the walk\n176\t  (loop [s o n (count (:occurrences p))]\n177\t    (let [x (predecessor p s)]\n178\t      (cond\n179\t        (nil? x) false\n180\t        (= a x) true\n181\t        (zero? n) false\n182\t        :else (recur x (dec n))))))\n183\t\n184\t\n185\t(defn member?\n186\t  \"True when op id `op` is carried in operation baseline `b`\n187\t   (yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint): by the root or any install child.  Ids\n188\t   compare by canonical content.\"\n189\t  [b op]\n190\t  (let [k (cbor/content-key op)]\n191\t    (boolean (some #(= k (cbor/content-key %)) (keys (:yin.k/ops b))))))\n192\t\n193\t\n194\t(defn- accepted-baseline\n195\t  \"The baseline of occurrence o's accepted checkpoint, read from content\n196\t   store `store` and verified: the first variant, in a fixed address\n197\t   order, whose bytes the store yields and the inspector turns into the\n198\t   recorded baseline.  The offered variants share one baseline (C5), so\n199\t   which one verifies cannot change the answer.  Nil when none does.\"\n200\t  [p store o]\n201\t  (let [{b :yin.k/baseline vs :yin.k/variants} (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n202\t        read (fn [address]\n203\t               (try\n204\t                 ((:get-bytes-fn store) address nil)\n205\t                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n206\t                   nil)))]\n207\t    (some (fn [address]\n208\t            (let [bs (read address)]\n209\t              (when (and (some? bs) (= b (checkpoint/inspect address bs)))\n210\t                b)))\n211\t          (sort-by str vs))))\n212\t\n213\t\n214\t(defn- scope\n215\t  \"Nil when op id `op` is in the scope of occurrence o, else\n216\t   :foreign-op-id, or :unreadable when o's accepted checkpoint cannot be\n217\t   read from `store` and verified.  Ancestry, read from p alone, comes\n218\t   first: no checkpoint makes a non-ancestor's id admissible.\"\n219\t  [p store o op]\n220\t  (let [a (:yin.k/occurrence op)]\n221\t    (cond\n222\t      (= o a) nil\n223\t      (not (ancestor? p a o)) :foreign-op-id\n224\t      :else (if-let [b (accepted-baseline p store o)]\n225\t              (when-not (member? b op) :foreign-op-id)\n226\t              :unreadable))))\n227\t\n228\t\n229\t;; ============================================================================="}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"fdb08464-5d12-43aa-870f-62a57771a5f6","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:33:12.048Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/admission.cljc","content":"\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Inherited ids (slice C9)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- predecessor\n  \"The occurrence whose completion edge goes to occurrence `s`, or nil.\n   A terminal edge names a result, not a successor, so it is no one's\n   predecessor.\"\n  [p s]\n  (some (fn [[o occ]]\n          (when (= s (get-in occ [:yin.k/closed :yin.k/successor])) o))\n        (:occurrences p)))\n\n\n(defn ancestor?\n  \"True when occurrence `a` is an ancestor of occurrence `o` through the\n   completion edges of projection p: the predecessor of o, or one of its\n   ancestors.  No ancestry runs through a terminal edge or an orphan,\n   and no occurrence is its own ancestor.  Derived, nothing indexed: each\n   step back scans the occurrences, so a check costs O(chain length x\n   occurrences) plus one content-store read per inherited admission, all\n   under the authority lock (a C12 cost note).\"\n  [p a o]\n  ;; the fold keeps the chain acyclic; the count only bounds the walk\n  (loop [s o n (count (:occurrences p))]\n    (let [x (predecessor p s)]\n      (cond\n        (nil? x) false\n        (= a x) true\n        (zero? n) false\n        :else (recur x (dec n))))))\n\n\n(defn member?\n  \"True when op id `op` is carried in operation baseline `b`\n   (yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint): by the root or any install child.  Ids\n   compare by canonical content.\"\n  [b op]\n  (let [k (cbor/content-key op)]\n    (boolean (some #(= k (cbor/content-key %)) (keys (:yin.k/ops b))))))\n\n\n(defn- accepted-baseline\n  \"The baseline of occurrence o's accepted checkpoint, read from content\n   store `store` and verified: the first variant, in a fixed address\n   order, whose bytes the store yields and the inspector turns into the\n   recorded baseline.  The offered variants share one baseline (C5), so\n   which one verifies cannot change the answer.  Nil when none does.\"\n  [p store o]\n  (let [{b :yin.k/baseline vs :yin.k/variants} (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n        read (fn [address]\n               (try\n                 ((:get-bytes-fn store) address nil)\n                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n                   nil)))]\n    (some (fn [address]\n            (let [bs (read address)]\n              (when (and (some? bs) (= b (checkpoint/inspect address bs)))\n                b)))\n          (sort-by str vs))))\n\n\n(defn- scope\n  \"Nil when op id `op` is in the scope of occurrence o, else\n   :foreign-op-id, or :unreadable when o's accepted checkpoint cannot be\n   read from `store` and verified.  Ancestry, read from p alone, comes\n   first: no checkpoint makes a non-ancestor's id admissible.\"\n  [p store o op]\n  (let [a (:yin.k/occurrence op)]\n    (cond\n      (= o a) nil\n      (not (ancestor? p a o)) :foreign-op-id\n      :else (if-let [b (accepted-baseline p store o)]\n              (when-not (member? b op) :foreign-op-id)\n              :unreadable))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================","numLines":80,"startLine":150,"totalLines":410}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LbuGEZWJned7Ydw3svrKdy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfyvgcDupCQRbUNm2kgWF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Xi8sZQiJfh8Zw7s3jpDoM","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":109126,"cache_read_input_tokens":237416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":109126},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"6ff9c95b-a0a7-4b71-ae12-ed8e28a8c4da","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:33:13.129Z","request_id":"req_011CfyvgawmrXmrmFPhZsh53","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015Xi8sZQiJfh8Zw7s3jpDoM":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Xi8sZQiJfh8Zw7s3jpDoM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.lift-support\n2\t  \"Test support for the version-1 lift (M-next D9): real machines the\n3\t   engine parks, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts, and\n4\t   `lift`, the whole enter / prepare / encode path over one machine.\n5\t\n6\t   Every body the D9 tests and the regenerated C4 fixtures check comes\n7\t   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map.  The one thing set by\n8\t   hand is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`): no code\n9\t   assigns ids until D11, whose fenced writer replaces that helper, and\n10\t   whose tests must show a real run produces entries equal in shape to\n11\t   what it sets.\"\n12\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n13\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n14\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n15\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n16\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n17\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n18\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n19\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n20\t            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\n21\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t;; =============================================================================\n25\t;; Machines\n26\t;; =============================================================================\n27\t\n28\t(defn- ring\n29\t  [capacity]\n30\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n31\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n32\t                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t(declare one-slot-stream)\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t(defn- make-det-stream\n39\t  \"A `:make-stream` whose streams carry no random identity, so a body\n40\t   that holds their cursors has the same bytes on every run and host.\"\n41\t  []\n42\t  (let [n (atom 0)]\n43\t    (fn [_capacity]\n44\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n45\t       :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"made-\" (swap! n inc)))})))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t(defn new-machine\n49\t  ([] (new-machine {}))\n50\t  ([opts]\n51\t   (semantic/create-vm\n52\t     (merge {:make-stream (make-det-stream)\n53\t             :capability-secret tu/secret\n54\t             :modules (module/default-registry)\n55\t             :secret-source (fn [origin]\n56\t                              (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))}\n57\t            opts))))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(def ^:private semantic-vector\n61\t  (comp :vector linearize/lower-rows vm/ast->semantic-bytecode))\n62\t\n63\t\n64\t(defn load-ast\n65\t  [machine ast]\n66\t  (semantic/load-vector machine (semantic-vector ast)\n67\t                        vm/semantic-contract))\n68\t\n69\t\n70\t(defn lit\n71\t  [x]\n72\t  {:type :literal, :value x})\n73\t\n74\t\n75\t(defn v\n76\t  [n]\n77\t  {:type :variable, :name n})\n78\t\n79\t\n80\t(defn lam\n81\t  [params body]\n82\t  {:type :lambda, :params params, :body body})\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn app\n86\t  [f & args]\n87\t  {:type :application, :operator f, :operands (vec args)})\n88\t\n89\t\n90\t(defn then\n91\t  [a b]\n92\t  (app (lam ['_] b) a))\n93\t\n94\t\n95\t(defn let1\n96\t  [param init body]\n97\t  (app (lam [param] body) init))\n98\t\n99\t\n100\t(defn def!\n101\t  [k val]\n102\t  (app (v 'yin/def) (lit k) val))\n103\t\n104\t\n105\t(defn cursor-of\n106\t  [source]\n107\t  {:type :stream/cursor, :source source})\n108\t\n109\t\n110\t(defn next-of\n111\t  [source]\n112\t  {:type :stream/next, :source source})\n113\t\n114\t\n115\t(defn one-slot-stream\n116\t  \"A stream that answers `full` while one value sits in it.\"\n117\t  [identity]\n118\t  (let [slot (atom :empty)]\n119\t    (reify\n120\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n121\t      (descriptor\n122\t        [_]\n123\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n124\t         :dao.stream/identity identity,\n125\t         :dao.stream/descriptor\n126\t         {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel,\n127\t          :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n128\t\n129\t\n130\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n131\t\n132\t      (cursor\n133\t        [_ _anchor]\n134\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok, :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n135\t\n136\t      (next\n137\t        [_ cursor]\n138\t        (if (and (= 0 cursor) (not= :empty @slot))\n139\t          (let [x @slot]\n140\t            (reset! slot :empty)\n141\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n142\t             :dao.stream/value x, :dao.stream/cursor 1})\n143\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))\n144\t\n145\t\n146\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n147\t\n148\t      (append!\n149\t        [_ x]\n150\t        (if (not= :empty @slot)\n151\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}\n152\t          (do (reset! slot x)\n153\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))))\n154\t\n155\t\n156\t(defn parked-reader\n157\t  \"A real machine parked on the second read of the stream it makes, A\n158\t   consumed: one :next frame over one cell.\"\n159\t  []\n160\t  (let [m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n161\t                             (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n162\t                                   (let1 'c (cursor-of (v 's))\n163\t                                         (then (next-of (v 'c))\n164\t                                               (next-of (v 'c)))))))\n165\t        entry (first (:wait-set m0))\n166\t        src (get (:resources m0) (:stream-id entry))]\n167\t    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n168\t    (vm/run m0)))\n169\t\n170\t\n171\t(defn parked-two-cursors\n172\t  \"Parks on a read through the cursor held under 'held-a; the store holds\n173\t   a cursor on each of two streams, so the waiter's cell is shared with\n174\t   the store's and a second cell is reached from the store alone.\"\n175\t  []\n176\t  (vm/run\n177\t    (load-ast\n178\t      (new-machine)\n179\t      (let1 'a {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n180\t            (let1 'b {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n181\t                  (then (def! 'held-a (cursor-of (v 'a)))\n182\t                        (then (def! 'held-b (cursor-of (v 'b)))\n183\t                              (next-of (v 'held-a)))))))))\n184\t\n185\t\n186\t(defn parked-writer\n187\t  \"A real machine parked on a blocked write: the warm one-slot stream\n188\t   keeps the value retained.  One :put frame.\"\n189\t  []\n190\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n191\t    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n192\t    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n193\t                       {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w), :val (lit \"v\")})\n194\t          [ref m0'] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)]\n195\t      (vm/run (assoc m0' :store {'w ref})))))\n196\t\n197\t\n198\t(defn parked-explicit\n199\t  \"A real machine at an explicit park, its record's environment holding\n200\t   a cursor on a stream.\"\n201\t  []\n202\t  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n203\t                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n204\t                          (app (lam ['c] {:type :vm/park})\n205\t                               (cursor-of (v 's)))))))\n206\t\n207\t\n208\t(defn parked-writer-shared\n209\t  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n210\t   under two resource ids: the write's own target and the environment's\n211\t   second reference.  Prepare must ask `serve!` once and key the answer\n212\t   under both.\"\n213\t  []\n214\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n215\t    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n216\t    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n217\t                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n218\t                             {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w)\n219\t                              :val (lit \"v\")}))\n220\t          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n221\t          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)]\n222\t      (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'w ra 'w2 rb})))))\n223\t\n224\t\n225\t(defn parked-linker\n226\t  \"A real machine parked on a link request whose response cursor is not\n227\t   installed: run under the :running gate, so the mint belongs to the\n228\t   driver and the entry carries no :cursor (the D6 gap the rulings\n229\t   name).  Its export is refused at entering and at the lift.\"\n230\t  []\n231\t  (vm/run (-> (new-machine {:link-request (ring 8) :link-response (ring 8)})\n232\t              (load-ast (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)))\n233\t              (assoc :yin.k/gate :running))))\n234\t\n235\t\n236\t(defn halted-machine\n237\t  \"A halted machine whose result is 42.\"\n238\t  []\n239\t  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit 42))))\n240\t\n241\t\n242\t(defn halted-with\n243\t  \"A halted machine whose result is the literal `value`.\"\n244\t  [value]\n245\t  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit value))))\n246\t\n247\t\n248\t(defn- fresh-cursors\n249\t  \"Two sealed cursor references, `k1` and `k2`, minted over two attached\n250\t   one-slot streams the program never names: the first place either cell\n251\t   is minted is the walk that reaches the references.\"\n252\t  [machine]\n253\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"k1\")\n254\t        x (one-slot-stream \"k2\")\n255\t        [wa m1] (engine/attach-resource machine w)\n256\t        [xa m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 x)\n257\t        [c1 m3] (engine/handle-cursor m2 {:stream wa} :k1)\n258\t        [c2 m4] (engine/handle-cursor m3 {:stream xa} :k2)]\n259\t    {:c1 c1, :c2 c2, :machine m4}))\n260\t\n261\t\n262\t(defn parked-cursor-keyed\n263\t  \"A real machine parked at an explicit park whose task store maps, under\n264\t   a name the parked code references, a map whose keys are two cursor\n265\t   references nothing else reaches, so the store walk's literal ordering\n266\t   is the first place either cell is minted.\"\n267\t  []\n268\t  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n269\t                            (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n270\t                                  (then (def! 'mapped (lit {}))\n271\t                                        (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park})\n272\t                                             (v 'mapped))))))\n273\t        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)]\n274\t    (assoc machine :store (assoc (:store machine) 'mapped {c1 1, c2 2}))))\n275\t\n276\t\n277\t(defn- linking-machine\n278\t  [request response]\n279\t  (new-machine {:link-request request :link-response response}))\n280\t\n281\t\n282\t(defn- module-response\n283\t  []\n284\t  {:status :ok,\n285\t   :image {:value (semantic-vector\n286\t                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n287\t                          (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's)))\n288\t                                (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42))))))},\n289\t   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod,\n290\t              :yin.module/exports #{'f}},\n291\t   :obligations []})\n292\t\n293\t\n294\t(defn parked-installer\n295\t  \"A real machine parked at :install with a live child blocked on its\n296\t   own read.\"\n297\t  []\n298\t  (let [request (ring 64)\n299\t        response (ring 64)\n300\t        m0 (vm/run (load-ast (linking-machine request response)\n301\t                             (then (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod))\n302\t                                   (app (v 'host.mod/f)))))\n303\t        entry (first (:wait-set m0))]\n304\t    (stream/append! response\n305\t                    (assoc (module-response)\n306\t                           :yin.link/id (:link-id entry)))\n307\t    (vm/run m0)))\n308\t\n309\t\n310\t(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n311\t  \"A real machine parked at an explicit park whose module store for\n312\t   'host.mod holds two cursor references nothing else reaches, named by\n313\t   a module closure in the task store -- the shape a lowered module\n314\t   closure has, its environment naming the module whose store it runs\n315\t   against -- so the module-store snapshot's walk is the first place\n316\t   either cell is minted.\"\n317\t  []\n318\t  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n319\t                            (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n320\t                                  (then (def! 'mod (lit 1))\n321\t                                        (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park})\n322\t                                             (v 'mod))))))\n323\t        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n324\t        seg (:segment (first (vals (:parked machine))))\n325\t        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n326\t                            {:type :closure, :params [], :entry 0,\n327\t                             :segment seg,\n328\t                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n329\t    (assoc machine\n330\t           :store (assoc (:store machine) 'mod clo)\n331\t           :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1, 'd c2}})))\n332\t\n333\t\n334\t(defn halted-with-cursors\n335\t  \"A halted machine whose result is `(f c1 c2)` for the two fresh cursor\n336\t   references nothing else reaches: the result walk is the first place\n337\t   either cell is minted.\"\n338\t  [f]\n339\t  (let [{:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors (halted-machine))]\n340\t    (assoc machine :value (f c1 c2))))\n341\t\n342\t\n343\t(defn halted-result-closure\n344\t  \"A halted machine whose result is a module closure -- its environment\n345\t   naming 'host.mod -- and whose 'host.mod module store holds two cursor\n346\t   references nothing else reaches: only the result names the module.\"\n347\t  []\n348\t  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lam [] (lit 1))))\n349\t        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n350\t        real (values/payload (:value machine))]\n351\t    (assoc machine\n352\t           :value (values/closure (:owner machine)\n353\t                                  (assoc real\n354\t                                         :env {engine/store-of-key\n355\t                                               'host.mod}))\n356\t           :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1, 'd c2}})))\n357\t\n358\t\n359\t(defn parked-writer-shared-late\n360\t  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n361\t   under two resource ids, with a third, independent stream reached\n362\t   between them -- the environment's bindings put the first alias, the\n363\t   independent stream, then the pending's alias -- so a prepare that\n364\t   serves the first alias and refuses the third leaves the second alias\n365\t   unserved, and the retry must resolve it from the record without\n366\t   serving the handle again.\"\n367\t  []\n368\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")\n369\t        x (one-slot-stream \"x\")]\n370\t    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n371\t    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n372\t                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n373\t                             (let1 'later-than-again (v 'x2)\n374\t                                   {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w),\n375\t                                    :val (lit \"v\")})))\n376\t          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n377\t          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)\n378\t          [rx m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 x)]\n379\t      (vm/run (assoc m3 :store {'w ra, 'w2 rb, 'x2 rx})))))\n380\t\n381\t\n382\t;; =============================================================================\n383\t;; Operation ids: set by hand until D11\n384\t;; =============================================================================\n385\t\n386\t(defn with-op-id\n387\t  \"`machine` with `id` as the `:op-id` of its first wait entry whose\n388\t   reason is `reason`, in the root or, with `path`, in the install child\n389\t   at `path`.  D11 replaces this: its fenced writer assigns ids, and its\n390\t   tests must show a real run's wait entries equal in shape to what this\n391\t   sets.\"\n392\t  ([machine reason id] (with-op-id machine [] reason id))\n393\t  ([machine path reason id]\n394\t   (let [at (into [] (mapcat (fn [m] [:installs m :vm])) path)\n395\t         waits (get-in machine (conj at :wait-set))\n396\t         i (first (keep-indexed #(when (= reason (:reason %2)) %1) waits))]\n397\t     (assert (some? i) (str \"no wait entry of reason \" reason))\n398\t     (assoc-in machine (into at [:wait-set i :op-id]) id))))\n399\t\n400\t\n401\t;; =============================================================================\n402\t;; The exporter and the lift\n403\t;; =============================================================================\n404\t\n405\t(defn serve-table\n406\t  \"A `serve!` answering one stable identity per handle, \\\"s0\\\", \\\"s1\\\"\n407\t   ... in the order the handles are first asked about.\"\n408\t  []\n409\t  (let [table (atom {})]\n410\t    (fn [h]\n411\t      (or (get @table h)\n412\t          (let [served {:dao.stream/identity (str \"s\" (count @table))\n413\t                        :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type\n414\t                                             :dao.stream.test/channel}}]\n415\t            (swap! table assoc h served)\n416\t            served)))))\n417\t\n418\t\n419\t(def occurrence \"8f0c6a52-6a1e-4e43-9d55-3f0a4c1b2e01\")\n420\t(def predecessor \"1d3e5b7a-0c2f-4a69-8b11-7e6d5c4b3a02\")\n421\t\n422\t\n423\t(def origin\n424\t  {:yin.k/occurrence predecessor\n425\t   :dao.lease/lease \"lease-7\"\n426\t   :yin.k/emitter \"peer-a\"})\n427\t\n428\t\n429\t(def arbitration\n430\t  {:dao.stream/identity \"arbitration-1\"\n431\t   :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :remote :peer \"peer-b\"}})\n432\t\n433\t\n434\t(defn op-id\n435\t  ([n] (op-id predecessor n))\n436\t  ([occ n] {:yin.k/occurrence occ :yin.k/seq n}))\n437\t\n438\t\n439\t(defn header\n440\t  \"The version-1 header argument of `prepare`: a first export when `o` is\n441\t   nil.\"\n442\t  ([n] (header n origin #{}))\n443\t  ([n o enrolled]\n444\t   (cond-> {:yin.k/occurrence occurrence\n445\t            :yin.k/arbitration arbitration\n446\t            :yin.k/next-op-seq n\n447\t            :yin.k/enrolled enrolled}\n448\t     (some? o) (assoc :yin.k/origin o))))\n449\t\n450\t\n451\t(defn prepared\n452\t  \"Enter exporting from `machine` and prepare it under `header` with a\n453\t   fresh deterministic exporter: `{:machine m :record r :prepared p}`.\n454\t   A refusal of `enter` is `:prepared`.\"\n455\t  [machine header]\n456\t  (let [e (export/enter machine)]\n457\t    (if (= :ok (:status e))\n458\t      {:machine (:machine e)\n459\t       :record (:record e)\n460\t       :prepared (export/prepare (:machine e) (:record e) (serve-table)\n461\t                                 header)}\n462\t      {:prepared e})))\n463\t\n464\t\n465\t(defn lift\n466\t  \"The whole path over `machine`: enter, prepare, encode.  Answers the\n467\t   encode result, or the refusal prepare (or enter) answered.\"\n468\t  [machine header]\n469\t  (let [{m :machine p :prepared} (prepared machine header)]\n470\t    (if (= :ok (:status p))\n471\t      (export/encode m (:record p))\n472\t      p)))\n473\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"8d119918-1559-4f89-b8f3-e4d74e8a549c","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:33:13.147Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.lift-support\n  \"Test support for the version-1 lift (M-next D9): real machines the\n   engine parks, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts, and\n   `lift`, the whole enter / prepare / encode path over one machine.\n\n   Every body the D9 tests and the regenerated C4 fixtures check comes\n   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map.  The one thing set by\n   hand is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`): no code\n   assigns ids until D11, whose fenced writer replaces that helper, and\n   whose tests must show a real run produces entries equal in shape to\n   what it sets.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Machines\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- ring\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n\n\n(declare one-slot-stream)\n\n\n(defn- make-det-stream\n  \"A `:make-stream` whose streams carry no random identity, so a body\n   that holds their cursors has the same bytes on every run and host.\"\n  []\n  (let [n (atom 0)]\n    (fn [_capacity]\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n       :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"made-\" (swap! n inc)))})))\n\n\n(defn new-machine\n  ([] (new-machine {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (semantic/create-vm\n     (merge {:make-stream (make-det-stream)\n             :capability-secret tu/secret\n             :modules (module/default-registry)\n             :secret-source (fn [origin]\n                              (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))}\n            opts))))\n\n\n(def ^:private semantic-vector\n  (comp :vector linearize/lower-rows vm/ast->semantic-bytecode))\n\n\n(defn load-ast\n  [machine ast]\n  (semantic/load-vector machine (semantic-vector ast)\n                        vm/semantic-contract))\n\n\n(defn lit\n  [x]\n  {:type :literal, :value x})\n\n\n(defn v\n  [n]\n  {:type :variable, :name n})\n\n\n(defn lam\n  [params body]\n  {:type :lambda, :params params, :body body})\n\n\n(defn app\n  [f & args]\n  {:type :application, :operator f, :operands (vec args)})\n\n\n(defn then\n  [a b]\n  (app (lam ['_] b) a))\n\n\n(defn let1\n  [param init body]\n  (app (lam [param] body) init))\n\n\n(defn def!\n  [k val]\n  (app (v 'yin/def) (lit k) val))\n\n\n(defn cursor-of\n  [source]\n  {:type :stream/cursor, :source source})\n\n\n(defn next-of\n  [source]\n  {:type :stream/next, :source source})\n\n\n(defn one-slot-stream\n  \"A stream that answers `full` while one value sits in it.\"\n  [identity]\n  (let [slot (atom :empty)]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n         :dao.stream/identity identity,\n         :dao.stream/descriptor\n         {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel,\n          :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok, :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (if (and (= 0 cursor) (not= :empty @slot))\n          (let [x @slot]\n            (reset! slot :empty)\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n             :dao.stream/value x, :dao.stream/cursor 1})\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (if (not= :empty @slot)\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}\n          (do (reset! slot x)\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))))\n\n\n(defn parked-reader\n  \"A real machine parked on the second read of the stream it makes, A\n   consumed: one :next frame over one cell.\"\n  []\n  (let [m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                             (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                                   (let1 'c (cursor-of (v 's))\n                                         (then (next-of (v 'c))\n                                               (next-of (v 'c)))))))\n        entry (first (:wait-set m0))\n        src (get (:resources m0) (:stream-id entry))]\n    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n    (vm/run m0)))\n\n\n(defn parked-two-cursors\n  \"Parks on a read through the cursor held under 'held-a; the store holds\n   a cursor on each of two streams, so the waiter's cell is shared with\n   the store's and a second cell is reached from the store alone.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run\n    (load-ast\n      (new-machine)\n      (let1 'a {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n            (let1 'b {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                  (then (def! 'held-a (cursor-of (v 'a)))\n                        (then (def! 'held-b (cursor-of (v 'b)))\n                              (next-of (v 'held-a)))))))))\n\n\n(defn parked-writer\n  \"A real machine parked on a blocked write: the warm one-slot stream\n   keeps the value retained.  One :put frame.\"\n  []\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n                       {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w), :val (lit \"v\")})\n          [ref m0'] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)]\n      (vm/run (assoc m0' :store {'w ref})))))\n\n\n(defn parked-explicit\n  \"A real machine at an explicit park, its record's environment holding\n   a cursor on a stream.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                          (app (lam ['c] {:type :vm/park})\n                               (cursor-of (v 's)))))))\n\n\n(defn parked-writer-shared\n  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n   under two resource ids: the write's own target and the environment's\n   second reference.  Prepare must ask `serve!` once and key the answer\n   under both.\"\n  []\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n                             {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w)\n                              :val (lit \"v\")}))\n          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)]\n      (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'w ra 'w2 rb})))))\n\n\n(defn parked-linker\n  \"A real machine parked on a link request whose response cursor is not\n   installed: run under the :running gate, so the mint belongs to the\n   driver and the entry carries no :cursor (the D6 gap the rulings\n   name).  Its export is refused at entering and at the lift.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (-> (new-machine {:link-request (ring 8) :link-response (ring 8)})\n              (load-ast (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)))\n              (assoc :yin.k/gate :running))))\n\n\n(defn halted-machine\n  \"A halted machine whose result is 42.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit 42))))\n\n\n(defn halted-with\n  \"A halted machine whose result is the literal `value`.\"\n  [value]\n  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit value))))\n\n\n(defn- fresh-cursors\n  \"Two sealed cursor references, `k1` and `k2`, minted over two attached\n   one-slot streams the program never names: the first place either cell\n   is minted is the walk that reaches the references.\"\n  [machine]\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"k1\")\n        x (one-slot-stream \"k2\")\n        [wa m1] (engine/attach-resource machine w)\n        [xa m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 x)\n        [c1 m3] (engine/handle-cursor m2 {:stream wa} :k1)\n        [c2 m4] (engine/handle-cursor m3 {:stream xa} :k2)]\n    {:c1 c1, :c2 c2, :machine m4}))\n\n\n(defn parked-cursor-keyed\n  \"A real machine parked at an explicit park whose task store maps, under\n   a name the parked code references, a map whose keys are two cursor\n   references nothing else reaches, so the store walk's literal ordering\n   is the first place either cell is minted.\"\n  []\n  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                            (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                                  (then (def! 'mapped (lit {}))\n                                        (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park})\n                                             (v 'mapped))))))\n        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)]\n    (assoc machine :store (assoc (:store machine) 'mapped {c1 1, c2 2}))))\n\n\n(defn- linking-machine\n  [request response]\n  (new-machine {:link-request request :link-response response}))\n\n\n(defn- module-response\n  []\n  {:status :ok,\n   :image {:value (semantic-vector\n                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                          (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's)))\n                                (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42))))))},\n   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod,\n              :yin.module/exports #{'f}},\n   :obligations []})\n\n\n(defn parked-installer\n  \"A real machine parked at :install with a live child blocked on its\n   own read.\"\n  []\n  (let [request (ring 64)\n        response (ring 64)\n        m0 (vm/run (load-ast (linking-machine request response)\n                             (then (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod))\n                                   (app (v 'host.mod/f)))))\n        entry (first (:wait-set m0))]\n    (stream/append! response\n                    (assoc (module-response)\n                           :yin.link/id (:link-id entry)))\n    (vm/run m0)))\n\n\n(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n  \"A real machine parked at an explicit park whose module store for\n   'host.mod holds two cursor references nothing else reaches, named by\n   a module closure in the task store -- the shape a lowered module\n   closure has, its environment naming the module whose store it runs\n   against -- so the module-store snapshot's walk is the first place\n   either cell is minted.\"\n  []\n  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                            (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                                  (then (def! 'mod (lit 1))\n                                        (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park})\n                                             (v 'mod))))))\n        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n        seg (:segment (first (vals (:parked machine))))\n        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n                            {:type :closure, :params [], :entry 0,\n                             :segment seg,\n                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n    (assoc machine\n           :store (assoc (:store machine) 'mod clo)\n           :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1, 'd c2}})))\n\n\n(defn halted-with-cursors\n  \"A halted machine whose result is `(f c1 c2)` for the two fresh cursor\n   references nothing else reaches: the result walk is the first place\n   either cell is minted.\"\n  [f]\n  (let [{:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors (halted-machine))]\n    (assoc machine :value (f c1 c2))))\n\n\n(defn halted-result-closure\n  \"A halted machine whose result is a module closure -- its environment\n   naming 'host.mod -- and whose 'host.mod module store holds two cursor\n   references nothing else reaches: only the result names the module.\"\n  []\n  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lam [] (lit 1))))\n        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n        real (values/payload (:value machine))]\n    (assoc machine\n           :value (values/closure (:owner machine)\n                                  (assoc real\n                                         :env {engine/store-of-key\n                                               'host.mod}))\n           :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1, 'd c2}})))\n\n\n(defn parked-writer-shared-late\n  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n   under two resource ids, with a third, independent stream reached\n   between them -- the environment's bindings put the first alias, the\n   independent stream, then the pending's alias -- so a prepare that\n   serves the first alias and refuses the third leaves the second alias\n   unserved, and the retry must resolve it from the record without\n   serving the handle again.\"\n  []\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")\n        x (one-slot-stream \"x\")]\n    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n                             (let1 'later-than-again (v 'x2)\n                                   {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w),\n                                    :val (lit \"v\")})))\n          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)\n          [rx m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 x)]\n      (vm/run (assoc m3 :store {'w ra, 'w2 rb, 'x2 rx})))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Operation ids: set by hand until D11\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn with-op-id\n  \"`machine` with `id` as the `:op-id` of its first wait entry whose\n   reason is `reason`, in the root or, with `path`, in the install child\n   at `path`.  D11 replaces this: its fenced writer assigns ids, and its\n   tests must show a real run's wait entries equal in shape to what this\n   sets.\"\n  ([machine reason id] (with-op-id machine [] reason id))\n  ([machine path reason id]\n   (let [at (into [] (mapcat (fn [m] [:installs m :vm])) path)\n         waits (get-in machine (conj at :wait-set))\n         i (first (keep-indexed #(when (= reason (:reason %2)) %1) waits))]\n     (assert (some? i) (str \"no wait entry of reason \" reason))\n     (assoc-in machine (into at [:wait-set i :op-id]) id))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The exporter and the lift\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn serve-table\n  \"A `serve!` answering one stable identity per handle, \\\"s0\\\", \\\"s1\\\"\n   ... in the order the handles are first asked about.\"\n  []\n  (let [table (atom {})]\n    (fn [h]\n      (or (get @table h)\n          (let [served {:dao.stream/identity (str \"s\" (count @table))\n                        :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type\n                                             :dao.stream.test/channel}}]\n            (swap! table assoc h served)\n            served)))))\n\n\n(def occurrence \"8f0c6a52-6a1e-4e43-9d55-3f0a4c1b2e01\")\n(def predecessor \"1d3e5b7a-0c2f-4a69-8b11-7e6d5c4b3a02\")\n\n\n(def origin\n  {:yin.k/occurrence predecessor\n   :dao.lease/lease \"lease-7\"\n   :yin.k/emitter \"peer-a\"})\n\n\n(def arbitration\n  {:dao.stream/identity \"arbitration-1\"\n   :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :remote :peer \"peer-b\"}})\n\n\n(defn op-id\n  ([n] (op-id predecessor n))\n  ([occ n] {:yin.k/occurrence occ :yin.k/seq n}))\n\n\n(defn header\n  \"The version-1 header argument of `prepare`: a first export when `o` is\n   nil.\"\n  ([n] (header n origin #{}))\n  ([n o enrolled]\n   (cond-> {:yin.k/occurrence occurrence\n            :yin.k/arbitration arbitration\n            :yin.k/next-op-seq n\n            :yin.k/enrolled enrolled}\n     (some? o) (assoc :yin.k/origin o))))\n\n\n(defn prepared\n  \"Enter exporting from `machine` and prepare it under `header` with a\n   fresh deterministic exporter: `{:machine m :record r :prepared p}`.\n   A refusal of `enter` is `:prepared`.\"\n  [machine header]\n  (let [e (export/enter machine)]\n    (if (= :ok (:status e))\n      {:machine (:machine e)\n       :record (:record e)\n       :prepared (export/prepare (:machine e) (:record e) (serve-table)\n                                 header)}\n      {:prepared e})))\n\n\n(defn lift\n  \"The whole path over `machine`: enter, prepare, encode.  Answers the\n   encode result, or the refusal prepare (or enter) answered.\"\n  [machine header]\n  (let [{m :machine p :prepared} (prepared machine header)]\n    (if (= :ok (:status p))\n      (export/encode m (:record p))\n      p)))\n","numLines":473,"startLine":1,"totalLines":473}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015Xi8sZQiJfh8Zw7s3jpDoM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
