{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MDiaCue3KDw2X6CEyYTZBK","type":"tool_result","content":"1084\t(defn- arm-exit\n1085\t  \"Arm the exit over the state's machine: enter exporting now (the\n1086\t   refusal answers and arms nothing).  The fenced machine stays as\n1087\t   :machine and travels in the cell; the answer is the armed state or\n1088\t   the refusal, never both.\"\n1089\t  [state role]\n1090\t  (let [e (export/enter (:machine state) {:version (:export-version state)})]\n1091\t    (if (= :ok (:status e))\n1092\t      {:state (-> state\n1093\t                  (assoc :machine (:machine e))\n1094\t                  (assoc :exit {:role role\n1095\t                                :m (:machine e)\n1096\t                                :record (:record e)}))\n1097\t       :refusal nil}\n1098\t      {:state (with-status state :yin.k/unsatisfied\n1099\t                {:yin.k/reason :not-liftable\n1100\t                 :refusal (select-keys e [:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind\n1101\t                                          :yin.k/path :yin.k/hold])})\n1102\t       :refusal e})))\n1103\t\n1104\t\n1105\t(defn hand-off\n1106\t  \"Arm the exit half over a holder whose machine is parked or blocked\n1107\t   at a liftable safepoint: the composition's explicit export of a\n1108\t   parked continuation (UCF 7.8's lift is composition-driven, never\n1109\t   automatic on a park).  The phase becomes :safepoint and the next\n1110\t   step mints the successor; a machine that cannot enter exporting\n1111\t   answers the refusal, arms nothing and keeps running.\"\n1112\t  [state]\n1113\t  (if (= :stalled (:phase state))\n1114\t    state\n1115\t    (let [{:keys [state refusal]} (arm-exit state :yin.k/successor)]\n1116\t      (if (nil? refusal)\n1117\t        (assoc state :phase :safepoint\n1118\t               :status :yin.k/ok\n1119\t               :detail {:yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state)\n1120\t                        :dao.lease/lease (:lease state)})\n1121\t        state))))\n1122\t\n1123\t\n1124\t(defn- exit-mint\n1125\t  \"The first step of the exit: mint the successor occurrence once and\n1126\t   journal it before prepare.  The header is built from the custody\n1127\t   map: a fresh occurrence, the same arbitration, an origin naming the\n1128\t   predecessor occurrence and lease and this driver as the emitter, the\n1129\t   current counter, and the enrolled set of the ledger fold.\"\n1130\t  [state]\n1131\t  (when (:holder state) (require-tenure! state))\n1132\t  (let [cell (:exit state)\n1133\t        cust (get-in (:machine state) [:yin.k/custody])\n1134\t        [enrolled reason] (enrolled-of state)]\n1135\t    (if (nil? enrolled)\n1136\t      (unsatisfied state reason {:dao.stream/identity (:arbitration state)})\n1137\t      (let [o (custody/mint-occurrence)\n1138\t            header {:yin.k/occurrence o\n1139\t                    :yin.k/arbitration (:yin.k/arbitration cust)\n1140\t                    :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq cust)\n1141\t                    :yin.k/enrolled enrolled\n1142\t                    :yin.k/origin {:yin.k/occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence cust)\n1143\t                                   :dao.lease/lease (:dao.lease/lease cust)\n1144\t                                   :yin.k/emitter (:me state)}}]\n1145\t        (journal! state\n1146\t                  {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/minted\n1147\t                   :yin.k/role (:role cell)\n1148\t                   :yin.k/occurrence o\n1149\t                   :yin.k/header header})\n1150\t        (-> state\n1151\t            (assoc :exit (assoc cell :occurrence o :header header))\n1152\t            (with-status :yin.k/ok\n1153\t              {:exit (:role cell) :step :minted}))))))\n1154\t\n1155\t\n1156\t(defn- exit-report-step\n1157\t  \"The resumed report bracket: one intent record durable before the\n1158\t   send, naming the successor's address; for a halt the report carries\n1159\t   the result body's address and the closure's edge is terminal.  The\n1160\t   acknowledgment is journaled when the front's authenticated reply\n1161\t   commits or replays it.\"\n1162\t  [state]\n1163\t  (when (:holder state) (require-tenure! state))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"ecdba420-6253-4d44-b363-031c744c3918","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:33:54.058Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc","content":"(defn- arm-exit\n  \"Arm the exit over the state's machine: enter exporting now (the\n   refusal answers and arms nothing).  The fenced machine stays as\n   :machine and travels in the cell; the answer is the armed state or\n   the refusal, never both.\"\n  [state role]\n  (let [e (export/enter (:machine state) {:version (:export-version state)})]\n    (if (= :ok (:status e))\n      {:state (-> state\n                  (assoc :machine (:machine e))\n                  (assoc :exit {:role role\n                                :m (:machine e)\n                                :record (:record e)}))\n       :refusal nil}\n      {:state (with-status state :yin.k/unsatisfied\n                {:yin.k/reason :not-liftable\n                 :refusal (select-keys e [:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind\n                                          :yin.k/path :yin.k/hold])})\n       :refusal e})))\n\n\n(defn hand-off\n  \"Arm the exit half over a holder whose machine is parked or blocked\n   at a liftable safepoint: the composition's explicit export of a\n   parked continuation (UCF 7.8's lift is composition-driven, never\n   automatic on a park).  The phase becomes :safepoint and the next\n   step mints the successor; a machine that cannot enter exporting\n   answers the refusal, arms nothing and keeps running.\"\n  [state]\n  (if (= :stalled (:phase state))\n    state\n    (let [{:keys [state refusal]} (arm-exit state :yin.k/successor)]\n      (if (nil? refusal)\n        (assoc state :phase :safepoint\n               :status :yin.k/ok\n               :detail {:yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state)\n                        :dao.lease/lease (:lease state)})\n        state))))\n\n\n(defn- exit-mint\n  \"The first step of the exit: mint the successor occurrence once and\n   journal it before prepare.  The header is built from the custody\n   map: a fresh occurrence, the same arbitration, an origin naming the\n   predecessor occurrence and lease and this driver as the emitter, the\n   current counter, and the enrolled set of the ledger fold.\"\n  [state]\n  (when (:holder state) (require-tenure! state))\n  (let [cell (:exit state)\n        cust (get-in (:machine state) [:yin.k/custody])\n        [enrolled reason] (enrolled-of state)]\n    (if (nil? enrolled)\n      (unsatisfied state reason {:dao.stream/identity (:arbitration state)})\n      (let [o (custody/mint-occurrence)\n            header {:yin.k/occurrence o\n                    :yin.k/arbitration (:yin.k/arbitration cust)\n                    :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq cust)\n                    :yin.k/enrolled enrolled\n                    :yin.k/origin {:yin.k/occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence cust)\n                                   :dao.lease/lease (:dao.lease/lease cust)\n                                   :yin.k/emitter (:me state)}}]\n        (journal! state\n                  {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/minted\n                   :yin.k/role (:role cell)\n                   :yin.k/occurrence o\n                   :yin.k/header header})\n        (-> state\n            (assoc :exit (assoc cell :occurrence o :header header))\n            (with-status :yin.k/ok\n              {:exit (:role cell) :step :minted}))))))\n\n\n(defn- exit-report-step\n  \"The resumed report bracket: one intent record durable before the\n   send, naming the successor's address; for a halt the report carries\n   the result body's address and the closure's edge is terminal.  The\n   ack