{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0146dKRmaDDF5LTsH4YoSJ9G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n2\t  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n3\t   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n4\t\n5\t   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n6\t   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n7\t   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n8\t   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n9\t   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n10\t   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n11\t   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n12\t   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n13\t   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n14\t\n15\t   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n16\t   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n17\t   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n18\t   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n19\t   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n20\t   layout refusals close the file.\"\n21\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n22\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n23\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n24\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n25\t            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n26\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n27\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n28\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n29\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n30\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n31\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n32\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n33\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n34\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n35\t            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n36\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n37\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n38\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n39\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n40\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n41\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n42\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n43\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n44\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n45\t            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t;; =============================================================================\n49\t;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n50\t;; =============================================================================\n51\t\n52\t(def source-index\n53\t  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n54\t   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n55\t  (atom {}))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(def code-index\n59\t  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n60\t  (atom {}))\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t(def ^:dynamic *projected*\n64\t  \"When bound, an atom {A v} of the vectors one world projected: the\n65\t   layouts' spaces read it instead of the whole file's code-index, so an\n66\t   alpha-equivalent A an unrelated fixture projected widens no lookup.\"\n67\t  nil)\n68\t\n69\t\n70\t(defn project\n71\t  [ast]\n72\t  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n73\t        a (jing/segment-key v)]\n74\t    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n75\t    (swap! code-index assoc a v)\n76\t    (when *projected* (swap! *projected* assoc a v))\n77\t    v))\n78\t\n79\t\n80\t(defn scoped\n81\t  \"f's result, every vector it projects recorded in a fresh *projected*.\"\n82\t  [f]\n83\t  (binding [*projected* (atom {})] (f)))\n84\t\n85\t\n86\t(defn file-wide\n87\t  \"f's result, the layouts' spaces reading every vector the file ever\n88\t   projected: only the fixtures that show that contamination.\"\n89\t  [f]\n90\t  (binding [*projected* code-index] (f)))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t(def ^:dynamic *lane*\n97\t  \"The kernel a world is built on: :semantic-register (the reference\n98\t   lane), or :stack or :register, which run A's derived image and lift\n99\t   and lower through the layouts (§5.3).\"\n100\t  :semantic-register)\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t(def lanes [:semantic-register :stack :register])\n104\t\n105\t\n106\t(defn- composition\n107\t  [opts]\n108\t  (merge {:make-stream tu/make-stream :capability-secret tu/secret\n109\t          :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))\n110\t          :modules stream-modules}\n111\t         opts))\n112\t\n113\t\n114\t(defn- kernel-opts\n115\t  \"A de Bruijn kernel's options for the same composition: the full\n116\t   primitive table, and the initial environment as :free-env.\"\n117\t  [opts]\n118\t  (cond-> (assoc (dissoc (composition opts) :env) :primitives vm/primitives)\n119\t    (contains? opts :env) (assoc :free-env (:env opts))))\n120\t\n121\t\n122\t(defn machine\n123\t  ([] (machine {}))\n124\t  ([opts]\n125\t   (case *lane*\n126\t     :semantic-register (sr/create-vm (composition opts))\n127\t     :stack (dvm/create-vm [] (kernel-opts opts))\n128\t     :register (rvm/create-vm (assoc {} :bodies [] :instructions []) (kernel-opts opts)))))\n129\t\n130\t\n131\t(defn lane-of\n132\t  [m]\n133\t  (let [f (:format (module/link-format m))]\n134\t    (cond (= dvm/format-tag f) :stack\n135\t          (= rvm/format-tag f) :register\n136\t          :else :semantic-register)))\n137\t\n138\t\n139\t(def segment-of\n140\t  \"layout/segment, once per A.\"\n141\t  (memoize layout/segment))\n142\t\n143\t\n144\t(defn kernel-space\n145\t  \"The layout space of the A vectors whose images de Bruijn kernel k\n146\t   holds, among those this world projected (`scoped`), or the file ever\n147\t   projected (`file-wide`). Unbound, it throws: an independent world's\n148\t   lookups never read another fixture's vectors.\"\n149\t  [k]\n150\t  (when-not *projected*\n151\t    (throw (ex-info \"kernel-space outside scoped or file-wide\" {})))\n152\t  (let [id (if (= :stack (lane-of k)) :stack-id :register-id)\n153\t        held (into #{} (map first) (:images k))]\n154\t    (layout/space (filter #(contains? held (id %)) (map segment-of (vals @*projected*))))))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn- kernel-load\n158\t  \"Attach v's derived image and start it at its row, beside whatever the\n159\t   kernel already holds: parked records keep naming their own rows.\"\n160\t  [k v]\n161\t  (let [kind (lane-of k)\n162\t        sg (segment-of v)\n163\t        k (if (= :stack kind)\n164\t            (dvm/attach-image k (:stack sg) vm/stack-contract)\n165\t            (rvm/attach-image k (:register sg) vm/register-contract))\n166\t        k (assoc k :pc (layout/offset kind k sg) :frames [] :continuation [] :store-of nil\n167\t                 :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)]\n168\t    (if (= :stack kind)\n169\t      (assoc k :stack [])\n170\t      (assoc k :registers (vec (repeat (:registers (first (:bodies (:register sg)))) nil))))))\n171\t\n172\t\n173\t(defn load-program\n174\t  [m ast]\n175\t  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n176\t    (sr/load-vector m (project ast) code/contract)\n177\t    (kernel-load m (project ast))))\n178\t\n179\t\n180\t(defn lane-closure\n181\t  \"Canonical closure payload c, its :segment an A, as machine m's value.\"\n182\t  [m c]\n183\t  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n184\t    (values/closure (:owner m) (update c :segment #(get (:code-aliases m) %)))\n185\t    (layout/positional-value (layout/lower-context m (kernel-space m)) (values/closure (:owner m) c))))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t(defn lift-opts\n189\t  []\n190\t  {:source-index @source-index})\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t(defn error\n194\t  [f]\n195\t  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n196\t\n197\t\n198\t;; =============================================================================\n199\t;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n200\t;; ============================================================================="}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e67cb0-f183-4c2e-b3d6-2e5b6c44b814","uuid":"c12e4938-8698-4084-a0e1-79e3bce77474","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:34:38.370Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def code-index\n  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def ^:dynamic *projected*\n  \"When bound, an atom {A v} of the vectors one world projected: the\n   layouts' spaces read it instead of the whole file's code-index, so an\n   alpha-equivalent A an unrelated fixture projected widens no lookup.\"\n  nil)\n\n\n(defn project\n  [ast]\n  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n        a (jing/segment-key v)]\n    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n    (swap! code-index assoc a v)\n    (when *projected* (swap! *projected* assoc a v))\n    v))\n\n\n(defn scoped\n  \"f's result, every vector it projects recorded in a fresh *projected*.\"\n  [f]\n  (binding [*projected* (atom {})] (f)))\n\n\n(defn file-wide\n  \"f's result, the layouts' spaces reading every vector the file ever\n   projected: only the fixtures that show that contamination.\"\n  [f]\n  (binding [*projected* code-index] (f)))\n\n\n(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n\n\n(def ^:dynamic *lane*\n  \"The kernel a world is built on: :semantic-register (the reference\n   lane), or :stack or :register, which run A's derived image and lift\n   and lower through the layouts (§5.3).\"\n  :semantic-register)\n\n\n(def lanes [:semantic-register :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- composition\n  [opts]\n  (merge {:make-stream tu/make-stream :capability-secret tu/secret\n          :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))\n          :modules stream-modules}\n         opts))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-opts\n  \"A de Bruijn kernel's options for the same composition: the full\n   primitive table, and the initial environment as :free-env.\"\n  [opts]\n  (cond-> (assoc (dissoc (composition opts) :env) :primitives vm/primitives)\n    (contains? opts :env) (assoc :free-env (:env opts))))\n\n\n(defn machine\n  ([] (machine {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (case *lane*\n     :semantic-register (sr/create-vm (composition opts))\n     :stack (dvm/create-vm [] (kernel-opts opts))\n     :register (rvm/create-vm (assoc {} :bodies [] :instructions []) (kernel-opts opts)))))\n\n\n(defn lane-of\n  [m]\n  (let [f (:format (module/link-format m))]\n    (cond (= dvm/format-tag f) :stack\n          (= rvm/format-tag f) :register\n          :else :semantic-register)))\n\n\n(def segment-of\n  \"layout/segment, once per A.\"\n  (memoize layout/segment))\n\n\n(defn kernel-space\n  \"The layout space of the A vectors whose images de Bruijn kernel k\n   holds, among those this world projected (`scoped`), or the file ever\n   projected (`file-wide`). Unbound, it throws: an independent world's\n   lookups never read another fixture's vectors.\"\n  [k]\n  (when-not *projected*\n    (throw (ex-info \"kernel-space outside scoped or file-wide\" {})))\n  (let [id (if (= :stack (lane-of k)) :stack-id :register-id)\n        held (into #{} (map first) (:images k))]\n    (layout/space (filter #(contains? held (id %)) (map segment-of (vals @*projected*))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-load\n  \"Attach v's derived image and start it at its row, beside whatever the\n   kernel already holds: parked records keep naming their own rows.\"\n  [k v]\n  (let [kind (lane-of k)\n        sg (segment-of v)\n        k (if (= :stack kind)\n            (dvm/attach-image k (:stack sg) vm/stack-contract)\n            (rvm/attach-image k (:register sg) vm/register-contract))\n        k (assoc k :pc (layout/offset kind k sg) :frames [] :continuation [] :store-of nil\n                 :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)]\n    (if (= :stack kind)\n      (assoc k :stack [])\n      (assoc k :registers (vec (repeat (:registers (first (:bodies (:register sg)))) nil))))))\n\n\n(defn load-program\n  [m ast]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (sr/load-vector m (project ast) code/contract)\n    (kernel-load m (project ast))))\n\n\n(defn lane-closure\n  \"Canonical closure payload c, its :segment an A, as machine m's value.\"\n  [m c]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (values/closure (:owner m) (update c :segment #(get (:code-aliases m) %)))\n    (layout/positional-value (layout/lower-context m (kernel-space m)) (values/closure (:owner m) c))))\n\n\n(defn lift-opts\n  []\n  {:source-index @source-index})\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n;; =============================================================================","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1931}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0146dKRmaDDF5LTsH4YoSJ9G","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
