 :slow -n <ns>`).\n47:# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n48:# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n49:# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n50:# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n51:# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\n52:# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n53:# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n54:# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n55:# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n56:# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n57:# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n58:# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n59:# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\n...\n11:bb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\n12:bb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\n13:bb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n15:bb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\n16:bb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\n17:bb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\n18:bb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\n19:bb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n20:bb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n21:bb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\n22:bb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n23:bb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those name